      },
      "cml:operator": "includes",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Temporal interval",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) The matters are as follows:",
      "cml:conclusionText": "a specific point in time"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ge-ss-2-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "=",
      "cml:logicSummary": "List of prohibited actions",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a) theft;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "theft is a serious Commonwealth offence"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gg",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15GG ART Minister may nominate ART members",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15gg"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.28",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister administering the Administrative Review Tribunal Act\n2024 (the ART Minister) may, by writing, nominate a person who\nholds one of the following appointments to the Administrative\nReview Tribunal to deal with applications under\nsubsection 15GU(1) (which deals with extending authorities for\ncontrolled operations beyond 3 months):\n\n(a) Deputy President;\n\n(b) a senior member;\n\n(c) a general member.\n\n(2) Despite subsection (1), the ART Minister must not nominate a\nperson who holds an appointment as a senior member appointed on\na sessional basis or a general member of the Tribunal unless the\nperson:\n\n(a) is enrolled as a legal practitioner of the High Court, of\nanother federal court or of the Supreme Court of a State or of\nthe Australian Capital Territory; and\n\n(b) has been so enrolled for not less than 5 years.\n\n(3) A nomination ceases to have effect if:\n\n\nControlled operations  Part IAB\nPreliminary  Division 1\n\nSection 15GG\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) the nominated Tribunal member ceases to hold an\nappointment described in subsection (1); or\n\n(b) the ART Minister, by writing, withdraws the nomination.\n\n(4) A nominated Tribunal member has, in relation to the performance\nor exercise of a function or power conferred on a nominated\nTribunal member by this Act, the same protection and immunity as\na Justice of the High Court has in relation to proceedings in the\nHigh Court.\n\n\nPart IAB  Controlled operations",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister administering the Administrative Review Tribunal Act\n2024 (the ART Minister) may, by writing, nominate a person who\nholds one of the following appointments to the Administrative\nReview Tribunal to deal with applications under\nsubsection 15GU(1) (which deals with extending authorities for\ncontrolled operations beyond 3 months):\n\n(a) Deputy President;\n\n(b) a senior member;\n\n(c) a general member.\n\n(2) Despite subsection (1), the ART Minister must not nominate a\nperson who holds an appointment as a senior member appointed on\na sessional basis or a general member of the Tribunal unless the\nperson:\n\n(a) is enrolled as a legal practitioner of the High Court, of\nanother federal court or of the Supreme Court of a State or of\nthe Australian Capital Territory; and\n\n(b) has been so enrolled for not less than 5 years.\n\n(3) A nomination ceases to have effect if:\n\n\nControlled operations  Part IAB\nPreliminary  Division 1\n\nSection 15GG\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) the nominated Tribunal member ceases to hold an\nappointment described in subsection (1); or\n\n(b) the ART Minister, by writing, withdraws the nomination.\n\n(4) A nominated Tribunal member has, in relation to the performance\nor exercise of a function or power conferred on a nominated\nTribunal member by this Act, the same protection and immunity as\na Justice of the High Court has in relation to proceedings in the\nHigh Court.\n\n\nPart IAB  Controlled operations",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gg-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gg-ss-2"
