    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gg-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15GG(4) ART Minister may nominate ART members",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15gg-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.28",
      "values:originalText": "(4) A nominated Tribunal member has, in relation to the performance\nor exercise of a function or power conferred on a nominated\nTribunal member by this Act, the same protection and immunity as\na Justice of the High Court has in relation to proceedings in the\nHigh Court.\n\n\nPart IAB  Controlled operations",
      "skos:definition": "(4) A nominated Tribunal member has, in relation to the performance\nor exercise of a function or power conferred on a nominated\nTribunal member by this Act, the same protection and immunity as\na Justice of the High Court has in relation to proceedings in the\nHigh Court.\n\n\nPart IAB  Controlled operations",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gg"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gg-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gg-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "34fa639b10574d02efd35fd5d2df23af2bc683cb2e149c94c23dc2dd5f462b7a",
      "skos:note": "Protection and immunity for nominated Tribunal members"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15gg-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15GG(4) ART Minister may nominate ART members",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 28,
      "values:originalText": "(4) A nominated Tribunal member has, in relation to the performance\nor exercise of a function or power conferred on a nominated\nTribunal member by this Act, the same protection and immunity as\na Justice of the High Court has in relation to proceedings in the\nHigh Court.\n\n\nPart IAB  Controlled operations"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gg-ss-4-norm",
