    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gh-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15GH(3) Applications for authorities to conduct controlled operations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15gh-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.30",
      "values:originalText": "(3) Nothing in this Part prevents an application for an authority being\nmade in respect of a controlled operation that has been the subject\nof a previous application, but in that case the subsequent\napplication must be a formal application.\nNote:\nAn urgent authority can be varied, but not so as to extend its\nduration—see sections 15GO and 15GS.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) Nothing in this Part prevents an application for an authority being\nmade in respect of a controlled operation that has been the subject\nof a previous application, but in that case the subsequent\napplication must be a formal application.\nNote:\nAn urgent authority can be varied, but not so as to extend its\nduration—see sections 15GO and 15GS.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gh"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gh-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gh-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1985751e49f4fce997dbfe6a50c59b33d359af9a8e935bd167f7e138318475a6",
      "skos:note": "Subsequent application for authority must be formal."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15gh-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15GH(3) Applications for authorities to conduct controlled operations",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 30,
      "values:originalText": "(3) Nothing in this Part prevents an application for an authority being\nmade in respect of a controlled operation that has been the subject\nof a previous application, but in that case the subsequent\napplication must be a formal application.\nNote:\nAn urgent authority can be varied, but not so as to extend its\nduration—see sections 15GO and 15GS."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gh-ss-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
