    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gh-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15GH(4) Applications for authorities to conduct controlled operations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15gh-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.30",
      "values:originalText": "(4) An application (whether formal or urgent) must:\n\n(a) provide sufficient information to enable the authorising\nofficer to decide whether or not to grant the application; and\n\n(b) state whether or not the proposed controlled operation, or any\nother controlled operation with respect to the same criminal\nactivity, has been the subject of an earlier application\n(whether formal or urgent) for an authority or variation of an\nauthority and, if so, whether or not the authority was given or\nthe variation granted; and\n\n\nControlled operations  Part IAB\nAuthorisation of controlled operations  Division 2\n\nSection 15GI\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(c) state the proposed period of effect of the authority, which\nmust not exceed:\n\n(i) in the case of a formal application—3 months; and\n\n(ii) in the case of an urgent application—7 days.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) An application (whether formal or urgent) must:\n\n(a) provide sufficient information to enable the authorising\nofficer to decide whether or not to grant the application; and\n\n(b) state whether or not the proposed controlled operation, or any\nother controlled operation with respect to the same criminal\nactivity, has been the subject of an earlier application\n(whether formal or urgent) for an authority or variation of an\nauthority and, if so, whether or not the authority was given or\nthe variation granted; and\n\n\nControlled operations  Part IAB\nAuthorisation of controlled operations  Division 2\n\nSection 15GI\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(c) state the proposed period of effect of the authority, which\nmust not exceed:\n\n(i) in the case of a formal application—3 months; and\n\n(ii) in the case of an urgent application—7 days.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gh"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gh-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gh-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7cafbf62f272c9931f684daf8514141465d9b43e243df9f207178829ffb72c90",
      "skos:note": "Application requirements for controlled operations",
      "dc:description": "sufficient information, earlier application details, proposed period of effect"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15gh-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15GH(4) Applications for authorities to conduct controlled operations",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 30,
      "values:originalText": "(4) An application (whether formal or urgent) must:\n\n(a) provide sufficient information to enable the authorising\nofficer to decide whether or not to grant the application; and\n\n(b) state whether or not the proposed controlled operation, or any\nother controlled operation with respect to the same criminal\nactivity, has been the subject of an earlier application\n(whether formal or urgent) for an authority or variation of an\nauthority and, if so, whether or not the authority was given or\nthe variation granted; and\n\n\nControlled operations  Part IAB\nAuthorisation of controlled operations  Division 2\n\nSection 15GI\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(c) state the proposed period of effect of the authority, which\nmust not exceed:\n\n(i) in the case of a formal application—3 months; and\n\n(ii) in the case of an urgent application—7 days."
    },
    {
