    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gj",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15GJ Manner of granting authority",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15gj"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.33",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An authority to conduct a controlled operation may be granted:\n\n(a) in the case of a formal application (other than a formal\napplication referred to in subparagraph (b)(ii))—by means of\na written document, signed by the authorising officer (such\nan authority is a formal authority); or\n\n(b) in the case of:\n\n(i) an urgent application; or\n\n(ii) a formal application, if the authorising officer is\nsatisfied that the delay caused by granting a formal\nauthority may affect the success of the controlled\noperation;\n\n\nPart IAB  Controlled operations",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An authority to conduct a controlled operation may be granted:\n\n(a) in the case of a formal application (other than a formal\napplication referred to in subparagraph (b)(ii))—by means of\na written document, signed by the authorising officer (such\nan authority is a formal authority); or\n\n(b) in the case of:\n\n(i) an urgent application; or\n\n(ii) a formal application, if the authorising officer is\nsatisfied that the delay caused by granting a formal\nauthority may affect the success of the controlled\noperation;\n\n\nPart IAB  Controlled operations",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gj-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gj-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gj-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e1ca7a1986c07deb386ec81ada181976b585e16ccb5bf77569172f10113ed679",
      "skos:note": "Authority to conduct controlled operation may be granted by written document or formal application with authorising officer's satisfaction."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15gj",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15GJ Manner of granting authority",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 33,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An authority to conduct a controlled operation may be granted:\n\n(a) in the case of a formal application (other than a formal\napplication referred to in subparagraph (b)(ii))—by means of\na written document, signed by the authorising officer (such\nan authority is a formal authority); or\n\n(b) in the case of:\n\n(i) an urgent application; or\n\n(ii) a formal application, if the authorising officer is\nsatisfied that the delay caused by granting a formal\nauthority may affect the success of the controlled\noperation;\n\n\nPart IAB  Controlled operations"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gj-norm",
