    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gl",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15GL Written record of urgent authority must be issued",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15gl"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.36",
      "values:originalText": "If an authorising officer grants an urgent authority, the authorising\nofficer must, within 7 days, issue a written record of the urgent\nauthority that complies with subsection 15GK(2) to the principal\nlaw enforcement officer for the controlled operation.\n\n\nControlled operations  Part IAB\nAuthorisation of controlled operations  Division 2\n\nSection 15GM\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "If an authorising officer grants an urgent authority, the authorising\nofficer must, within 7 days, issue a written record of the urgent\nauthority that complies with subsection 15GK(2) to the principal\nlaw enforcement officer for the controlled operation.\n\n\nControlled operations  Part IAB\nAuthorisation of controlled operations  Division 2\n\nSection 15GM\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gl-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gl-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3d43b3e4ee17b38bf0c0640e84588eae09ae87bf1c9b99d1f9710d8f2c9ce9ee",
      "skos:note": "Authorising officer must issue written record of urgent authority within 7 days."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15gl",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15GL Written record of urgent authority must be issued",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 36,
      "values:originalText": "If an authorising officer grants an urgent authority, the authorising\nofficer must, within 7 days, issue a written record of the urgent\nauthority that complies with subsection 15GK(2) to the principal\nlaw enforcement officer for the controlled operation.\n\n\nControlled operations  Part IAB\nAuthorisation of controlled operations  Division 2\n\nSection 15GM\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gl-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gl"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gl-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Authorising officer must issue written record.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gm",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15GM Change of principal law enforcement officer",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15gm"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.37",
      "values:originalText": "If an authorising officer in relation to a controlled operation\nbecomes satisfied that the principal law enforcement officer for the\ncontrolled operation ceases for any reason to have responsibility\nfor the controlled operation:\n\n(a) the authorising officer may, by instrument in writing,\nnominate another person as the principal law enforcement\nofficer for the controlled operation; and\n\n(b) with effect from the execution of the instrument or such later\ntime as is specified in the instrument, that other person\nbecomes the principal law enforcement officer for the\ncontrolled operation.",
      "skos:definition": "If an authorising officer in relation to a controlled operation\nbecomes satisfied that the principal law enforcement officer for the\ncontrolled operation ceases for any reason to have responsibility\nfor the controlled operation:\n\n(a) the authorising officer may, by instrument in writing,\nnominate another person as the principal law enforcement\nofficer for the controlled operation; and\n\n(b) with effect from the execution of the instrument or such later\ntime as is specified in the instrument, that other person\nbecomes the principal law enforcement officer for the\ncontrolled operation.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gm-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "04216488789e68fb33f4865f2866a9072baa8a11645cb086d5428392de9a25c3",
      "skos:note": "Authorising officer may nominate another person as principal law enforcement officer."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15gm",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15GM Change of principal law enforcement officer",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 37,
      "values:originalText": "If an authorising officer in relation to a controlled operation\nbecomes satisfied that the principal law enforcement officer for the\ncontrolled operation ceases for any reason to have responsibility\nfor the controlled operation:\n\n(a) the authorising officer may, by instrument in writing,\nnominate another person as the principal law enforcement\nofficer for the controlled operation; and\n\n(b) with effect from the execution of the instrument or such later\ntime as is specified in the instrument, that other person\nbecomes the principal law enforcement officer for the\ncontrolled operation."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gm-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gm"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gn",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15GN Commencement and duration of authorities",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15gn"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.37",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An authority to conduct a controlled operation comes into force,\nand the controlled operation is taken to commence, at the time the\nauthority is granted under section 15GI.\n\n(2) To avoid doubt, an urgent authority is granted when the authorising\nofficer tells the applicant that the urgent authority is granted.\nNote:\nAn authority is granted under subsection 15GI(1).\nParagraph 15GJ(1)(b) enables an authority to be granted orally in\nspecified circumstances.\n\n(3) An authority (whether formal or urgent) has effect for the period of\neffect specified in it under paragraph 15GK(1)(h) or (2)(h) unless:\n\n(a) it is cancelled before the end of the period of effect; or\n\n(b) in the case of a formal authority—the period of effect is\nextended under Subdivision B or C; or\n\n(c) in the case of an integrity testing controlled operation\nauthority—the integrity testing authority concerned (the\nearlier ITA) stops being in effect under Part IABA (see\nsection 15JJ).\nNote:\nFor integrity testing controlled operation authorities, see\nsubparagraph 15GI(2)(a)(ii).\n\n\nPart IAB  Controlled operations",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An authority to conduct a controlled operation comes into force,\nand the controlled operation is taken to commence, at the time the\nauthority is granted under section 15GI.\n\n(2) To avoid doubt, an urgent authority is granted when the authorising\nofficer tells the applicant that the urgent authority is granted.\nNote:\nAn authority is granted under subsection 15GI(1).\nParagraph 15GJ(1)(b) enables an authority to be granted orally in\nspecified circumstances.\n\n(3) An authority (whether formal or urgent) has effect for the period of\neffect specified in it under paragraph 15GK(1)(h) or (2)(h) unless:\n\n(a) it is cancelled before the end of the period of effect; or\n\n(b) in the case of a formal authority—the period of effect is\nextended under Subdivision B or C; or\n\n(c) in the case of an integrity testing controlled operation\nauthority—the integrity testing authority concerned (the\nearlier ITA) stops being in effect under Part IABA (see\nsection 15JJ).\nNote:\nFor integrity testing controlled operation authorities, see\nsubparagraph 15GI(2)(a)(ii).\n\n\nPart IAB  Controlled operations",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gn-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gn-ss-2"
        },
