          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15go-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5105adafa952c228307da206bcadb58749cd158e3f8d8f6d6a212c2c6b8e6139",
      "skos:note": "No variation of formal authority can exceed 3 months in effect."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15go-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15GO(4) Variation of authority by appropriate authorising officer",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 38,
      "values:originalText": "(4) A formal authority must not be varied in such a way that the period\nof effect of the authority will, after the variation is made, exceed 3\nmonths (including any previous extensions).\n\n\nControlled operations  Part IAB\nAuthorisation of controlled operations  Division 2\n\nSection 15GP\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026"
    },
