    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15go-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15GO(5) Variation of authority by appropriate authorising officer",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15go-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.38",
      "values:originalText": "(5) An authority must not be varied unless the authorising officer is\nsatisfied on reasonable grounds that the variation will not authorise\na significant alteration of the nature of the controlled operation\nconcerned, including an alteration that would change the nature of\nthe criminal offences to which the controlled operation relates.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) An authority must not be varied unless the authorising officer is\nsatisfied on reasonable grounds that the variation will not authorise\na significant alteration of the nature of the controlled operation\nconcerned, including an alteration that would change the nature of\nthe criminal offences to which the controlled operation relates.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15go"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
