    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gs",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15GS Form of variation of authority",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15gs"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.44",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A variation of an authority by an appropriate authorising officer\n(whether formal or urgent) must:\n\n(a) identify the controlled operation to which the authority\nrelates; and\n\n(b) state the name and rank or position of the person varying the\nauthority; and\n\n(c) if the authority was varied on an application made under\nsection 15GP, state:\n\n(i) the name of the applicant; and\n\n(ii) whether the application was a formal variation\napplication or an urgent variation application; and\n\n(d) state the date and time when the variation of authority is or\nwas granted; and\n\n(e) describe the variation having regard to the matters referred to\nin subsection 15GO(2); and\n\n(f) if the variation extends the period of effect of a formal\nauthority—state the period of the extension.\n\n(2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(f), the period of the extension\nmust not exceed:\n\n(a) in the case of a formal variation of authority—the period that\nwould result in the period of effect of the authority exceeding\n3 months (including any previous extensions); and\n\n(b) in the case of an urgent variation of authority—the lesser of:\n\n(i) 7 days; and\n\n(ii) a period that would result in the period of effect of the\nauthority exceeding 3 months (including any previous\nextensions).\n\n\nControlled operations  Part IAB\nAuthorisation of controlled operations  Division 2\n\nSection 15GT\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nSubdivision C—Variations of authorities by nominated\nTribunal member: extensions beyond 3 months",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A variation of an authority by an appropriate authorising officer\n(whether formal or urgent) must:\n\n(a) identify the controlled operation to which the authority\nrelates; and\n\n(b) state the name and rank or position of the person varying the\nauthority; and\n\n(c) if the authority was varied on an application made under\nsection 15GP, state:\n\n(i) the name of the applicant; and\n\n(ii) whether the application was a formal variation\napplication or an urgent variation application; and\n\n(d) state the date and time when the variation of authority is or\nwas granted; and\n\n(e) describe the variation having regard to the matters referred to\nin subsection 15GO(2); and\n\n(f) if the variation extends the period of effect of a formal\nauthority—state the period of the extension.\n\n(2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(f), the period of the extension\nmust not exceed:\n\n(a) in the case of a formal variation of authority—the period that\nwould result in the period of effect of the authority exceeding\n3 months (including any previous extensions); and\n\n(b) in the case of an urgent variation of authority—the lesser of:\n\n(i) 7 days; and\n\n(ii) a period that would result in the period of effect of the\nauthority exceeding 3 months (including any previous\nextensions).\n\n\nControlled operations  Part IAB\nAuthorisation of controlled operations  Division 2\n\nSection 15GT\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nSubdivision C—Variations of authorities by nominated\nTribunal member: extensions beyond 3 months",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gs-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gs-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3e7059a133d10d09659a9153fe66eae4335b1d9b7e270fc384bc8b0b26926d7f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15gs",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15GS Form of variation of authority",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 44,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A variation of an authority by an appropriate authorising officer\n(whether formal or urgent) must:\n\n(a) identify the controlled operation to which the authority\nrelates; and\n\n(b) state the name and rank or position of the person varying the\nauthority; and\n\n(c) if the authority was varied on an application made under\nsection 15GP, state:\n\n(i) the name of the applicant; and\n\n(ii) whether the application was a formal variation\napplication or an urgent variation application; and\n\n(d) state the date and time when the variation of authority is or\nwas granted; and\n\n(e) describe the variation having regard to the matters referred to\nin subsection 15GO(2); and\n\n(f) if the variation extends the period of effect of a formal\nauthority—state the period of the extension.\n\n(2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(f), the period of the extension\nmust not exceed:\n\n(a) in the case of a formal variation of authority—the period that\nwould result in the period of effect of the authority exceeding\n3 months (including any previous extensions); and\n\n(b) in the case of an urgent variation of authority—the lesser of:\n\n(i) 7 days; and\n\n(ii) a period that would result in the period of effect of the\nauthority exceeding 3 months (including any previous\nextensions).\n\n\nControlled operations  Part IAB\nAuthorisation of controlled operations  Division 2\n\nSection 15GT\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nSubdivision C—Variations of authorities by nominated\nTribunal member: extensions beyond 3 months"
    },
