    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gu",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15GU Application to nominated Tribunal member",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15gu"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.45",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The principal law enforcement officer for a controlled operation\nfor which there is a formal authority, or any other Australian law\nenforcement officer acting on behalf of the principal law\nenforcement officer, may apply to a nominated Tribunal member\nfor a variation of the authority that would extend its period of\neffect:\n\n(a) if the period of effect of the authority is 3 months or more\n(including any previous extensions); or\n\n(b) in such a way that the period of effect of the authority will,\nafter the variation is made, be 3 months or more (including\nany previous extensions).\n\n\nPart IAB  Controlled operations",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The principal law enforcement officer for a controlled operation\nfor which there is a formal authority, or any other Australian law\nenforcement officer acting on behalf of the principal law\nenforcement officer, may apply to a nominated Tribunal member\nfor a variation of the authority that would extend its period of\neffect:\n\n(a) if the period of effect of the authority is 3 months or more\n(including any previous extensions); or\n\n(b) in such a way that the period of effect of the authority will,\nafter the variation is made, be 3 months or more (including\nany previous extensions).\n\n\nPart IAB  Controlled operations",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gu-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gu-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c024a6436ad1581a035ea95629309ad1268e6aeacb28875569c9152dab9befcb",
      "skos:note": "Application for variation of authority period"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15gu",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15GU Application to nominated Tribunal member",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 45,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The principal law enforcement officer for a controlled operation\nfor which there is a formal authority, or any other Australian law\nenforcement officer acting on behalf of the principal law\nenforcement officer, may apply to a nominated Tribunal member\nfor a variation of the authority that would extend its period of\neffect:\n\n(a) if the period of effect of the authority is 3 months or more\n(including any previous extensions); or\n\n(b) in such a way that the period of effect of the authority will,\nafter the variation is made, be 3 months or more (including\nany previous extensions).\n\n\nPart IAB  Controlled operations"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gu-norm",
      "@type": "values:Permission",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gu"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gu-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Permit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Granting permission to apply for authority variation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gv",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15GV Determination of application",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15gv"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.47",
      "values:originalText": "(1) After considering an application for a variation of a formal\nauthority, and any additional information provided under\nsubsection 15GU(6), the nominated Tribunal member concerned:\n\n(a) may vary the authority in accordance with the application,\neither unconditionally or subject to conditions; or\n\n(b) may refuse the application.\n\n(2) The nominated Tribunal member must not grant the variation\nunless the nominated Tribunal member is satisfied on reasonable\ngrounds:\n\n(a) that either:\n\n(i) a serious Commonwealth offence or a serious State\noffence that has a federal aspect has been, is being or is\nlikely to be committed; or\n\n(ii) an integrity testing authority is in effect in relation to an\noffence that it is suspected has been, is being or is likely\nto be committed by a staff member of a target agency\n(see the notes at the foot of this subsection); and\n\n(b) that the nature and extent of the suspected criminal activity\nare such as to justify the variation; and\n\n(c) that any unlawful conduct involved in conducting the\ncontrolled operation will be limited to the maximum extent\nconsistent with conducting an effective controlled operation;\nand\n\n\nPart IAB  Controlled operations",
      "skos:definition": "(1) After considering an application for a variation of a formal\nauthority, and any additional information provided under\nsubsection 15GU(6), the nominated Tribunal member concerned:\n\n(a) may vary the authority in accordance with the application,\neither unconditionally or subject to conditions; or\n\n(b) may refuse the application.\n\n(2) The nominated Tribunal member must not grant the variation\nunless the nominated Tribunal member is satisfied on reasonable\ngrounds:\n\n(a) that either:\n\n(i) a serious Commonwealth offence or a serious State\noffence that has a federal aspect has been, is being or is\nlikely to be committed; or\n\n(ii) an integrity testing authority is in effect in relation to an\noffence that it is suspected has been, is being or is likely\nto be committed by a staff member of a target agency\n(see the notes at the foot of this subsection); and\n\n(b) that the nature and extent of the suspected criminal activity\nare such as to justify the variation; and\n\n(c) that any unlawful conduct involved in conducting the\ncontrolled operation will be limited to the maximum extent\nconsistent with conducting an effective controlled operation;\nand\n\n\nPart IAB  Controlled operations",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gv-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gv-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bc72585421eeab436cffb2202c846e14ebaca99de6e0925b9ae61eb6654e81f8"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15gv",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15GV Determination of application",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 47,
      "values:originalText": "(1) After considering an application for a variation of a formal\nauthority, and any additional information provided under\nsubsection 15GU(6), the nominated Tribunal member concerned:\n\n(a) may vary the authority in accordance with the application,\neither unconditionally or subject to conditions; or\n\n(b) may refuse the application.\n\n(2) The nominated Tribunal member must not grant the variation\nunless the nominated Tribunal member is satisfied on reasonable\ngrounds:\n\n(a) that either:\n\n(i) a serious Commonwealth offence or a serious State\noffence that has a federal aspect has been, is being or is\nlikely to be committed; or\n\n(ii) an integrity testing authority is in effect in relation to an\noffence that it is suspected has been, is being or is likely\nto be committed by a staff member of a target agency\n(see the notes at the foot of this subsection); and\n\n(b) that the nature and extent of the suspected criminal activity\nare such as to justify the variation; and\n\n(c) that any unlawful conduct involved in conducting the\ncontrolled operation will be limited to the maximum extent\nconsistent with conducting an effective controlled operation;\nand\n\n\nPart IAB  Controlled operations"
    },
