      "dc:description": "a, b, c, d, e, f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15gx-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15GX(1) Form of variation of formal authority",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 50,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A variation of a formal authority by a nominated Tribunal member\n(whether formal or urgent) must:\n\n(a) identify the controlled operation to which the authority\nrelates; and\n\n(b) state the name and position of the person varying the\nauthority; and\n\n(c) state the name of the applicant; and\n\n(d) state whether the application for the variation was a formal\nvariation application or an urgent variation application; and\n\n(e) state the date and time when the variation of authority is or\nwas granted; and\n\n(f) state the period of the extension."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gx-ss-1-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gx-ss-1"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gx-ss-1-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "must",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Must provide required information",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gx-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15GX(2) Form of variation of formal authority",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15gx-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.50",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The period of the extension:\n\n(a) must not exceed the period that would result in the period of\neffect of the authority exceeding 24 months (including any\nprevious extensions under this Subdivision or Subdivision\nB); and\n\n(b) must not exceed:\n\n(i) in the case of a formal variation of authority—3 months;\nand\n\n(ii) in the case of an urgent variation of authority—7 days.\nSubdivision D—Other matters",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The period of the extension:\n\n(a) must not exceed the period that would result in the period of\neffect of the authority exceeding 24 months (including any\nprevious extensions under this Subdivision or Subdivision\nB); and\n\n(b) must not exceed:\n\n(i) in the case of a formal variation of authority—3 months;\nand\n\n(ii) in the case of an urgent variation of authority—7 days.\nSubdivision D—Other matters",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gx"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
