          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gx-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gx-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1c29d7cc021ae375eaa95b78a99cb06edb693520b467f603d41d4848cfc6074e",
      "skos:note": "Maximum period for extension of authority"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15gx-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15GX(2) Form of variation of formal authority",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 50,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The period of the extension:\n\n(a) must not exceed the period that would result in the period of\neffect of the authority exceeding 24 months (including any\nprevious extensions under this Subdivision or Subdivision\nB); and\n\n(b) must not exceed:\n\n(i) in the case of a formal variation of authority—3 months;\nand\n\n(ii) in the case of an urgent variation of authority—7 days.\nSubdivision D—Other matters"
    },
