    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gy",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15GY Cancellation of authorities",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15gy"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.50",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An appropriate authorising officer may, by order in writing given\nto the principal law enforcement officer for a controlled operation,\ncancel the authority to conduct the controlled operation at any time\nand for any reason.\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), an appropriate authorising officer\nmay cancel an authority at any time at the request of the principal\nlaw enforcement officer for the controlled operation concerned.\n\n\nControlled operations  Part IAB\nAuthorisation of controlled operations  Division 2\n\nSection 15GZ\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(3) Cancellation of an authority takes effect at the time the order is\nmade or at the later time specified in the order.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An appropriate authorising officer may, by order in writing given\nto the principal law enforcement officer for a controlled operation,\ncancel the authority to conduct the controlled operation at any time\nand for any reason.\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), an appropriate authorising officer\nmay cancel an authority at any time at the request of the principal\nlaw enforcement officer for the controlled operation concerned.\n\n\nControlled operations  Part IAB\nAuthorisation of controlled operations  Division 2\n\nSection 15GZ\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(3) Cancellation of an authority takes effect at the time the order is\nmade or at the later time specified in the order.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gy-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gy-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15gy-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d9f5f9cd1c0444c52dc7969b67acbb2ea3cad88198b54a1f9ff6885d84ad5c35"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15gy",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15GY Cancellation of authorities",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 50,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An appropriate authorising officer may, by order in writing given\nto the principal law enforcement officer for a controlled operation,\ncancel the authority to conduct the controlled operation at any time\nand for any reason.\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), an appropriate authorising officer\nmay cancel an authority at any time at the request of the principal\nlaw enforcement officer for the controlled operation concerned.\n\n\nControlled operations  Part IAB\nAuthorisation of controlled operations  Division 2\n\nSection 15GZ\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(3) Cancellation of an authority takes effect at the time the order is\nmade or at the later time specified in the order."
    },
