      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bdcf04212c0206faa5e7929e3702540c289cfe96a3c699cc2866d7e280d79a72",
      "skos:note": "Participant must not deal with material depicting a sexual offence against any person."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15ha-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15HA(3) Protection from criminal responsibility for controlled conduct",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 52,
      "values:originalText": "(3) To avoid doubt, nothing in subparagraph (2)(d)(ii) is intended to\nprevent the participant being protected from criminal responsibility\nif the conduct involves the participant:\n\n(a) dealing with material depicting, material describing or\nmaterial otherwise involving a sexual offence against any\nperson; or\n\n(b) facilitating a person to deal with such material."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ha-ss-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ha-ss-3"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ha-ss-3-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibition",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits dealing with material depicting a sexual offence against any person.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(3) To avoid doubt, nothing in subparagraph (2)(d)(ii)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ha-ss-3-logic-linearlogic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LinearLogic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Conjunction",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits dealing with material depicting a sexual offence against any person and facilitating a person to deal with such material.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::linear",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(3) To avoid doubt, nothing in subparagraph (2)(d)(ii)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ha-ss-3-logic-alleninterval-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "TemporalInclusion",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Dealing with material depicting a sexual offence against any person must occur before the participant is protected from criminal responsibility.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(3) To avoid doubt, nothing in subparagraph (2)(d)(ii)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15hb",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15HB Indemnification of participants against civil liability",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15hb"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.53",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commonwealth must indemnify a participant in a controlled\noperation against any civil liability (including reasonable costs) the\nparticipant incurs because of conduct the participant engages in if:\n\n(a) the participant engages in the conduct in the course of, and\nfor the purposes of, the controlled operation in accordance\nwith the authority to conduct the controlled operation; and\n\n(b) the participant is identified in the authority as a person\nauthorised to engage in controlled conduct for the purposes\nof the controlled operation; and\n\n(c) the conduct does not involve the participant intentionally\ninducing a person to commit a Commonwealth offence or an\noffence under a law of a State or Territory that the person\nwould not otherwise have intended to commit; and\n\n(d) the conduct does not involve the participant engaging in any\nconduct that is likely to:\n\n(i) cause the death of, or serious injury to, any person; or\n\n(ii) involve the commission of a sexual offence against any\nperson; and\n\n(e) if the participant is a civilian participant in the operation—he\nor she acts in accordance with the instructions of a law\nenforcement officer; and\n\n(f) the requirements (if any) specified in the regulations have\nbeen met.\n\n(2) To avoid doubt, nothing in subparagraph (1)(d)(ii) is intended to\nprevent the participant being indemnified against civil liability if\nthe conduct involves the participant:\n\n\nPart IAB  Controlled operations",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Commonwealth must indemnify a participant in a controlled\noperation against any civil liability (including reasonable costs) the\nparticipant incurs because of conduct the participant engages in if:\n\n(a) the participant engages in the conduct in the course of, and\nfor the purposes of, the controlled operation in accordance\nwith the authority to conduct the controlled operation; and\n\n(b) the participant is identified in the authority as a person\nauthorised to engage in controlled conduct for the purposes\nof the controlled operation; and\n\n(c) the conduct does not involve the participant intentionally\ninducing a person to commit a Commonwealth offence or an\noffence under a law of a State or Territory that the person\nwould not otherwise have intended to commit; and\n\n(d) the conduct does not involve the participant engaging in any\nconduct that is likely to:\n\n(i) cause the death of, or serious injury to, any person; or\n\n(ii) involve the commission of a sexual offence against any\nperson; and\n\n(e) if the participant is a civilian participant in the operation—he\nor she acts in accordance with the instructions of a law\nenforcement officer; and\n\n(f) the requirements (if any) specified in the regulations have\nbeen met.\n\n(2) To avoid doubt, nothing in subparagraph (1)(d)(ii) is intended to\nprevent the participant being indemnified against civil liability if\nthe conduct involves the participant:\n\n\nPart IAB  Controlled operations",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15hb-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15hb-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7b02ef393f3568ab7481933e27850426fea27b72257d7f13b62f0dd8d2652ada"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15hb",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15HB Indemnification of participants against civil liability",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 53,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Commonwealth must indemnify a participant in a controlled\noperation against any civil liability (including reasonable costs) the\nparticipant incurs because of conduct the participant engages in if:\n\n(a) the participant engages in the conduct in the course of, and\nfor the purposes of, the controlled operation in accordance\nwith the authority to conduct the controlled operation; and\n\n(b) the participant is identified in the authority as a person\nauthorised to engage in controlled conduct for the purposes\nof the controlled operation; and\n\n(c) the conduct does not involve the participant intentionally\ninducing a person to commit a Commonwealth offence or an\noffence under a law of a State or Territory that the person\nwould not otherwise have intended to commit; and\n\n(d) the conduct does not involve the participant engaging in any\nconduct that is likely to:\n\n(i) cause the death of, or serious injury to, any person; or\n\n(ii) involve the commission of a sexual offence against any\nperson; and\n\n(e) if the participant is a civilian participant in the operation—he\nor she acts in accordance with the instructions of a law\nenforcement officer; and\n\n(f) the requirements (if any) specified in the regulations have\nbeen met.\n\n(2) To avoid doubt, nothing in subparagraph (1)(d)(ii) is intended to\nprevent the participant being indemnified against civil liability if\nthe conduct involves the participant:\n\n\nPart IAB  Controlled operations"
    },
