    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15hc",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15HC Effect of sections 15HA and 15HB on other laws relating to",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15hc"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.54",
      "values:originalText": "criminal investigation\n\nSections 15HA and 15HB do not apply to a person’s conduct that\nis, or could have been, authorised under Commonwealth law or a\nlaw of a State or Territory relating to the following:\n\n(a) arrest or detention of individuals;\n\n(b) searches of individuals;\n\n(c) entry onto, or searches or inspection of, premises;\n\n(d) searches, inspections or seizures of other property;\n\n(e) forensic procedure;\n\n(f) electronic surveillance devices or telecommunications\ninterception;\n\n(g) identification procedures;\n\n(h) the acquisition or use of assumed identities;\n\n(i) any other matter concerning powers of criminal investigation.",
      "skos:definition": "criminal investigation\n\nSections 15HA and 15HB do not apply to a person’s conduct that\nis, or could have been, authorised under Commonwealth law or a\nlaw of a State or Territory relating to the following:\n\n(a) arrest or detention of individuals;\n\n(b) searches of individuals;\n\n(c) entry onto, or searches or inspection of, premises;\n\n(d) searches, inspections or seizures of other property;\n\n(e) forensic procedure;\n\n(f) electronic surveillance devices or telecommunications\ninterception;\n\n(g) identification procedures;\n\n(h) the acquisition or use of assumed identities;\n\n(i) any other matter concerning powers of criminal investigation.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15hc-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15hc-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "91b06fbdc38a007b0cbcd6f620d7aabd792ca6de53050de057d4f6f35df7e055",
      "skos:note": "Exemptions from sections 15HA and 15HB"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15hc",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15HC Effect of sections 15HA and 15HB on other laws relating to",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 54,
      "values:originalText": "criminal investigation\n\nSections 15HA and 15HB do not apply to a person’s conduct that\nis, or could have been, authorised under Commonwealth law or a\nlaw of a State or Territory relating to the following:\n\n(a) arrest or detention of individuals;\n\n(b) searches of individuals;\n\n(c) entry onto, or searches or inspection of, premises;\n\n(d) searches, inspections or seizures of other property;\n\n(e) forensic procedure;\n\n(f) electronic surveillance devices or telecommunications\ninterception;\n\n(g) identification procedures;\n\n(h) the acquisition or use of assumed identities;\n\n(i) any other matter concerning powers of criminal investigation."
    },
    {
