    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15hd-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15HD(1) Effect of being unaware of variation or cancellation of",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 54,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If an authority to conduct a controlled operation is varied in a way\nthat limits its scope, this Part continues to apply to a participant in\nthe controlled operation as if the authority had not been varied in\nthat way, for so long as the participant:\n\n(a) is unaware of the variation; and\n\n(b) is not reckless about the existence of the variation."
    },
