    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15he",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15HE Protection from criminal responsibility for certain ancillary",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15he"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.55",
      "values:originalText": "conduct\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a person engages in conduct (the ancillary conduct) that\nrelates to controlled conduct (the related controlled conduct)\nengaged in by another person; and\n\n(b) engaging in the ancillary conduct is an ancillary offence in\nrelation to the offence constituted by the related controlled\nconduct.\n\n(2) Despite any other law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory,\nthe person who engaged in the ancillary conduct is not criminally\nresponsible for the ancillary offence if, at the time the person\nengaged in the ancillary conduct, he or she believed the related\ncontrolled conduct was being engaged in, or would be engaged in,\nby a participant in a controlled operation authorised under this Part.\n\n\nPart IAB  Controlled operations",
      "skos:definition": "conduct\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a person engages in conduct (the ancillary conduct) that\nrelates to controlled conduct (the related controlled conduct)\nengaged in by another person; and\n\n(b) engaging in the ancillary conduct is an ancillary offence in\nrelation to the offence constituted by the related controlled\nconduct.\n\n(2) Despite any other law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory,\nthe person who engaged in the ancillary conduct is not criminally\nresponsible for the ancillary offence if, at the time the person\nengaged in the ancillary conduct, he or she believed the related\ncontrolled conduct was being engaged in, or would be engaged in,\nby a participant in a controlled operation authorised under this Part.\n\n\nPart IAB  Controlled operations",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15he-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15he-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "85ca6d6d291c070dbcb28efa667bbed81c9c789b5bb515725a7bad753f6171ba"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15he",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15HE Protection from criminal responsibility for certain ancillary",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 55,
      "values:originalText": "conduct\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a person engages in conduct (the ancillary conduct) that\nrelates to controlled conduct (the related controlled conduct)\nengaged in by another person; and\n\n(b) engaging in the ancillary conduct is an ancillary offence in\nrelation to the offence constituted by the related controlled\nconduct.\n\n(2) Despite any other law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory,\nthe person who engaged in the ancillary conduct is not criminally\nresponsible for the ancillary offence if, at the time the person\nengaged in the ancillary conduct, he or she believed the related\ncontrolled conduct was being engaged in, or would be engaged in,\nby a participant in a controlled operation authorised under this Part.\n\n\nPart IAB  Controlled operations"
    },
