    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15hg-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15HG(4) Notification requirements",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15hg-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.56",
      "values:originalText": "(4) The chief officer is not required to give a notification under\nsubsection (2) or (3) until the chief officer is satisfied that the\nnotification would not:\n\n(a) compromise or hinder the controlled operation or any related\ninvestigation; or\n\n(b) compromise the identity of a participant in the controlled\noperation; or\n\n(c) endanger the life or safety of any person; or\n\n(d) prejudice any legal proceeding; or\n\n(e) otherwise be contrary to the public interest.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) The chief officer is not required to give a notification under\nsubsection (2) or (3) until the chief officer is satisfied that the\nnotification would not:\n\n(a) compromise or hinder the controlled operation or any related\ninvestigation; or\n\n(b) compromise the identity of a participant in the controlled\noperation; or\n\n(c) endanger the life or safety of any person; or\n\n(d) prejudice any legal proceeding; or\n\n(e) otherwise be contrary to the public interest.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15hg"
      },
