    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15hg-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15HG(5) Notification requirements",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15hg-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.56",
      "values:originalText": "(5) A chief officer may, by written instrument, delegate any of the\nchief officer’s powers or functions under this section to:\n\n(a) in relation to the Australian Federal Police—a Deputy\nCommissioner or a person of equivalent or higher rank; or\n\n(b) in relation to the Immigration and Border Protection\nDepartment—a person who holds or performs the duties of\nan SES Band 3 position, or an equivalent or higher position,\nin that Department; or\n\n(c) in relation to the ACC:\n\n(i) an Executive Director or a person occupying an\nequivalent or higher position; or\n\n(ii) a person occupying a position prescribed by the\nregulations; or\n\n\nPart IAB  Controlled operations",
      "skos:definition": "(5) A chief officer may, by written instrument, delegate any of the\nchief officer’s powers or functions under this section to:\n\n(a) in relation to the Australian Federal Police—a Deputy\nCommissioner or a person of equivalent or higher rank; or\n\n(b) in relation to the Immigration and Border Protection\nDepartment—a person who holds or performs the duties of\nan SES Band 3 position, or an equivalent or higher position,\nin that Department; or\n\n(c) in relation to the ACC:\n\n(i) an Executive Director or a person occupying an\nequivalent or higher position; or\n\n(ii) a person occupying a position prescribed by the\nregulations; or\n\n\nPart IAB  Controlled operations",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15hg"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15hg-ss-5-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9d7f3d1715acaa3736a2a24170369d42d41f50f5482734e9e3e62379e7f061b6",
      "skos:note": "Delegation of powers or functions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15hg-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15HG(5) Notification requirements",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 56,
      "values:originalText": "(5) A chief officer may, by written instrument, delegate any of the\nchief officer’s powers or functions under this section to:\n\n(a) in relation to the Australian Federal Police—a Deputy\nCommissioner or a person of equivalent or higher rank; or\n\n(b) in relation to the Immigration and Border Protection\nDepartment—a person who holds or performs the duties of\nan SES Band 3 position, or an equivalent or higher position,\nin that Department; or\n\n(c) in relation to the ACC:\n\n(i) an Executive Director or a person occupying an\nequivalent or higher position; or\n\n(ii) a person occupying a position prescribed by the\nregulations; or\n\n\nPart IAB  Controlled operations"
    },
