      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(1) This section applies...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...engaging in that conduct is a Commonwealth offence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15hh-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15HH(2) Protection from criminal responsibility for conduct under a",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15hh-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.58",
      "values:originalText": "(2) Despite any other law of the Commonwealth, the participant is not\ncriminally responsible for the Commonwealth offence, if:\n\n(a) the conduct is authorised by, and is engaged in in accordance\nwith, the authority to conduct the controlled operation; and\n\n(b) the conduct does not involve the participant intentionally\ninducing a person to commit a Commonwealth offence or an\noffence against a law of a State or Territory that the person\nwould not otherwise have intended to commit; and\n\n(c) the conduct does not involve the participant engaging in any\nconduct that is likely to:\n\n(i) cause the death of, or serious injury to, any person; or\n\n(ii) involve the commission of a sexual offence against any\nperson; and\n\n(d) if the person is a civilian participant in the operation—he or\nshe acts in accordance with the instructions of a law\nenforcement officer.\n\n\nControlled operations  Part IAB\nProtection from criminal responsibility and related provisions  Division 3\n\nSection 15HI\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(2) Despite any other law of the Commonwealth, the participant is not\ncriminally responsible for the Commonwealth offence, if:\n\n(a) the conduct is authorised by, and is engaged in in accordance\nwith, the authority to conduct the controlled operation; and\n\n(b) the conduct does not involve the participant intentionally\ninducing a person to commit a Commonwealth offence or an\noffence against a law of a State or Territory that the person\nwould not otherwise have intended to commit; and\n\n(c) the conduct does not involve the participant engaging in any\nconduct that is likely to:\n\n(i) cause the death of, or serious injury to, any person; or\n\n(ii) involve the commission of a sexual offence against any\nperson; and\n\n(d) if the person is a civilian participant in the operation—he or\nshe acts in accordance with the instructions of a law\nenforcement officer.\n\n\nControlled operations  Part IAB\nProtection from criminal responsibility and related provisions  Division 3\n\nSection 15HI\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15hh"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15hh-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15hh-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cd600d5779c09d798bcb54ecb08256b5a04462deedb13803db81f616551ab7a5",
      "skos:note": "Participant must act in accordance with instructions of a law enforcement officer."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15hh-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15HH(2) Protection from criminal responsibility for conduct under a",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 58,
      "values:originalText": "(2) Despite any other law of the Commonwealth, the participant is not\ncriminally responsible for the Commonwealth offence, if:\n\n(a) the conduct is authorised by, and is engaged in in accordance\nwith, the authority to conduct the controlled operation; and\n\n(b) the conduct does not involve the participant intentionally\ninducing a person to commit a Commonwealth offence or an\noffence against a law of a State or Territory that the person\nwould not otherwise have intended to commit; and\n\n(c) the conduct does not involve the participant engaging in any\nconduct that is likely to:\n\n(i) cause the death of, or serious injury to, any person; or\n\n(ii) involve the commission of a sexual offence against any\nperson; and\n\n(d) if the person is a civilian participant in the operation—he or\nshe acts in accordance with the instructions of a law\nenforcement officer.\n\n\nControlled operations  Part IAB\nProtection from criminal responsibility and related provisions  Division 3\n\nSection 15HI\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026"
    },
