    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15hi",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15HI Effect of section 15HH on other laws relating to criminal",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15hi"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.59",
      "values:originalText": "investigation\n\nSection 15HH does not apply to a person’s conduct that is, or could\nhave been, authorised under a Commonwealth law or a law of a\nState or Territory relating to the following:\n\n(a) arrest or detention of individuals;\n\n(b) searches of individuals;\n\n(c) entry onto, or searches or inspection of, premises;\n\n(d) searches, inspections or seizures of other property;\n\n(e) forensic procedure;\n\n(f) electronic surveillance devices or telecommunications\ninterception;\n\n(g) identification procedures;\n\n(h) the acquisition or use of assumed identities;\n\n(i) any other matter concerning powers of criminal investigation.",
      "skos:definition": "investigation\n\nSection 15HH does not apply to a person’s conduct that is, or could\nhave been, authorised under a Commonwealth law or a law of a\nState or Territory relating to the following:\n\n(a) arrest or detention of individuals;\n\n(b) searches of individuals;\n\n(c) entry onto, or searches or inspection of, premises;\n\n(d) searches, inspections or seizures of other property;\n\n(e) forensic procedure;\n\n(f) electronic surveillance devices or telecommunications\ninterception;\n\n(g) identification procedures;\n\n(h) the acquisition or use of assumed identities;\n\n(i) any other matter concerning powers of criminal investigation.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15hi-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15hi-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e5c464b72f9badbb3ff717504e9d39c1de377098da0857c73e6ee8f8b5165688",
      "skos:note": "Section 15HH does not apply to certain criminal investigation activities."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15hi",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15HI Effect of section 15HH on other laws relating to criminal",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 59,
      "values:originalText": "investigation\n\nSection 15HH does not apply to a person’s conduct that is, or could\nhave been, authorised under a Commonwealth law or a law of a\nState or Territory relating to the following:\n\n(a) arrest or detention of individuals;\n\n(b) searches of individuals;\n\n(c) entry onto, or searches or inspection of, premises;\n\n(d) searches, inspections or seizures of other property;\n\n(e) forensic procedure;\n\n(f) electronic surveillance devices or telecommunications\ninterception;\n\n(g) identification procedures;\n\n(h) the acquisition or use of assumed identities;\n\n(i) any other matter concerning powers of criminal investigation."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15hi-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15hi"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15hi-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "excludes",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Excluded activities",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Section 15HH",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Certain criminal investigation activities"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15hj",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15HJ Protection from criminal responsibility for certain ancillary",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15hj"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.59",
      "values:originalText": "conduct\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a person engages in conduct (the ancillary conduct) that\nrelates to conduct (the related conduct) that:\n\n(i) was engaged in by another person; and\n\n(ii) constitutes an offence for which a person would, but for\nsection 15HH, be criminally responsible; and\n\n(b) engaging in the ancillary conduct is an ancillary offence\n(within the meaning of the Criminal Code) in relation to the\noffence constituted by the related conduct.\n\n(2) Despite any law of the Commonwealth, the person who engaged in\nthe ancillary conduct is not criminally responsible for the ancillary\n\n\nPart IAB  Controlled operations",
      "skos:definition": "conduct\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a person engages in conduct (the ancillary conduct) that\nrelates to conduct (the related conduct) that:\n\n(i) was engaged in by another person; and\n\n(ii) constitutes an offence for which a person would, but for\nsection 15HH, be criminally responsible; and\n\n(b) engaging in the ancillary conduct is an ancillary offence\n(within the meaning of the Criminal Code) in relation to the\noffence constituted by the related conduct.\n\n(2) Despite any law of the Commonwealth, the person who engaged in\nthe ancillary conduct is not criminally responsible for the ancillary\n\n\nPart IAB  Controlled operations",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15hj-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15hj-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "85ca6d6d291c070dbcb28efa667bbed81c9c789b5bb515725a7bad753f6171ba"
    },
