    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15hk",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15HK Unauthorised disclosure of information",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15hk"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.61",
      "values:originalText": "Disclosures by entrusted persons\n\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person is, or has been, an entrusted person; and\n\n(b) information came to the knowledge or into the possession of\nthe person in the person’s capacity as an entrusted person;\nand\n\n(c) the person discloses the information; and\n\n(d) the information relates to a controlled operation.\nNote:\nRecklessness is the fault element for paragraphs (1)(b) and (d)—see\nsection 5.6 of the Criminal Code.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.\n\n(1A) Strict liability applies to paragraph (1)(a).\nNote:\nFor strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code.\n\n(1B) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person is, or has been, an entrusted person; and\n\n(b) information came to the knowledge or into the possession of\nthe person in the person’s capacity as an entrusted person;\nand\n\n(c) the person discloses the information; and\n\n(d) the information relates to a controlled operation; and\n\n(e) either or both of the following subparagraphs apply:\n\n(i) the person intends to endanger the health or safety of\nany person or prejudice the effective conduct of a\ncontrolled operation;\n\n(ii) the disclosure will endanger the health or safety of any\nperson or prejudice the effective conduct of a controlled\noperation.\n\n\nPart IAB  Controlled operations",
      "skos:definition": "Disclosures by entrusted persons\n\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person is, or has been, an entrusted person; and\n\n(b) information came to the knowledge or into the possession of\nthe person in the person’s capacity as an entrusted person;\nand\n\n(c) the person discloses the information; and\n\n(d) the information relates to a controlled operation.\nNote:\nRecklessness is the fault element for paragraphs (1)(b) and (d)—see\nsection 5.6 of the Criminal Code.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.\n\n(1A) Strict liability applies to paragraph (1)(a).\nNote:\nFor strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code.\n\n(1B) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person is, or has been, an entrusted person; and\n\n(b) information came to the knowledge or into the possession of\nthe person in the person’s capacity as an entrusted person;\nand\n\n(c) the person discloses the information; and\n\n(d) the information relates to a controlled operation; and\n\n(e) either or both of the following subparagraphs apply:\n\n(i) the person intends to endanger the health or safety of\nany person or prejudice the effective conduct of a\ncontrolled operation;\n\n(ii) the disclosure will endanger the health or safety of any\nperson or prejudice the effective conduct of a controlled\noperation.\n\n\nPart IAB  Controlled operations",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15hk-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15hk-ss-1a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15hk-ss-1b"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "97befda1bcfb8474623d897240fe4615e517820c10b13e3ff458f6375fcf50d6"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15hk",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15HK Unauthorised disclosure of information",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 61,
      "values:originalText": "Disclosures by entrusted persons\n\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person is, or has been, an entrusted person; and\n\n(b) information came to the knowledge or into the possession of\nthe person in the person’s capacity as an entrusted person;\nand\n\n(c) the person discloses the information; and\n\n(d) the information relates to a controlled operation.\nNote:\nRecklessness is the fault element for paragraphs (1)(b) and (d)—see\nsection 5.6 of the Criminal Code.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.\n\n(1A) Strict liability applies to paragraph (1)(a).\nNote:\nFor strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code.\n\n(1B) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person is, or has been, an entrusted person; and\n\n(b) information came to the knowledge or into the possession of\nthe person in the person’s capacity as an entrusted person;\nand\n\n(c) the person discloses the information; and\n\n(d) the information relates to a controlled operation; and\n\n(e) either or both of the following subparagraphs apply:\n\n(i) the person intends to endanger the health or safety of\nany person or prejudice the effective conduct of a\ncontrolled operation;\n\n(ii) the disclosure will endanger the health or safety of any\nperson or prejudice the effective conduct of a controlled\noperation.\n\n\nPart IAB  Controlled operations"
    },
