    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15hp",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15HP Keeping documents connected with controlled operations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15hp"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.71",
      "values:originalText": "The chief officer of an authorising agency must cause the\nfollowing to be kept:\n\n(a) each formal application made to an authorising officer of the\nagency;\n\n(b) each written record of an urgent application made to such an\nauthorising officer;\n\n(c) each formal authority granted by such an authorising officer;\n\n(d) each written record of an urgent authority issued under\nsection 15GL;\n\n\nPart IAB  Controlled operations",
      "skos:definition": "The chief officer of an authorising agency must cause the\nfollowing to be kept:\n\n(a) each formal application made to an authorising officer of the\nagency;\n\n(b) each written record of an urgent application made to such an\nauthorising officer;\n\n(c) each formal authority granted by such an authorising officer;\n\n(d) each written record of an urgent authority issued under\nsection 15GL;\n\n\nPart IAB  Controlled operations",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15hp-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15hp-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b85bc94fac7b3f69692108cb0f23d591b7372dd057b6efd3225946bab4408384",
      "skos:note": "Must keep certain documents connected with controlled operations.",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15hp",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15HP Keeping documents connected with controlled operations",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 71,
      "values:originalText": "The chief officer of an authorising agency must cause the\nfollowing to be kept:\n\n(a) each formal application made to an authorising officer of the\nagency;\n\n(b) each written record of an urgent application made to such an\nauthorising officer;\n\n(c) each formal authority granted by such an authorising officer;\n\n(d) each written record of an urgent authority issued under\nsection 15GL;\n\n\nPart IAB  Controlled operations"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15hp-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15hp"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15hp-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Must provide documents",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15hq",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15HQ General register",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15hq"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.72",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The chief officer of each authorising agency must cause a general\nregister to be kept.\n\n(2) The general register is to specify:\n\n(a) for each application under this Part made to an authorising\nofficer of the agency (including an application for a variation\nof an authority):\n\n(i) the date of the application; and\n\n(ii) whether the application was formal or urgent; and\n\n(iii) whether the application was granted, refused or\nwithdrawn; and\n\n(iv) if the application was refused or withdrawn—the date\nand time of the refusal or withdrawal; and\n\n(b) for each authority under this Part granted by an authorising\nofficer of the agency:\n\n(i) the date and time the authority was granted; and\n\n(ii) whether the authority was formal or urgent; and\n\n\nControlled operations  Part IAB\nCompliance and monitoring  Division 4\n\nSection 15HQ\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(iii) the name and rank or position of the person who granted\nthe authority; and\n\n(iv) each serious Commonwealth offence or serious State\noffence that has a federal aspect in respect of which\ncontrolled conduct under the authority was to be\nengaged in; and\n\n(v) the period of effect of the authority; and\n\n(vi) the identity of each person authorised to engage in\ncontrolled conduct for the purposes of the controlled\noperation; and\n\n(vii) with respect to the law enforcement participants, the\nnature of the controlled conduct that those participants\nwere authorised to engage in; and\n\n(viii) with respect to the civilian participants, the particular\ncontrolled conduct (if any) that each such participant\nwas authorised to engage in; and\n\n(viiia) the nature of the controlled conduct that was engaged in\nby law enforcement participants and civilian\nparticipants (if any); and\n\n(ix) if the authority was cancelled, the date and time of\ncancellation; and\n\n(x) the date and time the controlled operation began, the\ndate on which the operation ceased, and the outcomes of\nthe operation; and\n\n(xi) if the controlled operation involved illicit goods (to the\nextent known), the nature and quantity of the illicit\ngoods and the route and all foreign countries through\nwhich the illicit goods passed in the course of the\noperation; and\n\n(xii) details of any loss of or serious damage to property\n(other than property of the law enforcement agency on\nbehalf of which the operation is conducted or a\nparticipant in the operation) occurring in the course of\nor as a direct result of the controlled operation; and\n\n(xiii) details of any personal injuries occurring in the course\nof or as a direct result of the operation; and\n\n\nPart IAB  Controlled operations",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The chief officer of each authorising agency must cause a general\nregister to be kept.\n\n(2) The general register is to specify:\n\n(a) for each application under this Part made to an authorising\nofficer of the agency (including an application for a variation\nof an authority):\n\n(i) the date of the application; and\n\n(ii) whether the application was formal or urgent; and\n\n(iii) whether the application was granted, refused or\nwithdrawn; and\n\n(iv) if the application was refused or withdrawn—the date\nand time of the refusal or withdrawal; and\n\n(b) for each authority under this Part granted by an authorising\nofficer of the agency:\n\n(i) the date and time the authority was granted; and\n\n(ii) whether the authority was formal or urgent; and\n\n\nControlled operations  Part IAB\nCompliance and monitoring  Division 4\n\nSection 15HQ\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(iii) the name and rank or position of the person who granted\nthe authority; and\n\n(iv) each serious Commonwealth offence or serious State\noffence that has a federal aspect in respect of which\ncontrolled conduct under the authority was to be\nengaged in; and\n\n(v) the period of effect of the authority; and\n\n(vi) the identity of each person authorised to engage in\ncontrolled conduct for the purposes of the controlled\noperation; and\n\n(vii) with respect to the law enforcement participants, the\nnature of the controlled conduct that those participants\nwere authorised to engage in; and\n\n(viii) with respect to the civilian participants, the particular\ncontrolled conduct (if any) that each such participant\nwas authorised to engage in; and\n\n(viiia) the nature of the controlled conduct that was engaged in\nby law enforcement participants and civilian\nparticipants (if any); and\n\n(ix) if the authority was cancelled, the date and time of\ncancellation; and\n\n(x) the date and time the controlled operation began, the\ndate on which the operation ceased, and the outcomes of\nthe operation; and\n\n(xi) if the controlled operation inv",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15hq-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15hq-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "49551334366c8533c92a5c3dfe985338786c154a6739972cfcf57b22ca2dedd5"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15hq",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15HQ General register",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 72,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The chief officer of each authorising agency must cause a general\nregister to be kept.\n\n(2) The general register is to specify:\n\n(a) for each application under this Part made to an authorising\nofficer of the agency (including an application for a variation\nof an authority):\n\n(i) the date of the application; and\n\n(ii) whether the application was formal or urgent; and\n\n(iii) whether the application was granted, refused or\nwithdrawn; and\n\n(iv) if the application was refused or withdrawn—the date\nand time of the refusal or withdrawal; and\n\n(b) for each authority under this Part granted by an authorising\nofficer of the agency:\n\n(i) the date and time the authority was granted; and\n\n(ii) whether the authority was formal or urgent; and\n\n\nControlled operations  Part IAB\nCompliance and monitoring  Division 4\n\nSection 15HQ\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(iii) the name and rank or position of the person who granted\nthe authority; and\n\n(iv) each serious Commonwealth offence or serious State\noffence that has a federal aspect in respect of which\ncontrolled conduct under the authority was to be\nengaged in; and\n\n(v) the period of effect of the authority; and\n\n(vi) the identity of each person authorised to engage in\ncontrolled conduct for the purposes of the controlled\noperation; and\n\n(vii) with respect to the law enforcement participants, the\nnature of the controlled conduct that those participants\nwere authorised to engage in; and\n\n(viii) with respect to the civilian participants, the particular\ncontrolled conduct (if any) that each such participant\nwas authorised to engage in; and\n\n(viiia) the nature of the controlled conduct that was engaged in\nby law enforcement participants and civilian\nparticipants (if any); and\n\n(ix) if the authority was cancelled, the date and time of\ncancellation; and\n\n(x) the date and time the controlled operation began, the\ndate on which the operation ceased, and the outcomes of\nthe operation; and\n\n(xi) if the controlled operation involved illicit goods (to the\nextent known), the nature and quantity of the illicit\ngoods and the route and all foreign countries through\nwhich the illicit goods passed in the course of the\noperation; and\n\n(xii) details of any loss of or serious damage to property\n(other than property of the law enforcement agency on\nbehalf of which the operation is conducted or a\nparticipant in the operation) occurring in the course of\nor as a direct result of the controlled operation; and\n\n(xiii) details of any personal injuries occurring in the course\nof or as a direct result of the operation; and\n\n\nPart IAB  Controlled operations"
    },
    {
