    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15hs",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15HS Inspection of records by the Ombudsman",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15hs"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.75",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Ombudsman must, from time to time and at least once every\n12 months, inspect the records of each authorising agency, except\nthe ACC, to determine the extent of compliance with this Part by\nthe agency and by law enforcement officers of that agency.\n\n(3) For the purpose of an inspection under this section, the\nOmbudsman:\n\n(a) may, after notifying the chief officer of the agency, enter at\nany reasonable time premises occupied by the agency; and\n\n(b) is entitled to have full and free access at all reasonable times\nto all records of the agency that are relevant to the inspection;\nand\n\n(c) may require a member of staff of the agency to give the\nOmbudsman any information that the Ombudsman considers\nnecessary, being information that is in the member’s\npossession, or to which the member has access, and that is\nrelevant to the inspection; and\n\n(d) may, despite any other law, make copies of, and take extracts\nfrom, records of the agency.\n\n\nPart IAB  Controlled operations",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Ombudsman must, from time to time and at least once every\n12 months, inspect the records of each authorising agency, except\nthe ACC, to determine the extent of compliance with this Part by\nthe agency and by law enforcement officers of that agency.\n\n(3) For the purpose of an inspection under this section, the\nOmbudsman:\n\n(a) may, after notifying the chief officer of the agency, enter at\nany reasonable time premises occupied by the agency; and\n\n(b) is entitled to have full and free access at all reasonable times\nto all records of the agency that are relevant to the inspection;\nand\n\n(c) may require a member of staff of the agency to give the\nOmbudsman any information that the Ombudsman considers\nnecessary, being information that is in the member’s\npossession, or to which the member has access, and that is\nrelevant to the inspection; and\n\n(d) may, despite any other law, make copies of, and take extracts\nfrom, records of the agency.\n\n\nPart IAB  Controlled operations",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15hs-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15hs-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c617ef4238cbf25af17a915e1aaaab7445481dfdff5fa45b816b7558e3d04913"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15hs",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15HS Inspection of records by the Ombudsman",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 75,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Ombudsman must, from time to time and at least once every\n12 months, inspect the records of each authorising agency, except\nthe ACC, to determine the extent of compliance with this Part by\nthe agency and by law enforcement officers of that agency.\n\n(3) For the purpose of an inspection under this section, the\nOmbudsman:\n\n(a) may, after notifying the chief officer of the agency, enter at\nany reasonable time premises occupied by the agency; and\n\n(b) is entitled to have full and free access at all reasonable times\nto all records of the agency that are relevant to the inspection;\nand\n\n(c) may require a member of staff of the agency to give the\nOmbudsman any information that the Ombudsman considers\nnecessary, being information that is in the member’s\npossession, or to which the member has access, and that is\nrelevant to the inspection; and\n\n(d) may, despite any other law, make copies of, and take extracts\nfrom, records of the agency.\n\n\nPart IAB  Controlled operations"
    },
    {
