    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ht-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15HT(4) Power to obtain relevant information",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15ht-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.76",
      "values:originalText": "(4) If the Ombudsman:\n\n(a) has reasonable grounds to believe that a law enforcement\nofficer of a particular law enforcement agency (whether or\nnot the agency is an authorising agency) is able to give\ninformation relevant to an inspection under this Division of\nan authorising agency’s records; and\n\n(b) does not know the officer’s identity;\n\n\nControlled operations  Part IAB\nCompliance and monitoring  Division 4\n\nSection 15HU\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nthe Ombudsman may, by writing given to the chief officer of the\nagency, require the chief officer, or a person nominated by the\nchief officer, to attend:\n\n(c) before a specified inspecting officer; and\n\n(d) at a specified place; and\n\n(e) within a specified period or at a specified time on a specified\nday;\nto answer questions relevant to the inspection.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) If the Ombudsman:\n\n(a) has reasonable grounds to believe that a law enforcement\nofficer of a particular law enforcement agency (whether or\nnot the agency is an authorising agency) is able to give\ninformation relevant to an inspection under this Division of\nan authorising agency’s records; and\n\n(b) does not know the officer’s identity;\n\n\nControlled operations  Part IAB\nCompliance and monitoring  Division 4\n\nSection 15HU\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nthe Ombudsman may, by writing given to the chief officer of the\nagency, require the chief officer, or a person nominated by the\nchief officer, to attend:\n\n(c) before a specified inspecting officer; and\n\n(d) at a specified place; and\n\n(e) within a specified period or at a specified time on a specified\nday;\nto answer questions relevant to the inspection.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ht"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ht-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ht-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b973eca766fcb52b1512fb89c5a2b11e22d7ec0ff2fce698fb9ca811bbdc705f",
      "skos:note": "The Ombudsman may require a chief officer to attend an inspection."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15ht-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15HT(4) Power to obtain relevant information",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 76,
      "values:originalText": "(4) If the Ombudsman:\n\n(a) has reasonable grounds to believe that a law enforcement\nofficer of a particular law enforcement agency (whether or\nnot the agency is an authorising agency) is able to give\ninformation relevant to an inspection under this Division of\nan authorising agency’s records; and\n\n(b) does not know the officer’s identity;\n\n\nControlled operations  Part IAB\nCompliance and monitoring  Division 4\n\nSection 15HU\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nthe Ombudsman may, by writing given to the chief officer of the\nagency, require the chief officer, or a person nominated by the\nchief officer, to attend:\n\n(c) before a specified inspecting officer; and\n\n(d) at a specified place; and\n\n(e) within a specified period or at a specified time on a specified\nday;\nto answer questions relevant to the inspection."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ht-ss-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ht-ss-4"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ht-ss-4-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MAY",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to provide information",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The Ombudsman has reasonable grounds to believe...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The chief officer must attend the inspection."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ht-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15HT(5) Power to obtain relevant information",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15ht-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.76",
      "values:originalText": "(5) The place, and the period or the time and day, specified in a\nrequirement under this section, must be reasonable having regard\nto the circumstances in which the requirement is made.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) The place, and the period or the time and day, specified in a\nrequirement under this section, must be reasonable having regard\nto the circumstances in which the requirement is made.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ht"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ht-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ht-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e8c236521817e68a444b08311a8a8fec231a0596314d705adf2848b50fc7a67f",
      "skos:note": "Requirement must be reasonable"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15ht-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15HT(5) Power to obtain relevant information",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 76,
      "values:originalText": "(5) The place, and the period or the time and day, specified in a\nrequirement under this section, must be reasonable having regard\nto the circumstances in which the requirement is made."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ht-ss-5-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
