      "cml:premiseText": "Section 15GI",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Obligation to admit"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15j",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15J Secretary of Immigration and Border Protection Department to",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15j"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.82",
      "values:originalText": "be notified of certain authorities\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) an authority is granted under section 15GI by an AFP\nauthorising officer, an ACC authorising officer or a NACC\nauthorising officer; and\n\n(b) the applicant for the authority believes that illicit goods\ninvolved in the conduct of the operation may be dealt with by\nan officer of Customs.\n\n(2) The applicant must, as soon as practicable after the authority is\ngranted, notify the Secretary of the Immigration and Border\nProtection Department, or a person (the nominated person)\nnominated by him or her for the purposes of this section, in writing\nof:\n\n(a) the applicant’s name; and\n\n(b) the date on which the authority was granted; and\n\n(c) to the extent to which it is known:\n\n(i) the place or places at which the illicit goods will pass\ninto customs control under the Customs Act 1901; and\n\n\nControlled operations  Part IAB\nMiscellaneous  Division 5\n\nSection 15J\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(ii) the time or times when, and the day or days on which,\nthe illicit goods are expected to pass into customs\ncontrol under the Customs Act 1901.\n\n(3) A failure to comply with this section does not affect the validity of\nan authority.\n\n\nPart IABA  Integrity testing",
      "skos:definition": "be notified of certain authorities\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) an authority is granted under section 15GI by an AFP\nauthorising officer, an ACC authorising officer or a NACC\nauthorising officer; and\n\n(b) the applicant for the authority believes that illicit goods\ninvolved in the conduct of the operation may be dealt with by\nan officer of Customs.\n\n(2) The applicant must, as soon as practicable after the authority is\ngranted, notify the Secretary of the Immigration and Border\nProtection Department, or a person (the nominated person)\nnominated by him or her for the purposes of this section, in writing\nof:\n\n(a) the applicant’s name; and\n\n(b) the date on which the authority was granted; and\n\n(c) to the extent to which it is known:\n\n(i) the place or places at which the illicit goods will pass\ninto customs control under the Customs Act 1901; and\n\n\nControlled operations  Part IAB\nMiscellaneous  Division 5\n\nSection 15J\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(ii) the time or times when, and the day or days on which,\nthe illicit goods are expected to pass into customs\ncontrol under the Customs Act 1901.\n\n(3) A failure to comply with this section does not affect the validity of\nan authority.\n\n\nPart IABA  Integrity testing",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15j-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15j-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15j-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c9f80f1c911e34c91f47a3b38dbc7fa9d29d43a4d6edc72d5c762d4608caccd4"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15j",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15J Secretary of Immigration and Border Protection Department to",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 82,
      "values:originalText": "be notified of certain authorities\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) an authority is granted under section 15GI by an AFP\nauthorising officer, an ACC authorising officer or a NACC\nauthorising officer; and\n\n(b) the applicant for the authority believes that illicit goods\ninvolved in the conduct of the operation may be dealt with by\nan officer of Customs.\n\n(2) The applicant must, as soon as practicable after the authority is\ngranted, notify the Secretary of the Immigration and Border\nProtection Department, or a person (the nominated person)\nnominated by him or her for the purposes of this section, in writing\nof:\n\n(a) the applicant’s name; and\n\n(b) the date on which the authority was granted; and\n\n(c) to the extent to which it is known:\n\n(i) the place or places at which the illicit goods will pass\ninto customs control under the Customs Act 1901; and\n\n\nControlled operations  Part IAB\nMiscellaneous  Division 5\n\nSection 15J\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(ii) the time or times when, and the day or days on which,\nthe illicit goods are expected to pass into customs\ncontrol under the Customs Act 1901.\n\n(3) A failure to comply with this section does not affect the validity of\nan authority.\n\n\nPart IABA  Integrity testing"
    },
