      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.82",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The applicant must, as soon as practicable after the authority is\ngranted, notify the Secretary of the Immigration and Border\nProtection Department, or a person (the nominated person)\nnominated by him or her for the purposes of this section, in writing\nof:\n\n(a) the applicant’s name; and\n\n(b) the date on which the authority was granted; and\n\n(c) to the extent to which it is known:\n\n(i) the place or places at which the illicit goods will pass\ninto customs control under the Customs Act 1901; and\n\n\nControlled operations  Part IAB\nMiscellaneous  Division 5\n\nSection 15J\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(ii) the time or times when, and the day or days on which,\nthe illicit goods are expected to pass into customs\ncontrol under the Customs Act 1901.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The applicant must, as soon as practicable after the authority is\ngranted, notify the Secretary of the Immigration and Border\nProtection Department, or a person (the nominated person)\nnominated by him or her for the purposes of this section, in writing\nof:\n\n(a) the applicant’s name; and\n\n(b) the date on which the authority was granted; and\n\n(c) to the extent to which it is known:\n\n(i) the place or places at which the illicit goods will pass\ninto customs control under the Customs Act 1901; and\n\n\nControlled operations  Part IAB\nMiscellaneous  Division 5\n\nSection 15J\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(ii) the time or times when, and the day or days on which,\nthe illicit goods are expected to pass into customs\ncontrol under the Customs Act 1901.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15j"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15j-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15j-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b9212729f52648e02a871f64a02c5d191db6212e2784a61ba79509437aab68c9",
      "skos:note": "Notify the Secretary of Immigration and Border Protection Department or a nominated person in writing of certain information.",
      "dc:description": "yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15j-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15J(2) Secretary of Immigration and Border Protection Department to",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 82,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The applicant must, as soon as practicable after the authority is\ngranted, notify the Secretary of the Immigration and Border\nProtection Department, or a person (the nominated person)\nnominated by him or her for the purposes of this section, in writing\nof:\n\n(a) the applicant’s name; and\n\n(b) the date on which the authority was granted; and\n\n(c) to the extent to which it is known:\n\n(i) the place or places at which the illicit goods will pass\ninto customs control under the Customs Act 1901; and\n\n\nControlled operations  Part IAB\nMiscellaneous  Division 5\n\nSection 15J\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(ii) the time or times when, and the day or days on which,\nthe illicit goods are expected to pass into customs\ncontrol under the Customs Act 1901."
    },
