    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15je",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15JE Integrity testing authorities—circumstances in which",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15je"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.88",
      "values:originalText": "applications may be made\n\n(1) The following table has effect:\n\nIntegrity testing—circumstances in which applications may be made\nItem\nIf a proposed\nintegrity testing\noperation is\nconcerned with …\na staff member of the\nfollowing agency may\napply for authority for\nthe operation …\nfrom the following\nofficer (an\nappropriate\nauthorising officer)\n…\nthe integrity of a staff\nmember of the ACC\nthe ACC\n(a) the Chief\nExecutive Officer\nof the ACC; or\n(b) an SES employee\nin the ACC.\nthe integrity of a staff\nmember of the\nAustralian Federal\nPolice\nthe Australian Federal\nPolice\n(a) the\nCommissioner; or\n(b) a Deputy\nCommissioner; or\n(c) an SES employee\nin the Australian\nFederal Police.\nthe integrity of a staff\nmember of the\nImmigration and\nBorder Protection\nDepartment\nthe Immigration and\nBorder Protection\nDepartment\n(a) the Secretary of\nthe Immigration\nand Border\nProtection\nDepartment; or\n(b) an SES employee\nin the\nImmigration and\nBorder Protection\nDepartment.\n\n\nIntegrity testing  Part IABA\nIntegrity testing operations: authority  Division 2\n\nSection 15JE\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nIntegrity testing—circumstances in which applications may be made\nItem\nIf a proposed\nintegrity testing\noperation is\nconcerned with …\na staff member of the\nfollowing agency may\napply for authority for\nthe operation …\nfrom the following\nofficer (an\nappropriate\nauthorising officer)\n…\na corruption\ninvestigation that\nrelates to a staff\nmember of a target\nagency\n(a) the National\nAnti-Corruption\nCommission; or\n(b) if the corruption issue\nbeing investigated\nrelates to a staff\nmember of the\nACC—the ACC; or\n(c) if the corruption issue\nbeing investigated\nrelates to a staff\nmember of the\nAustralian Federal\nPolice—the\nAustralian Federal\nPolice; or\n(d) if the corruption issue\nbeing investigated\nrelates to a staff\nmember of the\nImmigration and\nBorder Protection\nDepartment—that\nDepartment\n(a) the National\nAnti-Corruption\nCommissioner; or\n(b) a National\nAnti-Corruption\nDeputy\nCommissioner; or\n(c) an SES employee\nin the National\nAnti-Corruption\nCommission.\nNote 1:\nFor target agency, see section 15JC.\nNote 2:\nReferences to a staff member include references to more than one staff\nmember (see section 23 of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901).\n\n(2) The application of item 4 of the table in subsection (1) in relation\nto a staff member of the ACC, the Australian Federal Police or the\nImmigration and Border Protection Department does not prevent\nthe application of any of the other items in the table in relation to\nthe integrity of the staff member.\n\n\nPart IABA  Integrity testing",
      "skos:definition": "applications may be made\n\n(1) The following table has effect:\n\nIntegrity testing—circumstances in which applications may be made\nItem\nIf a proposed\nintegrity testing\noperation is\nconcerned with …\na staff member of the\nfollowing agency may\napply for authority for\nthe operation …\nfrom the following\nofficer (an\nappropriate\nauthorising officer)\n…\nthe integrity of a staff\nmember of the ACC\nthe ACC\n(a) the Chief\nExecutive Officer\nof the ACC; or\n(b) an SES employee\nin the ACC.\nthe integrity of a staff\nmember of the\nAustralian Federal\nPolice\nthe Australian Federal\nPolice\n(a) the\nCommissioner; or\n(b) a Deputy\nCommissioner; or\n(c) an SES employee\nin the Australian\nFederal Police.\nthe integrity of a staff\nmember of the\nImmigration and\nBorder Protection\nDepartment\nthe Immigration and\nBorder Protection\nDepartment\n(a) the Secretary of\nthe Immigration\nand Border\nProtection\nDepartment; or\n(b) an SES employee\nin the\nImmigration and\nBorder Protection\nDepartment.\n\n\nIntegrity testing  Part IABA\nIntegrity testing operations: authority  Division 2\n\nSection 15JE\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nIntegrity testing—circumstances in which applications may be made\nItem\nIf a proposed\nintegrity testing\noperation is\nconcerned with …\na staff member of the\nfollowing agency may\napply for authority for\nthe operation …\nfrom the following\nofficer (an\nappropriate\nauthorising officer)\n…\na corruption\ninvestigation that\nrelates to a staff\nmember of a target\nagency\n(a) the National\nAnti-Corruption\nCommission; or\n(b) if the corruption issue\nbeing investigated\nrelates to a staff\nmember of the\nACC—the ACC; or\n(c) if the corruption issue\nbeing investigated\nrelates to a staff\nmember of the\nAustralian Federal\nPolice—the\nAustralian Federal\nPolice; or\n(d) if the corruption issue\nbeing investigated\nrelates to a staff\nmember of the\nImmigration and\nBorder Protection\nDepartment—that\nDepartment\n(a) the National\nAnti-Corruption\nCommissioner; or\n(b) a National\nAnti-Corruption\nDeputy\nCommissioner; or\n(c) an ",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15je-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15je-ss-2"
