    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15jm",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15JM Integrity testing authorities—defects",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15jm"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.94",
      "values:originalText": "An application for an integrity testing authority or for the variation\nof an authority, and any integrity testing authority or variation\ngranted on the basis of such an application, is not invalidated by\nany defect, other than a defect that affects the application, authority\nor variation in a material particular.\n\n\nIntegrity testing  Part IABA\nIntegrity testing operations: protection of participants  Division 3\n\nSection 15JN\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "An application for an integrity testing authority or for the variation\nof an authority, and any integrity testing authority or variation\ngranted on the basis of such an application, is not invalidated by\nany defect, other than a defect that affects the application, authority\nor variation in a material particular.\n\n\nIntegrity testing  Part IABA\nIntegrity testing operations: protection of participants  Division 3\n\nSection 15JN\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15jm-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15jm-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "edcc389d79f53f232277da864f84a67c9433f2c6c21ef37d763211d362f852d6",
      "skos:note": "An application for an integrity testing authority or for the variation of an authority, and any integrity testing authority or variation granted on the basis of such an application, is not invalidated by any defect."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15jm",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15JM Integrity testing authorities—defects",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 94,
      "values:originalText": "An application for an integrity testing authority or for the variation\nof an authority, and any integrity testing authority or variation\ngranted on the basis of such an application, is not invalidated by\nany defect, other than a defect that affects the application, authority\nor variation in a material particular.\n\n\nIntegrity testing  Part IABA\nIntegrity testing operations: protection of participants  Division 3\n\nSection 15JN\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15jm-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15jm"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15jm-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Implies",
      "cml:logicSummary": "If a defect affects the application, authority or variation in a material particular, then the application is invalidated.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "defect(a) ∧ (a = application ∨ a = authority ∨ a = variation)",
      "cml:conclusionText": "(a = application ∨ a = authority ∨ a = variation) → ¬(application is invalidated by defect(a))"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15jn",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15JN Integrity testing operations—authorised conduct",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15jn"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.95",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), an integrity testing authority for an\nintegrity testing operation authorises each person identified in the\nauthority as a participant to take part in the operation, subject to\nany conditions set out in the authority.\nNote:\nParagraphs 15JH(1)(d) and (e) require participants to be identified,\nand the nature of the operation to be described, in the authority.\nSubsection 15JH(2), however, allows for participants to be identified\nin the authority by an assumed identity, or by code.\n\n(2) A participant is authorised to take part in the integrity testing\noperation for the period of effect of the authority, unless:\n\n(a) the authority states (or is varied to state) a shorter period\nduring which the person is so authorised; or\n\n(b) the authority is varied to provide that the person is no longer\nso authorised; or\n\n(c) the authority is cancelled before the end of that period.\n\n(3) An integrity testing authority does not authorise a participant\nidentified in the authority to delegate participation to another\nperson.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), an integrity testing authority for an\nintegrity testing operation authorises each person identified in the\nauthority as a participant to take part in the operation, subject to\nany conditions set out in the authority.\nNote:\nParagraphs 15JH(1)(d) and (e) require participants to be identified,\nand the nature of the operation to be described, in the authority.\nSubsection 15JH(2), however, allows for participants to be identified\nin the authority by an assumed identity, or by code.\n\n(2) A participant is authorised to take part in the integrity testing\noperation for the period of effect of the authority, unless:\n\n(a) the authority states (or is varied to state) a shorter period\nduring which the person is so authorised; or\n\n(b) the authority is varied to provide that the person is no longer\nso authorised; or\n\n(c) the authority is cancelled before the end of that period.\n\n(3) An integrity testing authority does not authorise a participant\nidentified in the authority to delegate participation to another\nperson.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15jn-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15jn-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15jn-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2a087db36becac2683460fca99848b5b742a0cffa4c78f2bda2f859d7743c4a2"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15jn",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15JN Integrity testing operations—authorised conduct",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 95,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), an integrity testing authority for an\nintegrity testing operation authorises each person identified in the\nauthority as a participant to take part in the operation, subject to\nany conditions set out in the authority.\nNote:\nParagraphs 15JH(1)(d) and (e) require participants to be identified,\nand the nature of the operation to be described, in the authority.\nSubsection 15JH(2), however, allows for participants to be identified\nin the authority by an assumed identity, or by code.\n\n(2) A participant is authorised to take part in the integrity testing\noperation for the period of effect of the authority, unless:\n\n(a) the authority states (or is varied to state) a shorter period\nduring which the person is so authorised; or\n\n(b) the authority is varied to provide that the person is no longer\nso authorised; or\n\n(c) the authority is cancelled before the end of that period.\n\n(3) An integrity testing authority does not authorise a participant\nidentified in the authority to delegate participation to another\nperson."
    },
