    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15jo",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15JO Integrity testing operations—indemnity against civil liability",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15jo"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.95",
      "values:originalText": "The Commonwealth must indemnify a participant in an integrity\ntesting operation that is authorised by an integrity testing authority\nagainst any civil liability (including reasonable costs) the\nparticipant incurs because of conduct the participant engages in if:\n\n(a) the participant engages in the conduct in the course of, and\nfor the purposes of, the operation in accordance with the\nauthority; and\n\n(b) the participant is identified in the authority; and\n\n\nPart IABA  Integrity testing",
      "skos:definition": "The Commonwealth must indemnify a participant in an integrity\ntesting operation that is authorised by an integrity testing authority\nagainst any civil liability (including reasonable costs) the\nparticipant incurs because of conduct the participant engages in if:\n\n(a) the participant engages in the conduct in the course of, and\nfor the purposes of, the operation in accordance with the\nauthority; and\n\n(b) the participant is identified in the authority; and\n\n\nPart IABA  Integrity testing",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15jo-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15jo-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "101c88ecd483e06591ae0dbad822cf2812a61b14ad9aacfadae43383d70e81bb",
      "skos:note": "Commonwealth must indemnify participant in integrity testing operation against civil liability."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15jo",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15JO Integrity testing operations—indemnity against civil liability",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 95,
      "values:originalText": "The Commonwealth must indemnify a participant in an integrity\ntesting operation that is authorised by an integrity testing authority\nagainst any civil liability (including reasonable costs) the\nparticipant incurs because of conduct the participant engages in if:\n\n(a) the participant engages in the conduct in the course of, and\nfor the purposes of, the operation in accordance with the\nauthority; and\n\n(b) the participant is identified in the authority; and\n\n\nPart IABA  Integrity testing"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15jo-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15jo"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15jo-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Commonwealth has an obligation to indemnify participant.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The Commonwealth must indemnify...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...against any civil liability..."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15jp",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15JP Integrity testing operations—participants unaware of",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15jp"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.96",
      "values:originalText": "variation or cancellation of authority\n\n(1) If an integrity testing authority for an integrity testing operation is\nvaried in a way that limits the scope of the operation, this\nPart continues to apply to a participant in the operation as if the\nauthority had not been varied in that way, for so long as the\nparticipant:\n\n(a) is unaware of the variation; and\n\n(b) is not reckless about the existence of the variation.\n\n(2) If an integrity testing authority to conduct an integrity testing\noperation is cancelled, this Part continues to apply to a person who\nwas a participant in the operation immediately before the\ncancellation as if the authority had not been cancelled in that way,\nfor so long as the person:\n\n(a) is unaware of the cancellation; and\n\n(b) is not reckless about the existence of the cancellation.\n\n(3) For the purposes of this section, a person is reckless about the\nexistence of the variation or cancellation of an integrity testing\nauthority if:\n\n\nIntegrity testing  Part IABA\nIntegrity testing operations: protection of participants  Division 3\n\nSection 15JP\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) the person is aware of a substantial risk that the variation or\ncancellation has happened; and\n\n(b) having regard to the circumstances known to the person, it is\nunjustifiable to take the risk that the authority has not been\nvaried or cancelled.\n\n\nPart IABA  Integrity testing",
      "skos:definition": "variation or cancellation of authority\n\n(1) If an integrity testing authority for an integrity testing operation is\nvaried in a way that limits the scope of the operation, this\nPart continues to apply to a participant in the operation as if the\nauthority had not been varied in that way, for so long as the\nparticipant:\n\n(a) is unaware of the variation; and\n\n(b) is not reckless about the existence of the variation.\n\n(2) If an integrity testing authority to conduct an integrity testing\noperation is cancelled, this Part continues to apply to a person who\nwas a participant in the operation immediately before the\ncancellation as if the authority had not been cancelled in that way,\nfor so long as the person:\n\n(a) is unaware of the cancellation; and\n\n(b) is not reckless about the existence of the cancellation.\n\n(3) For the purposes of this section, a person is reckless about the\nexistence of the variation or cancellation of an integrity testing\nauthority if:\n\n\nIntegrity testing  Part IABA\nIntegrity testing operations: protection of participants  Division 3\n\nSection 15JP\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) the person is aware of a substantial risk that the variation or\ncancellation has happened; and\n\n(b) having regard to the circumstances known to the person, it is\nunjustifiable to take the risk that the authority has not been\nvaried or cancelled.\n\n\nPart IABA  Integrity testing",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15jp-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15jp-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15jp-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "abf2169c7ae5d766ec982f835fed5c6303699b3b3f0a651131c932343d287804"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15jp",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15JP Integrity testing operations—participants unaware of",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 96,
      "values:originalText": "variation or cancellation of authority\n\n(1) If an integrity testing authority for an integrity testing operation is\nvaried in a way that limits the scope of the operation, this\nPart continues to apply to a participant in the operation as if the\nauthority had not been varied in that way, for so long as the\nparticipant:\n\n(a) is unaware of the variation; and\n\n(b) is not reckless about the existence of the variation.\n\n(2) If an integrity testing authority to conduct an integrity testing\noperation is cancelled, this Part continues to apply to a person who\nwas a participant in the operation immediately before the\ncancellation as if the authority had not been cancelled in that way,\nfor so long as the person:\n\n(a) is unaware of the cancellation; and\n\n(b) is not reckless about the existence of the cancellation.\n\n(3) For the purposes of this section, a person is reckless about the\nexistence of the variation or cancellation of an integrity testing\nauthority if:\n\n\nIntegrity testing  Part IABA\nIntegrity testing operations: protection of participants  Division 3\n\nSection 15JP\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) the person is aware of a substantial risk that the variation or\ncancellation has happened; and\n\n(b) having regard to the circumstances known to the person, it is\nunjustifiable to take the risk that the authority has not been\nvaried or cancelled.\n\n\nPart IABA  Integrity testing"
    },
