        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15jp-ss-3-logic-epistemic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f58196575701ca48f376169e1b88fb992fc01d5f076567008e6c8ce161bdcf8b",
      "skos:note": "Be aware of substantial risk that variation or cancellation has happened and unjustifiable to take the risk."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15jp-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15JP(3) Integrity testing operations—participants unaware of",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 96,
      "values:originalText": "(3) For the purposes of this section, a person is reckless about the\nexistence of the variation or cancellation of an integrity testing\nauthority if:\n\n\nIntegrity testing  Part IABA\nIntegrity testing operations: protection of participants  Division 3\n\nSection 15JP\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) the person is aware of a substantial risk that the variation or\ncancellation has happened; and\n\n(b) having regard to the circumstances known to the person, it is\nunjustifiable to take the risk that the authority has not been\nvaried or cancelled.\n\n\nPart IABA  Integrity testing"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15jp-ss-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
