          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15js-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15js-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "089002424bdf9613ff151451ecf51a26b72879d017f65e96e0524ee01adf6c96",
      "skos:note": "Annual report requirements for integrity testing authorities",
      "dc:description": "Details of granted authorities, suspected criminal activity, and authority periods"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15js-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15JS(2) Integrity testing operations—annual reports",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 102,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The details to be set out in the report are as follows:\n\n(a) the number of integrity testing authorities granted by\nauthorising officers of the agency;\n\n(b) the nature of the suspected criminal activity in relation to\nwhich each authority was given;\n\n(c) the period of effect of each authority (including any\nextension of the period granted by variation);\n\n(d) if an authority was cancelled—the reasons for cancellation."
    },
