    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15js-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15JS(5) Integrity testing operations—annual reports",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15js-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.102",
      "values:originalText": "(5) In this section:\nchief officer, of an integrity testing agency, means:\n\n(a) for the ACC—the Chief Executive Officer of the ACC; or\n\n(b) for the Australian Federal Police—the Commissioner; or\n\n(c) for the Immigration and Border Protection Department—the\nSecretary of that Department; or\n\n\nIntegrity testing  Part IABA\nIntegrity testing operations: reporting  Division 5\n\nSection 15JS\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(d) for the National Anti-Corruption Commission—the National\nAnti-Corruption Commissioner.\nLaw Enforcement Minister means the Minister responsible for the\nadministration of the National Anti-Corruption Commission Act\n2022.\n\n\nPart IABA  Integrity testing",
      "skos:definition": "(5) In this section:\nchief officer, of an integrity testing agency, means:\n\n(a) for the ACC—the Chief Executive Officer of the ACC; or\n\n(b) for the Australian Federal Police—the Commissioner; or\n\n(c) for the Immigration and Border Protection Department—the\nSecretary of that Department; or\n\n\nIntegrity testing  Part IABA\nIntegrity testing operations: reporting  Division 5\n\nSection 15JS\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(d) for the National Anti-Corruption Commission—the National\nAnti-Corruption Commissioner.\nLaw Enforcement Minister means the Minister responsible for the\nadministration of the National Anti-Corruption Commission Act\n2022.\n\n\nPart IABA  Integrity testing",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15js"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15js-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15js-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15js-ss-5-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ae5ce29bb6f95d28f23256d7487bc1e17c91d6e173f509b2f0932f4a25f82530",
      "skos:note": "Annual reports must be provided by integrity testing agencies.",
      "dc:description": "annual reports"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15js-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15JS(5) Integrity testing operations—annual reports",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 102,
      "values:originalText": "(5) In this section:\nchief officer, of an integrity testing agency, means:\n\n(a) for the ACC—the Chief Executive Officer of the ACC; or\n\n(b) for the Australian Federal Police—the Commissioner; or\n\n(c) for the Immigration and Border Protection Department—the\nSecretary of that Department; or\n\n\nIntegrity testing  Part IABA\nIntegrity testing operations: reporting  Division 5\n\nSection 15JS\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(d) for the National Anti-Corruption Commission—the National\nAnti-Corruption Commissioner.\nLaw Enforcement Minister means the Minister responsible for the\nadministration of the National Anti-Corruption Commission Act\n2022.\n\n\nPart IABA  Integrity testing"
    },
