    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15jt",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15JT Evidence of integrity testing authorities",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15jt"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.104",
      "values:originalText": "A document purporting to be an integrity testing authority:\n\n(a) is admissible in any legal proceedings; and\n\n(b) in the absence of evidence to the contrary, is proof in any\nproceedings (not being criminal or disciplinary proceedings\nagainst a law enforcement officer) that the person granting\nthe authority was satisfied of the facts he or she was required\nto be satisfied of to grant the authority.\n\n\nAssumed Identities  Part IAC\nPreliminary  Division 1\n\nSection 15K\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nPart IAC—Assumed Identities",
      "skos:definition": "A document purporting to be an integrity testing authority:\n\n(a) is admissible in any legal proceedings; and\n\n(b) in the absence of evidence to the contrary, is proof in any\nproceedings (not being criminal or disciplinary proceedings\nagainst a law enforcement officer) that the person granting\nthe authority was satisfied of the facts he or she was required\nto be satisfied of to grant the authority.\n\n\nAssumed Identities  Part IAC\nPreliminary  Division 1\n\nSection 15K\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nPart IAC—Assumed Identities",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15jt-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15jt-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1b74e265bcc1673944988a2497a93020e24fc449bd819de0d50a992a568f9c53",
      "skos:note": "A document purporting to be an integrity testing authority is admissible in legal proceedings."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15jt",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15JT Evidence of integrity testing authorities",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 104,
      "values:originalText": "A document purporting to be an integrity testing authority:\n\n(a) is admissible in any legal proceedings; and\n\n(b) in the absence of evidence to the contrary, is proof in any\nproceedings (not being criminal or disciplinary proceedings\nagainst a law enforcement officer) that the person granting\nthe authority was satisfied of the facts he or she was required\nto be satisfied of to grant the authority.\n\n\nAssumed Identities  Part IAC\nPreliminary  Division 1\n\nSection 15K\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nPart IAC—Assumed Identities"
    },
    {
