    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ka",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15KA Application for authority to acquire or use assumed identity",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15ka"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.111",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A law enforcement officer of a law enforcement agency may apply\nto the chief officer mentioned in subsection (2) for an authority for\nthe officer or any other person to do either or both of the following:\n\n(a) acquire an assumed identity;\n\n(b) use an assumed identity.\n\n(2) An application by a law enforcement officer of a law enforcement\nagency under subsection (1) is to be made to:\n\n(a) if the person who is to acquire or use the assumed identity is\na foreign officer, or the assumed identity is to be used in a\nforeign country:\n\n(i) if the applicant is a member of the staff of the ACC—\nthe chief officer of the ACC; or\n\n(ii) in any other case—the chief officer of the Australian\nFederal Police; or\n\n(b) in any other case—the chief officer of the law enforcement\nagency.\n\n(3) An intelligence officer of an intelligence agency may apply to the\nchief officer of the agency for an authority for the officer or any\nother person (including a foreign officer) to do either or both of the\nfollowing:\n\n(a) acquire an assumed identity;\n\n(b) use an assumed identity.\n\n(3A) An application may only be made under subsection (3) by an\nintelligence officer of the Office of National Intelligence (ONI) for\nthe purpose of ONI carrying out its function under\nparagraph 7(1)(g) of the Office of National Intelligence Act 2018.\n\n(4) A separate application must be made in respect of each assumed\nidentity to be acquired or used.\n\n\nPart IAC  Assumed Identities",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A law enforcement officer of a law enforcement agency may apply\nto the chief officer mentioned in subsection (2) for an authority for\nthe officer or any other person to do either or both of the following:\n\n(a) acquire an assumed identity;\n\n(b) use an assumed identity.\n\n(2) An application by a law enforcement officer of a law enforcement\nagency under subsection (1) is to be made to:\n\n(a) if the person who is to acquire or use the assumed identity is\na foreign officer, or the assumed identity is to be used in a\nforeign country:\n\n(i) if the applicant is a member of the staff of the ACC—\nthe chief officer of the ACC; or\n\n(ii) in any other case—the chief officer of the Australian\nFederal Police; or\n\n(b) in any other case—the chief officer of the law enforcement\nagency.\n\n(3) An intelligence officer of an intelligence agency may apply to the\nchief officer of the agency for an authority for the officer or any\nother person (including a foreign officer) to do either or both of the\nfollowing:\n\n(a) acquire an assumed identity;\n\n(b) use an assumed identity.\n\n(3A) An application may only be made under subsection (3) by an\nintelligence officer of the Office of National Intelligence (ONI) for\nthe purpose of ONI carrying out its function under\nparagraph 7(1)(g) of the Office of National Intelligence Act 2018.\n\n(4) A separate application must be made in respect of each assumed\nidentity to be acquired or used.\n\n\nPart IAC  Assumed Identities",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ka-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ka-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ka-ss-3"
