    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15kc",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15KC Form of authority",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15kc"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.115",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An authority must be:\n\n(a) in writing in the form approved by the chief officer; and\n\n(b) signed by the person granting it.\n\n(2) An authority must state the following:\n\n(a) the name of the person granting the authority;\n\n(b) the date of the authority;\n\n(c) details of the assumed identity authorised;\n\n(d) details of any evidence of the assumed identity that may be\nacquired under the authority;\n\n(e) the conditions (if any) to which the authority is subject;\n\n(f) why the authority is granted;\n\n\nPart IAC  Assumed Identities",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An authority must be:\n\n(a) in writing in the form approved by the chief officer; and\n\n(b) signed by the person granting it.\n\n(2) An authority must state the following:\n\n(a) the name of the person granting the authority;\n\n(b) the date of the authority;\n\n(c) details of the assumed identity authorised;\n\n(d) details of any evidence of the assumed identity that may be\nacquired under the authority;\n\n(e) the conditions (if any) to which the authority is subject;\n\n(f) why the authority is granted;\n\n\nPart IAC  Assumed Identities",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15kc-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15kc-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e6a584a43c7f5e62215052639a737af37e051df296ba18d7cbcbc51e2d66b7bc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15kc",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15KC Form of authority",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 115,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An authority must be:\n\n(a) in writing in the form approved by the chief officer; and\n\n(b) signed by the person granting it.\n\n(2) An authority must state the following:\n\n(a) the name of the person granting the authority;\n\n(b) the date of the authority;\n\n(c) details of the assumed identity authorised;\n\n(d) details of any evidence of the assumed identity that may be\nacquired under the authority;\n\n(e) the conditions (if any) to which the authority is subject;\n\n(f) why the authority is granted;\n\n\nPart IAC  Assumed Identities"
    },
