      "cml:premiseText": "(4) If the chief officer is satisfied...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "he or she must cancel the authority under section 15KE."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15kf-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15KF(5) Yearly review of authority",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15kf-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.118",
      "values:originalText": "(5) If the chief officer is satisfied on a review that use of the assumed\nidentity under the authority is still necessary, he or she must record\nhis or her opinion, and the reasons for it, in writing.\nNote:\nThe chief officer may delegate functions under this section—see\nsection 15LH.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) If the chief officer is satisfied on a review that use of the assumed\nidentity under the authority is still necessary, he or she must record\nhis or her opinion, and the reasons for it, in writing.\nNote:\nThe chief officer may delegate functions under this section—see\nsection 15LH.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15kf"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15kf-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15kf-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "52c6b936202c25738f4c9905901aa5ebe96fa6bfe582a2dabee14ad44d74ad21",
      "skos:note": "Chief officer must record opinion and reasons if use of assumed identity is necessary.",
      "dc:description": "Opinion and reasons"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15kf-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15KF(5) Yearly review of authority",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 118,
      "values:originalText": "(5) If the chief officer is satisfied on a review that use of the assumed\nidentity under the authority is still necessary, he or she must record\nhis or her opinion, and the reasons for it, in writing.\nNote:\nThe chief officer may delegate functions under this section—see\nsection 15LH."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15kf-ss-5-norm",
