    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15kg",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15KG Making entries in register of births, deaths or marriages",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15kg"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.119",
      "values:originalText": "The chief officer of:\n\n(a) a law enforcement agency; or\n\n(b) an intelligence agency (other than the Office of National\nIntelligence or the Australian Signals Directorate);\nmay apply, under a corresponding assumed identity law, to the\nSupreme Court of a State or Territory of a participating jurisdiction\nfor an order that an entry be made in a register of births, deaths or\nmarriages under the relevant law of that jurisdiction in relation to\nthe acquisition of an assumed identity under an authority or\ncorresponding authority.",
      "skos:definition": "The chief officer of:\n\n(a) a law enforcement agency; or\n\n(b) an intelligence agency (other than the Office of National\nIntelligence or the Australian Signals Directorate);\nmay apply, under a corresponding assumed identity law, to the\nSupreme Court of a State or Territory of a participating jurisdiction\nfor an order that an entry be made in a register of births, deaths or\nmarriages under the relevant law of that jurisdiction in relation to\nthe acquisition of an assumed identity under an authority or\ncorresponding authority.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15kg-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15kg-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8971edca901207d1f08fefbd76810bed7aa2667461a45d3ae30337b2bfd8aad7",
      "skos:note": "Permits chief officers of law enforcement agencies or intelligence agencies to apply for an order in the Supreme Court of a State or Territory."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15kg",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15KG Making entries in register of births, deaths or marriages",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 119,
      "values:originalText": "The chief officer of:\n\n(a) a law enforcement agency; or\n\n(b) an intelligence agency (other than the Office of National\nIntelligence or the Australian Signals Directorate);\nmay apply, under a corresponding assumed identity law, to the\nSupreme Court of a State or Territory of a participating jurisdiction\nfor an order that an entry be made in a register of births, deaths or\nmarriages under the relevant law of that jurisdiction in relation to\nthe acquisition of an assumed identity under an authority or\ncorresponding authority."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15kg-norm",
      "@type": "values:Permission",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15kg"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15kg-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Permit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Allows action",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15kh",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15KH Effect of authority ceasing to be in force on register of births,",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15kh"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.119",
      "values:originalText": "deaths or marriages\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) an authority for an assumed identity ceases to be in force;\nand\n\n(b) there is an entry in relation to that assumed identity in a\nregister of births, deaths or marriages because of an order\nunder a corresponding assumed identity law.\n\n(2) The chief officer of a law enforcement agency or an intelligence\nagency (other than the Office of National Intelligence or the\nAustralian Signals Directorate) must apply for an order under the\ncorresponding assumed identity law to cancel the entry within 28\ndays after the day the authority ceases to be in force.\n\n\nPart IAC  Assumed Identities",
      "skos:definition": "deaths or marriages\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) an authority for an assumed identity ceases to be in force;\nand\n\n(b) there is an entry in relation to that assumed identity in a\nregister of births, deaths or marriages because of an order\nunder a corresponding assumed identity law.\n\n(2) The chief officer of a law enforcement agency or an intelligence\nagency (other than the Office of National Intelligence or the\nAustralian Signals Directorate) must apply for an order under the\ncorresponding assumed identity law to cancel the entry within 28\ndays after the day the authority ceases to be in force.\n\n\nPart IAC  Assumed Identities",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15kh-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15kh-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "fd8ca8e4b5150e9bd85b0d5e76e060e0b26dccf84a6ccbae28cae9d56e81f323"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15kh",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15KH Effect of authority ceasing to be in force on register of births,",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 119,
      "values:originalText": "deaths or marriages\n\n(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) an authority for an assumed identity ceases to be in force;\nand\n\n(b) there is an entry in relation to that assumed identity in a\nregister of births, deaths or marriages because of an order\nunder a corresponding assumed identity law.\n\n(2) The chief officer of a law enforcement agency or an intelligence\nagency (other than the Office of National Intelligence or the\nAustralian Signals Directorate) must apply for an order under the\ncorresponding assumed identity law to cancel the entry within 28\ndays after the day the authority ceases to be in force.\n\n\nPart IAC  Assumed Identities"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15kh-ss-1",
