    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15kl",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15KL Cancellation of evidence of assumed identity",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15kl"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.121",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The chief officer of an issuing agency who produces evidence of\nan assumed identity under this Part must cancel the evidence if\ndirected in writing to do so by the chief officer who requested the\nevidence.\nNote 1:\nThe chief officer who requested the evidence may delegate functions\nunder this section—see section 15LH.\n\n\nPart IAC  Assumed Identities",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The chief officer of an issuing agency who produces evidence of\nan assumed identity under this Part must cancel the evidence if\ndirected in writing to do so by the chief officer who requested the\nevidence.\nNote 1:\nThe chief officer who requested the evidence may delegate functions\nunder this section—see section 15LH.\n\n\nPart IAC  Assumed Identities",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15kl-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15kl-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "99f99496f92c14222c54cf5eb6d65ad1edcc13c74887e4a532a23d62b5c324e5",
      "skos:note": "Chief officer must cancel evidence of assumed identity upon written direction."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15kl",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15KL Cancellation of evidence of assumed identity",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 121,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The chief officer of an issuing agency who produces evidence of\nan assumed identity under this Part must cancel the evidence if\ndirected in writing to do so by the chief officer who requested the\nevidence.\nNote 1:\nThe chief officer who requested the evidence may delegate functions\nunder this section—see section 15LH.\n\n\nPart IAC  Assumed Identities"
    },
