      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The person is an authorised person (other than an authorised civilian) and the acquisition or use is in accordance with an authority; and",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The person may acquire or use an assumed identity if..."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15kp-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Permit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Acquiring or using an assumed identity is permitted under certain conditions.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The person is an authorised civilian and the acquisition or use is in accordance with an authority; and",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The person may acquire or use an assumed identity if..."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15kp-logic-deontic-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Permit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Acquiring or using an assumed identity is permitted under certain conditions.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Any direction by the person’s supervisor under the authority.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The person may acquire or use an assumed identity if..."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15kq",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15KQ Protection from criminal liability—authorised persons",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15kq"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.124",
      "values:originalText": "If an authorised person does something that, apart from this\nsection, would be a Commonwealth offence or an offence under a\nlaw of a State or Territory, the person is not criminally responsible\nfor the offence if:\n\n(a) the thing is done in the course of acquiring or using an\nassumed identity in accordance with an authority; and\n\n(b) the thing is done:\n\n(i) in the case of an authorised intelligence officer, an\nauthorised law enforcement officer or an authorised\nforeign officer—in the course of his or her duty; or\n\n(ii) in the case of an authorised civilian—in accordance\nwith any direction by his or her supervisor under the\nauthority; and\n\n(c) doing the thing would not be an offence if the assumed\nidentity were the person’s real identity.\n\n\nAssumed Identities  Part IAC\nEffect of Authority  Division 4\n\nSection 15KR\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "If an authorised person does something that, apart from this\nsection, would be a Commonwealth offence or an offence under a\nlaw of a State or Territory, the person is not criminally responsible\nfor the offence if:\n\n(a) the thing is done in the course of acquiring or using an\nassumed identity in accordance with an authority; and\n\n(b) the thing is done:\n\n(i) in the case of an authorised intelligence officer, an\nauthorised law enforcement officer or an authorised\nforeign officer—in the course of his or her duty; or\n\n(ii) in the case of an authorised civilian—in accordance\nwith any direction by his or her supervisor under the\nauthority; and\n\n(c) doing the thing would not be an offence if the assumed\nidentity were the person’s real identity.\n\n\nAssumed Identities  Part IAC\nEffect of Authority  Division 4\n\nSection 15KR\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15kq-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15kq-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15kq-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "30d29bbd65eb7fc54e469c9e37b3a1475d36b32c8bd7e4a385d152c94ab33c93",
      "skos:note": "An authorised person is not criminally responsible for an offence if they act in accordance with authority."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15kq",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15KQ Protection from criminal liability—authorised persons",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 124,
      "values:originalText": "If an authorised person does something that, apart from this\nsection, would be a Commonwealth offence or an offence under a\nlaw of a State or Territory, the person is not criminally responsible\nfor the offence if:\n\n(a) the thing is done in the course of acquiring or using an\nassumed identity in accordance with an authority; and\n\n(b) the thing is done:\n\n(i) in the case of an authorised intelligence officer, an\nauthorised law enforcement officer or an authorised\nforeign officer—in the course of his or her duty; or\n\n(ii) in the case of an authorised civilian—in accordance\nwith any direction by his or her supervisor under the\nauthority; and\n\n(c) doing the thing would not be an offence if the assumed\nidentity were the person’s real identity.\n\n\nAssumed Identities  Part IAC\nEffect of Authority  Division 4\n\nSection 15KR\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026"
    },
    {
