    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ks",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15KS Indemnity for authorised persons",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15ks"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.125",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if the chief officer of either a law enforcement\nagency or an intelligence agency grants an authority.\n\n(2) The Commonwealth must indemnify the authorised person under\nthe authority for any liability incurred by the person (including\nreasonable costs) because of something done by the person if:\n\n(a) the thing is done in the course of acquiring or using an\nassumed identity in accordance with the authority; and\n\n(b) the thing is done:\n\n(i) in the case of an authorised intelligence officer, an\nauthorised law enforcement officer or an authorised\nforeign officer—in the course of his or her duty; or\n\n(ii) in the case of an authorised civilian—in accordance\nwith any direction by his or her supervisor under the\nauthority; and\n\n(c) any requirements prescribed under the regulations have been\nmet.\n\n\nPart IAC  Assumed Identities",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies if the chief officer of either a law enforcement\nagency or an intelligence agency grants an authority.\n\n(2) The Commonwealth must indemnify the authorised person under\nthe authority for any liability incurred by the person (including\nreasonable costs) because of something done by the person if:\n\n(a) the thing is done in the course of acquiring or using an\nassumed identity in accordance with the authority; and\n\n(b) the thing is done:\n\n(i) in the case of an authorised intelligence officer, an\nauthorised law enforcement officer or an authorised\nforeign officer—in the course of his or her duty; or\n\n(ii) in the case of an authorised civilian—in accordance\nwith any direction by his or her supervisor under the\nauthority; and\n\n(c) any requirements prescribed under the regulations have been\nmet.\n\n\nPart IAC  Assumed Identities",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ks-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ks-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d4713051a0a810f66efed6718deb326852599e36912f9c6c733d629142952923"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15ks",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15KS Indemnity for authorised persons",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 125,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if the chief officer of either a law enforcement\nagency or an intelligence agency grants an authority.\n\n(2) The Commonwealth must indemnify the authorised person under\nthe authority for any liability incurred by the person (including\nreasonable costs) because of something done by the person if:\n\n(a) the thing is done in the course of acquiring or using an\nassumed identity in accordance with the authority; and\n\n(b) the thing is done:\n\n(i) in the case of an authorised intelligence officer, an\nauthorised law enforcement officer or an authorised\nforeign officer—in the course of his or her duty; or\n\n(ii) in the case of an authorised civilian—in accordance\nwith any direction by his or her supervisor under the\nauthority; and\n\n(c) any requirements prescribed under the regulations have been\nmet.\n\n\nPart IAC  Assumed Identities"
    },
