      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.128",
      "values:originalText": "(3) The following provisions have effect, after the transfer, as if the\nchief officer of the receiving agency had granted the authority\ninstead of the chief officer of the originating agency:\n\n(a) section 15KE (which deals with variation and cancellation of\nauthorities);\n\n(b) section 15KF (which deals with review of authorities);\n\n(c) sections 15KI and 15KX (which deal with requests for\nevidence of assumed identities).\n\n\nAssumed Identities  Part IAC\nEffect of Authority  Division 4\n\nSection 15KW\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(3) The following provisions have effect, after the transfer, as if the\nchief officer of the receiving agency had granted the authority\ninstead of the chief officer of the originating agency:\n\n(a) section 15KE (which deals with variation and cancellation of\nauthorities);\n\n(b) section 15KF (which deals with review of authorities);\n\n(c) sections 15KI and 15KX (which deal with requests for\nevidence of assumed identities).\n\n\nAssumed Identities  Part IAC\nEffect of Authority  Division 4\n\nSection 15KW\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15kw"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15kw-ss-3-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f952d8f5dd2dd0db216d17411a65cbbae9c96dc93fe48f5d06f8e705983adff8",
      "skos:note": "Provisions have effect as if chief officer of receiving agency granted authority instead of originating agency"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15kw-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15KW(3) Consequences of transfer of control of authorities",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 128,
      "values:originalText": "(3) The following provisions have effect, after the transfer, as if the\nchief officer of the receiving agency had granted the authority\ninstead of the chief officer of the originating agency:\n\n(a) section 15KE (which deals with variation and cancellation of\nauthorities);\n\n(b) section 15KF (which deals with review of authorities);\n\n(c) sections 15KI and 15KX (which deal with requests for\nevidence of assumed identities).\n\n\nAssumed Identities  Part IAC\nEffect of Authority  Division 4\n\nSection 15KW\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15kw-ss-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15kw-ss-3"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15kw-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15KW(4) Consequences of transfer of control of authorities",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15kw-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.128",
      "values:originalText": "(4) To avoid doubt, the obligation under section 15KF, as that section\nhas effect because of subsection (3), for the chief officer of the\nreceiving agency to review the authority, only arises:\n\n(a) in the case of an authority transferred under\nsubsection 15KV(1):\n\n(i) 3 years after the last review of the authority by the chief\nofficer of an intelligence agency; or\n\n(ii) if no such review has been undertaken—3 years after\nthe authority was granted; and\n\n(b) in the case of an authority transferred under\nsubsection 15KV(2):\n\n(i) 12 months after the last review of the authority by the\nchief officer of a law enforcement agency; or\n\n(ii) if no such review has been undertaken—12 months after\nthe authority was granted.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) To avoid doubt, the obligation under section 15KF, as that section\nhas effect because of subsection (3), for the chief officer of the\nreceiving agency to review the authority, only arises:\n\n(a) in the case of an authority transferred under\nsubsection 15KV(1):\n\n(i) 3 years after the last review of the authority by the chief\nofficer of an intelligence agency; or\n\n(ii) if no such review has been undertaken—3 years after\nthe authority was granted; and\n\n(b) in the case of an authority transferred under\nsubsection 15KV(2):\n\n(i) 12 months after the last review of the authority by the\nchief officer of a law enforcement agency; or\n\n(ii) if no such review has been undertaken—12 months after\nthe authority was granted.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15kw"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15kw-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15kw-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b68aed89d14b85c2513b67ea3c6f467ee5acd57dd3360f3d08a728027b405b66",
      "skos:note": "Chief officer of receiving agency must review authority within specified timeframes."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15kw-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15KW(4) Consequences of transfer of control of authorities",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 128,
      "values:originalText": "(4) To avoid doubt, the obligation under section 15KF, as that section\nhas effect because of subsection (3), for the chief officer of the\nreceiving agency to review the authority, only arises:\n\n(a) in the case of an authority transferred under\nsubsection 15KV(1):\n\n(i) 3 years after the last review of the authority by the chief\nofficer of an intelligence agency; or\n\n(ii) if no such review has been undertaken—3 years after\nthe authority was granted; and\n\n(b) in the case of an authority transferred under\nsubsection 15KV(2):\n\n(i) 12 months after the last review of the authority by the\nchief officer of a law enforcement agency; or\n\n(ii) if no such review has been undertaken—12 months after\nthe authority was granted."
    },
