    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15kx",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15KX Requests to a participating jurisdiction for evidence of",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15kx"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.130",
      "values:originalText": "assumed identity\n\n(1) This section applies if an authority granted under section 15KB\nauthorises a request under this section.\n\n(2) The person specified in subsection (2A) may request the chief\nofficer of an issuing agency of a participating jurisdiction stated in\nthe authority to:\n\n(a) produce evidence of the assumed identity in accordance with\nthe authority; and\n\n(b) give evidence of the assumed identity to the following:\n\n(i) the authorised person named in the authority;\n\n(ii) an officer of the law enforcement agency or the\nintelligence agency who is named in the request.\nNote:\nSection 15KW modifies the effect of this provision if control of the\nauthority is transferred.\n\n(2A) For the purposes of subsection (2), the person who may make the\nrequest is:\n\n(a) the chief officer of a law enforcement agency who granted\nthe authority; or\n\n(b) the chief officer of an intelligence agency (other than the\nOffice of National Intelligence or the Australian Signals\nDirectorate) who granted the authority; or\n\n(c) if the chief officer of the Office of National Intelligence\ngranted the authority—the chief officer of the Australian\nSecurity Intelligence Organisation or the Australian Secret\nIntelligence Service; or\n\n(d) if the chief officer of the Australian Signals Directorate\ngranted the authority—the chief officer of the Australian\nSecurity Intelligence Organisation or the Australian Secret\nIntelligence Service.\n\n\nAssumed Identities  Part IAC\nMutual Recognition under Corresponding Laws  Division 5\n\nSection 15KY\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nNote:\nThe chief officer may delegate functions under this section—see\nsection 15LH.\n\n(3) The request must state that it is a request under this section.\n\n(4) A request must not be made under this section for an entry in a\nregister of births, deaths or marriages.",
      "skos:definition": "assumed identity\n\n(1) This section applies if an authority granted under section 15KB\nauthorises a request under this section.\n\n(2) The person specified in subsection (2A) may request the chief\nofficer of an issuing agency of a participating jurisdiction stated in\nthe authority to:\n\n(a) produce evidence of the assumed identity in accordance with\nthe authority; and\n\n(b) give evidence of the assumed identity to the following:\n\n(i) the authorised person named in the authority;\n\n(ii) an officer of the law enforcement agency or the\nintelligence agency who is named in the request.\nNote:\nSection 15KW modifies the effect of this provision if control of the\nauthority is transferred.\n\n(2A) For the purposes of subsection (2), the person who may make the\nrequest is:\n\n(a) the chief officer of a law enforcement agency who granted\nthe authority; or\n\n(b) the chief officer of an intelligence agency (other than the\nOffice of National Intelligence or the Australian Signals\nDirectorate) who granted the authority; or\n\n(c) if the chief officer of the Office of National Intelligence\ngranted the authority—the chief officer of the Australian\nSecurity Intelligence Organisation or the Australian Secret\nIntelligence Service; or\n\n(d) if the chief officer of the Australian Signals Directorate\ngranted the authority—the chief officer of the Australian\nSecurity Intelligence Organisation or the Australian Secret\nIntelligence Service.\n\n\nAssumed Identities  Part IAC\nMutual Recognition under Corresponding Laws  Division 5\n\nSection 15KY\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nNote:\nThe chief officer may delegate functions under this section—see\nsection 15LH.\n\n(3) The request must state that it is a request under this section.\n\n(4) A request must not be made under this section for an entry in a\nregister of births, deaths or marriages.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15kx-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15kx-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15kx-ss-2a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15kx-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15kx-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "53975c8037963ac3c56ebc4845a2b03053492abb166b2c7391d34bf86798588a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15kx",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15KX Requests to a participating jurisdiction for evidence of",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 130,
      "values:originalText": "assumed identity\n\n(1) This section applies if an authority granted under section 15KB\nauthorises a request under this section.\n\n(2) The person specified in subsection (2A) may request the chief\nofficer of an issuing agency of a participating jurisdiction stated in\nthe authority to:\n\n(a) produce evidence of the assumed identity in accordance with\nthe authority; and\n\n(b) give evidence of the assumed identity to the following:\n\n(i) the authorised person named in the authority;\n\n(ii) an officer of the law enforcement agency or the\nintelligence agency who is named in the request.\nNote:\nSection 15KW modifies the effect of this provision if control of the\nauthority is transferred.\n\n(2A) For the purposes of subsection (2), the person who may make the\nrequest is:\n\n(a) the chief officer of a law enforcement agency who granted\nthe authority; or\n\n(b) the chief officer of an intelligence agency (other than the\nOffice of National Intelligence or the Australian Signals\nDirectorate) who granted the authority; or\n\n(c) if the chief officer of the Office of National Intelligence\ngranted the authority—the chief officer of the Australian\nSecurity Intelligence Organisation or the Australian Secret\nIntelligence Service; or\n\n(d) if the chief officer of the Australian Signals Directorate\ngranted the authority—the chief officer of the Australian\nSecurity Intelligence Organisation or the Australian Secret\nIntelligence Service.\n\n\nAssumed Identities  Part IAC\nMutual Recognition under Corresponding Laws  Division 5\n\nSection 15KY\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nNote:\nThe chief officer may delegate functions under this section—see\nsection 15LH.\n\n(3) The request must state that it is a request under this section.\n\n(4) A request must not be made under this section for an entry in a\nregister of births, deaths or marriages."
    },
