    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15l",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15L Indemnity for issuing agencies and officers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15l"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.132",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if the chief officer of either a law enforcement\nagency or an intelligence agency makes a request to the chief\nofficer of an issuing agency of a participating jurisdiction under\nsection 15KX.\n\n(2) The agency that makes the request must indemnify the issuing\nagency and any officer of the issuing agency, for any liability\nincurred by the issuing agency or the officer of the issuing agency\n(including reasonable costs) if:\n\n(a) the liability is incurred because of something done in the\ncourse of duty by the issuing agency or the officer of the\nissuing agency to comply with the request; and\n\n(b) any requirements prescribed under the regulations have been\nmet.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies if the chief officer of either a law enforcement\nagency or an intelligence agency makes a request to the chief\nofficer of an issuing agency of a participating jurisdiction under\nsection 15KX.\n\n(2) The agency that makes the request must indemnify the issuing\nagency and any officer of the issuing agency, for any liability\nincurred by the issuing agency or the officer of the issuing agency\n(including reasonable costs) if:\n\n(a) the liability is incurred because of something done in the\ncourse of duty by the issuing agency or the officer of the\nissuing agency to comply with the request; and\n\n(b) any requirements prescribed under the regulations have been\nmet.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15l-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15l-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9033779664903df7bc43c15a623b88abe766fd095353103b037be5d4e600c430"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15l",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15L Indemnity for issuing agencies and officers",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 132,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if the chief officer of either a law enforcement\nagency or an intelligence agency makes a request to the chief\nofficer of an issuing agency of a participating jurisdiction under\nsection 15KX.\n\n(2) The agency that makes the request must indemnify the issuing\nagency and any officer of the issuing agency, for any liability\nincurred by the issuing agency or the officer of the issuing agency\n(including reasonable costs) if:\n\n(a) the liability is incurred because of something done in the\ncourse of duty by the issuing agency or the officer of the\nissuing agency to comply with the request; and\n\n(b) any requirements prescribed under the regulations have been\nmet."
    },
    {
