      "skos:note": "Agency must indemnify issuing agency and officers for liability incurred while complying with request."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15l-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15L(2) Indemnity for issuing agencies and officers",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 132,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The agency that makes the request must indemnify the issuing\nagency and any officer of the issuing agency, for any liability\nincurred by the issuing agency or the officer of the issuing agency\n(including reasonable costs) if:\n\n(a) the liability is incurred because of something done in the\ncourse of duty by the issuing agency or the officer of the\nissuing agency to comply with the request; and\n\n(b) any requirements prescribed under the regulations have been\nmet."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15l-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15l-ss-2"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15l-ss-2-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Agency has an obligation to indemnify issuing agency and officers.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15la",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15LA Application of this Part to authorities under corresponding",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15la"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.132",
      "values:originalText": "laws\n\n(1) The following provisions apply to anything done in relation to a\ncorresponding authority as if it were an authority granted under\nsection 15KB:\n\n(a) section 15KP (assumed identity may be acquired and used);\n\n(b) section 15KT (particular qualifications);\n\n\nAssumed Identities  Part IAC\nMutual Recognition under Corresponding Laws  Division 5\n\nSection 15LA\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(c) section 15KU (effect of being unaware of variation or\ncancellation of authority);\n\n(d) section 15LB (misuse of assumed identity);\n\n(e) section 15LC (disclosing information about assumed\nidentity).\n\n(2) Sections 15KN, 15KQ and 15KR apply to anything done in\nrelation to a corresponding authority as if:\n\n(a) the corresponding authority were an authority granted under\nsection 15KB; and\n\n(b) references in those sections to an offence under a law of a\nState or Territory were omitted.\n\n\nPart IAC  Assumed Identities",
      "skos:definition": "laws\n\n(1) The following provisions apply to anything done in relation to a\ncorresponding authority as if it were an authority granted under\nsection 15KB:\n\n(a) section 15KP (assumed identity may be acquired and used);\n\n(b) section 15KT (particular qualifications);\n\n\nAssumed Identities  Part IAC\nMutual Recognition under Corresponding Laws  Division 5\n\nSection 15LA\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(c) section 15KU (effect of being unaware of variation or\ncancellation of authority);\n\n(d) section 15LB (misuse of assumed identity);\n\n(e) section 15LC (disclosing information about assumed\nidentity).\n\n(2) Sections 15KN, 15KQ and 15KR apply to anything done in\nrelation to a corresponding authority as if:\n\n(a) the corresponding authority were an authority granted under\nsection 15KB; and\n\n(b) references in those sections to an offence under a law of a\nState or Territory were omitted.\n\n\nPart IAC  Assumed Identities",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15la-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15la-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8954b4ce200e1b10594592fbed1a8ba405c3e70d3a3ae2909815f7b5cdaf992c"
    },
