    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ld",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15LD Reports about authorities for assumed identities etc.—law",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15ld"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.136",
      "values:originalText": "enforcement agencies\n\n(1) As soon as practicable after the end of each financial year, the\nchief officer of a law enforcement agency must submit a report to\nthe Minister administering the National Anti-Corruption\nCommission Act 2022 (the NACC Minister) that includes the\nfollowing information for the year:\n\n(a) the number of authorities granted during the year;\n\n(b) a general description of the activities undertaken by\nauthorised civilians and authorised law enforcement officers\nwhen using assumed identities under this Part during the\nyear;\n\n(c) the number of applications for authorities that were refused\nduring the year;\n\n\nAssumed Identities  Part IAC\nCompliance and Monitoring  Division 6\n\nSection 15LE\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(d) the number of authorities of which control was transferred by\nthe chief officer under section 15KV during the year;\n\n(e) the number of authorities of which control was transferred to\nthe chief officer under section 15KV during the year;\n\n(f) a statement whether or not any fraud or other unlawful\nactivity was identified by an audit under section 15LG during\nthe year;\n\n(g) any other information relating to authorities and assumed\nidentities and the administration of this Part that the NACC\nMinister considers appropriate.\n\n(2) The chief officer must advise the NACC Minister of any\ninformation in the report that, in the chief officer’s opinion, should\nbe excluded from the report before the report is laid before the\nParliament because the information, if made public, could\nreasonably be expected to:\n\n(a) endanger a person’s safety; or\n\n(b) prejudice an investigation or prosecution; or\n\n(c) compromise any law enforcement agency’s operational\nactivities or methodologies.\n\n(3) The NACC Minister must exclude information from the report if\nsatisfied on the advice of the chief officer of any of the grounds set\nout in subsection (2) and must cause a copy of the report to be laid\nbefore each House of the Parliament within 15 sitting days of that\nHouse after the day on which the NACC Minister receives the\nreport.",
      "skos:definition": "enforcement agencies\n\n(1) As soon as practicable after the end of each financial year, the\nchief officer of a law enforcement agency must submit a report to\nthe Minister administering the National Anti-Corruption\nCommission Act 2022 (the NACC Minister) that includes the\nfollowing information for the year:\n\n(a) the number of authorities granted during the year;\n\n(b) a general description of the activities undertaken by\nauthorised civilians and authorised law enforcement officers\nwhen using assumed identities under this Part during the\nyear;\n\n(c) the number of applications for authorities that were refused\nduring the year;\n\n\nAssumed Identities  Part IAC\nCompliance and Monitoring  Division 6\n\nSection 15LE\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(d) the number of authorities of which control was transferred by\nthe chief officer under section 15KV during the year;\n\n(e) the number of authorities of which control was transferred to\nthe chief officer under section 15KV during the year;\n\n(f) a statement whether or not any fraud or other unlawful\nactivity was identified by an audit under section 15LG during\nthe year;\n\n(g) any other information relating to authorities and assumed\nidentities and the administration of this Part that the NACC\nMinister considers appropriate.\n\n(2) The chief officer must advise the NACC Minister of any\ninformation in the report that, in the chief officer’s opinion, should\nbe excluded from the report before the report is laid before the\nParliament because the information, if made public, could\nreasonably be expected to:\n\n(a) endanger a person’s safety; or\n\n(b) prejudice an investigation or prosecution; or\n\n(c) compromise any law enforcement agency’s operational\nactivities or methodologies.\n\n(3) The NACC Minister must exclude information from the report if\nsatisfied on the advice of the chief officer of any of the grounds set\nout in subsection (2) and must cause a copy of the report to be laid\nbefore each House of the Parliament within 15 sitt",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ld-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ld-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ld-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0cced6ed77be747d3b1f163daa10d980c5120a5fe65e4b95fc70fd947456f90d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15ld",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15LD Reports about authorities for assumed identities etc.—law",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 136,
      "values:originalText": "enforcement agencies\n\n(1) As soon as practicable after the end of each financial year, the\nchief officer of a law enforcement agency must submit a report to\nthe Minister administering the National Anti-Corruption\nCommission Act 2022 (the NACC Minister) that includes the\nfollowing information for the year:\n\n(a) the number of authorities granted during the year;\n\n(b) a general description of the activities undertaken by\nauthorised civilians and authorised law enforcement officers\nwhen using assumed identities under this Part during the\nyear;\n\n(c) the number of applications for authorities that were refused\nduring the year;\n\n\nAssumed Identities  Part IAC\nCompliance and Monitoring  Division 6\n\nSection 15LE\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(d) the number of authorities of which control was transferred by\nthe chief officer under section 15KV during the year;\n\n(e) the number of authorities of which control was transferred to\nthe chief officer under section 15KV during the year;\n\n(f) a statement whether or not any fraud or other unlawful\nactivity was identified by an audit under section 15LG during\nthe year;\n\n(g) any other information relating to authorities and assumed\nidentities and the administration of this Part that the NACC\nMinister considers appropriate.\n\n(2) The chief officer must advise the NACC Minister of any\ninformation in the report that, in the chief officer’s opinion, should\nbe excluded from the report before the report is laid before the\nParliament because the information, if made public, could\nreasonably be expected to:\n\n(a) endanger a person’s safety; or\n\n(b) prejudice an investigation or prosecution; or\n\n(c) compromise any law enforcement agency’s operational\nactivities or methodologies.\n\n(3) The NACC Minister must exclude information from the report if\nsatisfied on the advice of the chief officer of any of the grounds set\nout in subsection (2) and must cause a copy of the report to be laid\nbefore each House of the Parliament within 15 sitting days of that\nHouse after the day on which the NACC Minister receives the\nreport."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ld-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15LD(1) Reports about authorities for assumed identities etc.—law",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15ld-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.136",
      "values:originalText": "(1) As soon as practicable after the end of each financial year, the\nchief officer of a law enforcement agency must submit a report to\nthe Minister administering the National Anti-Corruption\nCommission Act 2022 (the NACC Minister) that includes the\nfollowing information for the year:\n\n(a) the number of authorities granted during the year;\n\n(b) a general description of the activities undertaken by\nauthorised civilians and authorised law enforcement officers\nwhen using assumed identities under this Part during the\nyear;\n\n(c) the number of applications for authorities that were refused\nduring the year;\n\n\nAssumed Identities  Part IAC\nCompliance and Monitoring  Division 6\n\nSection 15LE\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(d) the number of authorities of which control was transferred by\nthe chief officer under section 15KV during the year;\n\n(e) the number of authorities of which control was transferred to\nthe chief officer under section 15KV during the year;\n\n(f) a statement whether or not any fraud or other unlawful\nactivity was identified by an audit under section 15LG during\nthe year;\n\n(g) any other information relating to authorities and assumed\nidentities and the administration of this Part that the NACC\nMinister considers appropriate.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) As soon as practicable after the end of each financial year, the\nchief officer of a law enforcement agency must submit a report to\nthe Minister administering the National Anti-Corruption\nCommission Act 2022 (the NACC Minister) that includes the\nfollowing information for the year:\n\n(a) the number of authorities granted during the year;\n\n(b) a general description of the activities undertaken by\nauthorised civilians and authorised law enforcement officers\nwhen using assumed identities under this Part during the\nyear;\n\n(c) the number of applications for authorities that were refused\nduring the year;\n\n\nAssumed Identities  Part IAC\nCompliance and Monitoring  Division 6\n\nSection 15LE\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(d) the number of authorities of which control was transferred by\nthe chief officer under section 15KV during the year;\n\n(e) the number of authorities of which control was transferred to\nthe chief officer under section 15KV during the year;\n\n(f) a statement whether or not any fraud or other unlawful\nactivity was identified by an audit under section 15LG during\nthe year;\n\n(g) any other information relating to authorities and assumed\nidentities and the administration of this Part that the NACC\nMinister considers appropriate.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ld"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ld-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ld-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ld-ss-1-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "51976b90748c8a43b72ed2181c43f6ddbea1ff7c9495089aac96a6e874cf9874",
      "skos:note": "Chief officer must submit report to NACC Minister with specific information about authorities and assumed identities.",
      "dc:description": "true"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15ld-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15LD(1) Reports about authorities for assumed identities etc.—law",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 136,
      "values:originalText": "(1) As soon as practicable after the end of each financial year, the\nchief officer of a law enforcement agency must submit a report to\nthe Minister administering the National Anti-Corruption\nCommission Act 2022 (the NACC Minister) that includes the\nfollowing information for the year:\n\n(a) the number of authorities granted during the year;\n\n(b) a general description of the activities undertaken by\nauthorised civilians and authorised law enforcement officers\nwhen using assumed identities under this Part during the\nyear;\n\n(c) the number of applications for authorities that were refused\nduring the year;\n\n\nAssumed Identities  Part IAC\nCompliance and Monitoring  Division 6\n\nSection 15LE\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(d) the number of authorities of which control was transferred by\nthe chief officer under section 15KV during the year;\n\n(e) the number of authorities of which control was transferred to\nthe chief officer under section 15KV during the year;\n\n(f) a statement whether or not any fraud or other unlawful\nactivity was identified by an audit under section 15LG during\nthe year;\n\n(g) any other information relating to authorities and assumed\nidentities and the administration of this Part that the NACC\nMinister considers appropriate."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ld-ss-1-norm",
