      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ld-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15LD(2) Reports about authorities for assumed identities etc.—law",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15ld-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.136",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The chief officer must advise the NACC Minister of any\ninformation in the report that, in the chief officer’s opinion, should\nbe excluded from the report before the report is laid before the\nParliament because the information, if made public, could\nreasonably be expected to:\n\n(a) endanger a person’s safety; or\n\n(b) prejudice an investigation or prosecution; or\n\n(c) compromise any law enforcement agency’s operational\nactivities or methodologies.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The chief officer must advise the NACC Minister of any\ninformation in the report that, in the chief officer’s opinion, should\nbe excluded from the report before the report is laid before the\nParliament because the information, if made public, could\nreasonably be expected to:\n\n(a) endanger a person’s safety; or\n\n(b) prejudice an investigation or prosecution; or\n\n(c) compromise any law enforcement agency’s operational\nactivities or methodologies.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ld"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ld-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ld-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ld-ss-2-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ld-ss-2-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ld-ss-2-logic-diffusion-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ld-ss-2-logic-cogai-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f6f391e094e33ff0ba286cd9241a73294d42c50cc86a0049f8ccb94479eb3fab",
      "skos:note": "Exclusion of information from reports to protect safety and investigations."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15ld-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15LD(2) Reports about authorities for assumed identities etc.—law",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 136,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The chief officer must advise the NACC Minister of any\ninformation in the report that, in the chief officer’s opinion, should\nbe excluded from the report before the report is laid before the\nParliament because the information, if made public, could\nreasonably be expected to:\n\n(a) endanger a person’s safety; or\n\n(b) prejudice an investigation or prosecution; or\n\n(c) compromise any law enforcement agency’s operational\nactivities or methodologies."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ld-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ld-ss-2"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
