      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.141",
      "values:originalText": "(2) A chief officer may delegate to a senior officer of the law\nenforcement agency or the intelligence agency (as the case may be)\nany of the chief officer’s functions under this Part relating to the\ngranting, variation, cancellation and transfer of control of\nauthorities (including, but not limited to conducting reviews under\nsection 15KF, making applications under section 15KG, giving\ndirections under section 15KL and making requests under\nsection 15KI or 15KX).",
      "skos:definition": "(2) A chief officer may delegate to a senior officer of the law\nenforcement agency or the intelligence agency (as the case may be)\nany of the chief officer’s functions under this Part relating to the\ngranting, variation, cancellation and transfer of control of\nauthorities (including, but not limited to conducting reviews under\nsection 15KF, making applications under section 15KG, giving\ndirections under section 15KL and making requests under\nsection 15KI or 15KX).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15lh"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15lh-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15lh-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15lh-ss-2-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cb603657ac0fc7a572ec1c0db320e490bbaea4fe939bac53d80b41c17115a900",
      "skos:note": "A chief officer may delegate certain functions to a senior officer."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15lh-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15LH(2) Delegation of chief officer’s functions",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 141,
      "values:originalText": "(2) A chief officer may delegate to a senior officer of the law\nenforcement agency or the intelligence agency (as the case may be)\nany of the chief officer’s functions under this Part relating to the\ngranting, variation, cancellation and transfer of control of\nauthorities (including, but not limited to conducting reviews under\nsection 15KF, making applications under section 15KG, giving\ndirections under section 15KL and making requests under\nsection 15KI or 15KX)."
    },
    {
