      "cml:conclusionText": "Senior officer assumes delegated function during chief officer's term"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15lh-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15LH(3) Delegation of chief officer’s functions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15lh-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.141",
      "values:originalText": "(3) In this section:\nsenior officer means:\n\n(a) in relation to the Australian Federal Police:\n\n(i) any senior executive AFP employee of the Australian\nFederal Police within the meaning of section 25 of the\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979; or\n\n(ii) any Deputy Commissioner of Police within the meaning\nof section 6 of the Australian Federal Police Act 1979;\nor\n\n(iii) a person occupying a position in the Australian Federal\nPolice that is equivalent to or higher than the positions\nmentioned in subparagraphs (i) and (ii); and\n\n(b) in relation to the Immigration and Border Protection\nDepartment—any SES employee in that Department; and\n\n(c) in relation to the ACC—any SES employee who is a member\nof the staff of the ACC within the meaning of section 47 of\nthe Australian Crime Commission Act 2002, or a person\noccupying an equivalent or higher position in the ACC; and\n\n(d) in relation to the National Anti-Corruption Commission:\n\n\nPart IAC  Assumed Identities",
      "skos:definition": "(3) In this section:\nsenior officer means:\n\n(a) in relation to the Australian Federal Police:\n\n(i) any senior executive AFP employee of the Australian\nFederal Police within the meaning of section 25 of the\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979; or\n\n(ii) any Deputy Commissioner of Police within the meaning\nof section 6 of the Australian Federal Police Act 1979;\nor\n\n(iii) a person occupying a position in the Australian Federal\nPolice that is equivalent to or higher than the positions\nmentioned in subparagraphs (i) and (ii); and\n\n(b) in relation to the Immigration and Border Protection\nDepartment—any SES employee in that Department; and\n\n(c) in relation to the ACC—any SES employee who is a member\nof the staff of the ACC within the meaning of section 47 of\nthe Australian Crime Commission Act 2002, or a person\noccupying an equivalent or higher position in the ACC; and\n\n(d) in relation to the National Anti-Corruption Commission:\n\n\nPart IAC  Assumed Identities",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15lh"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15lh-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15lh-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15lh-ss-3-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f4aec95692a293dc32e2f765c7553c5aaa475ffb8d15dfbeb997bf26491a8454",
      "skos:note": "Defines senior officer roles in various agencies."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15lh-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15LH(3) Delegation of chief officer’s functions",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 141,
      "values:originalText": "(3) In this section:\nsenior officer means:\n\n(a) in relation to the Australian Federal Police:\n\n(i) any senior executive AFP employee of the Australian\nFederal Police within the meaning of section 25 of the\nAustralian Federal Police Act 1979; or\n\n(ii) any Deputy Commissioner of Police within the meaning\nof section 6 of the Australian Federal Police Act 1979;\nor\n\n(iii) a person occupying a position in the Australian Federal\nPolice that is equivalent to or higher than the positions\nmentioned in subparagraphs (i) and (ii); and\n\n(b) in relation to the Immigration and Border Protection\nDepartment—any SES employee in that Department; and\n\n(c) in relation to the ACC—any SES employee who is a member\nof the staff of the ACC within the meaning of section 47 of\nthe Australian Crime Commission Act 2002, or a person\noccupying an equivalent or higher position in the ACC; and\n\n(d) in relation to the National Anti-Corruption Commission:\n\n\nPart IAC  Assumed Identities"
    },
