    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15m",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15M Definitions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15m"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.143",
      "values:originalText": "(1) In this Part:\nassumed name of an operative has the meaning given by\nparagraph 15MG(1)(a)(i).\nchief officer of a law enforcement agency means the following:\n\n(a) in relation to the Australian Federal Police—the\nCommissioner of the Australian Federal Police;\n\n(b) in relation to the Immigration and Border Protection\nDepartment—Secretary of that Department;\n\n(c) in relation to the ACC—the Chief Executive Officer of the\nACC;\n\n(d) in relation to the National Anti-Corruption Commission—the\nNational Anti-Corruption Commissioner;\n\n(e) in relation to the Australian Taxation Office—the\nCommissioner of Taxation;\n\n(f) in relation to a Commonwealth agency specified in the\nregulations for the purposes of the definition of law\nenforcement agency—the officer specified in the regulations\nas the chief officer of that agency.\nconduct includes any act or omission.\ncorresponding witness identity protection certificate means a\ncertificate given under a provision of a corresponding witness\nidentity protection law that corresponds to section 15ME.\ncorresponding witness identity protection law means:\n\n(a) a law of a State or Territory; or\n\n\nPart IACA  Witness identity protection for operatives",
      "skos:definition": "(1) In this Part:\nassumed name of an operative has the meaning given by\nparagraph 15MG(1)(a)(i).\nchief officer of a law enforcement agency means the following:\n\n(a) in relation to the Australian Federal Police—the\nCommissioner of the Australian Federal Police;\n\n(b) in relation to the Immigration and Border Protection\nDepartment—Secretary of that Department;\n\n(c) in relation to the ACC—the Chief Executive Officer of the\nACC;\n\n(d) in relation to the National Anti-Corruption Commission—the\nNational Anti-Corruption Commissioner;\n\n(e) in relation to the Australian Taxation Office—the\nCommissioner of Taxation;\n\n(f) in relation to a Commonwealth agency specified in the\nregulations for the purposes of the definition of law\nenforcement agency—the officer specified in the regulations\nas the chief officer of that agency.\nconduct includes any act or omission.\ncorresponding witness identity protection certificate means a\ncertificate given under a provision of a corresponding witness\nidentity protection law that corresponds to section 15ME.\ncorresponding witness identity protection law means:\n\n(a) a law of a State or Territory; or\n\n\nPart IACA  Witness identity protection for operatives",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15m-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15m-logic-descriptionlogic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "59bb7585b4e22e40c9b01475c7d9f271eca4e95a42c168381b44e9acd2a5a515",
      "skos:note": "Defines terms for Part IACA"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15m",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15M Definitions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 143,
      "values:originalText": "(1) In this Part:\nassumed name of an operative has the meaning given by\nparagraph 15MG(1)(a)(i).\nchief officer of a law enforcement agency means the following:\n\n(a) in relation to the Australian Federal Police—the\nCommissioner of the Australian Federal Police;\n\n(b) in relation to the Immigration and Border Protection\nDepartment—Secretary of that Department;\n\n(c) in relation to the ACC—the Chief Executive Officer of the\nACC;\n\n(d) in relation to the National Anti-Corruption Commission—the\nNational Anti-Corruption Commissioner;\n\n(e) in relation to the Australian Taxation Office—the\nCommissioner of Taxation;\n\n(f) in relation to a Commonwealth agency specified in the\nregulations for the purposes of the definition of law\nenforcement agency—the officer specified in the regulations\nas the chief officer of that agency.\nconduct includes any act or omission.\ncorresponding witness identity protection certificate means a\ncertificate given under a provision of a corresponding witness\nidentity protection law that corresponds to section 15ME.\ncorresponding witness identity protection law means:\n\n(a) a law of a State or Territory; or\n\n\nPart IACA  Witness identity protection for operatives"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15m-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
