    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15mf",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15MF Statutory declaration by operative",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15mf"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.149",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Before a witness identity protection certificate is given for an\noperative, the operative must make a statutory declaration of the\nfollowing matters:\n\n(a) whether the operative has been convicted or found guilty of\nan offence and, if so, particulars of each offence;\n\n(b) whether any charges against the operative for an offence are\npending or outstanding and, if so, particulars of each charge;\n\n(c) if the operative is or was a law enforcement officer:\n\n(i) whether the operative has been found guilty of\nprofessional misconduct and, if so, particulars of each\nfinding; and\n\n\nPart IACA  Witness identity protection for operatives",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Before a witness identity protection certificate is given for an\noperative, the operative must make a statutory declaration of the\nfollowing matters:\n\n(a) whether the operative has been convicted or found guilty of\nan offence and, if so, particulars of each offence;\n\n(b) whether any charges against the operative for an offence are\npending or outstanding and, if so, particulars of each charge;\n\n(c) if the operative is or was a law enforcement officer:\n\n(i) whether the operative has been found guilty of\nprofessional misconduct and, if so, particulars of each\nfinding; and\n\n\nPart IACA  Witness identity protection for operatives",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15mf-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15mf-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0a9af070fcf481a6c2b25f06a9c005adc40eaf217cb60e1428ba8bc2b95181dc",
      "skos:note": "Statutory declaration by operative regarding convictions and charges.",
      "dc:description": "a statutory declaration of the following matters"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15mf",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15MF Statutory declaration by operative",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 149,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Before a witness identity protection certificate is given for an\noperative, the operative must make a statutory declaration of the\nfollowing matters:\n\n(a) whether the operative has been convicted or found guilty of\nan offence and, if so, particulars of each offence;\n\n(b) whether any charges against the operative for an offence are\npending or outstanding and, if so, particulars of each charge;\n\n(c) if the operative is or was a law enforcement officer:\n\n(i) whether the operative has been found guilty of\nprofessional misconduct and, if so, particulars of each\nfinding; and\n\n\nPart IACA  Witness identity protection for operatives"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15mf-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15mf"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15mf-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Statutory declaration is required.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15mg",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15MG Form of witness identity protection certificate",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15mg"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.150",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A witness identity protection certificate for an operative in relation\nto a proceeding must state the following:\n\n(a) if the operative:\n\n(i) is known to a party to the proceeding or a party’s lawyer\nby a name other than the operative’s real name—that\nname (the assumed name); or\n\n(ii) is not known to any party to the proceeding or any\nparty’s lawyer by a name—the operative’s court name\nfor the proceeding;\n\n\nWitness identity protection for operatives  Part IACA\nWitness Identity Protection Certificates for Operatives  Division 2\n\nSection 15MH\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) the period the operative was involved in the investigation to\nwhich the proceeding relates;\n\n(c) the name of the agency;\n\n(d) the date of the certificate;\n\n(e) the grounds for giving the certificate;\n\n(f) whether the operative has been convicted or found guilty of\nan offence and, if so, particulars of each offence;\n\n(g) whether any charges against the operative for an offence are\npending or outstanding and, if so, particulars of each charge;\n\n(h) if the operative is or was a law enforcement officer:\n\n(i) whether the operative has been found guilty of\nprofessional misconduct and, if so, particulars of each\nfinding; and\n\n(ii) whether any allegations of professional misconduct\nagainst the operative are outstanding and, if so,\nparticulars of each allegation;\n\n(i) whether, to the knowledge of the person giving the\ncertificate, a court has made any adverse comment about the\noperative’s credibility and, if so, particulars of the comment;\n\n(j) whether, to the knowledge of the person giving the\ncertificate, the operative has made a false representation\nwhen the truth was required and, if so, particulars of the\nrepresentation;\n\n(k) if there is anything else known to the person giving the\ncertificate that may be relevant to the operative’s\ncredibility—particulars of the thing.\n\n(2) A witness identity protection certificate for an operative must not\ncontain information that may allow the operative’s identity, or\nwhere the operative lives, to be revealed.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A witness identity protection certificate for an operative in relation\nto a proceeding must state the following:\n\n(a) if the operative:\n\n(i) is known to a party to the proceeding or a party’s lawyer\nby a name other than the operative’s real name—that\nname (the assumed name); or\n\n(ii) is not known to any party to the proceeding or any\nparty’s lawyer by a name—the operative’s court name\nfor the proceeding;\n\n\nWitness identity protection for operatives  Part IACA\nWitness Identity Protection Certificates for Operatives  Division 2\n\nSection 15MH\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) the period the operative was involved in the investigation to\nwhich the proceeding relates;\n\n(c) the name of the agency;\n\n(d) the date of the certificate;\n\n(e) the grounds for giving the certificate;\n\n(f) whether the operative has been convicted or found guilty of\nan offence and, if so, particulars of each offence;\n\n(g) whether any charges against the operative for an offence are\npending or outstanding and, if so, particulars of each charge;\n\n(h) if the operative is or was a law enforcement officer:\n\n(i) whether the operative has been found guilty of\nprofessional misconduct and, if so, particulars of each\nfinding; and\n\n(ii) whether any allegations of professional misconduct\nagainst the operative are outstanding and, if so,\nparticulars of each allegation;\n\n(i) whether, to the knowledge of the person giving the\ncertificate, a court has made any adverse comment about the\noperative’s credibility and, if so, particulars of the comment;\n\n(j) whether, to the knowledge of the person giving the\ncertificate, the operative has made a false representation\nwhen the truth was required and, if so, particulars of the\nrepresentation;\n\n(k) if there is anything else known to the person giving the\ncertificate that may be relevant to the operative’s\ncredibility—particulars of the thing.\n\n(2) A witness identity protection certificate for an operative must not\ncontain information that may allow the",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15mg-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15mg-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "421f8b79f14f7c3ca59c676d186a881fc45b1d6641f3d215b943df6c553db62e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15mg",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15MG Form of witness identity protection certificate",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 150,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A witness identity protection certificate for an operative in relation\nto a proceeding must state the following:\n\n(a) if the operative:\n\n(i) is known to a party to the proceeding or a party’s lawyer\nby a name other than the operative’s real name—that\nname (the assumed name); or\n\n(ii) is not known to any party to the proceeding or any\nparty’s lawyer by a name—the operative’s court name\nfor the proceeding;\n\n\nWitness identity protection for operatives  Part IACA\nWitness Identity Protection Certificates for Operatives  Division 2\n\nSection 15MH\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) the period the operative was involved in the investigation to\nwhich the proceeding relates;\n\n(c) the name of the agency;\n\n(d) the date of the certificate;\n\n(e) the grounds for giving the certificate;\n\n(f) whether the operative has been convicted or found guilty of\nan offence and, if so, particulars of each offence;\n\n(g) whether any charges against the operative for an offence are\npending or outstanding and, if so, particulars of each charge;\n\n(h) if the operative is or was a law enforcement officer:\n\n(i) whether the operative has been found guilty of\nprofessional misconduct and, if so, particulars of each\nfinding; and\n\n(ii) whether any allegations of professional misconduct\nagainst the operative are outstanding and, if so,\nparticulars of each allegation;\n\n(i) whether, to the knowledge of the person giving the\ncertificate, a court has made any adverse comment about the\noperative’s credibility and, if so, particulars of the comment;\n\n(j) whether, to the knowledge of the person giving the\ncertificate, the operative has made a false representation\nwhen the truth was required and, if so, particulars of the\nrepresentation;\n\n(k) if there is anything else known to the person giving the\ncertificate that may be relevant to the operative’s\ncredibility—particulars of the thing.\n\n(2) A witness identity protection certificate for an operative must not\ncontain information that may allow the operative’s identity, or\nwhere the operative lives, to be revealed."
    },
