        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(7) Unless the court considers that the interests of justice require otherwise...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The information must be provided."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15mm-ss-7-logic-cogai-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:CogAI"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Recognize",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Recognition of operative's identity disclosure",
      "cml:executionSurface": "sparql_library::parsers::chk_parser",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(7) Unless the court considers that the interests of justice require otherwise...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The operative's identity must be disclosed."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15mn",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15MN Application for leave—joinder as respondent",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15mn"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.156",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a witness identity protection certificate for an operative in\nrelation to a proceeding is filed in a court; and\n\n(b) a person applies:\n\n(i) for leave under section 15MI or 15MM; or\n\n(ii) for an order under section 15MK or 15MM.\n\n(2) The court in which the application is pending may allow a person\nto join the application as a respondent if:\n\n(a) the person is:\n\n\nWitness identity protection for operatives  Part IACA\nWitness Identity Protection Certificates for Operatives  Division 2\n\nSection 15MO\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(i) the operative in relation to whom the witness identity\nprotection certificate is given; or\n\n(ii) the chief officer of the agency who gave the witness\nidentity protection certificate; and\n\n(b) the person applies to be joined to the application as a\nrespondent; and\n\n(c) the person has sufficient interest in the subject matter of the\napplication.\n\n(3) If a court allows a person to join the application as a respondent\nunder subsection (2), the court must allow the person, or the\nperson’s legal representative, to appear and be heard.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a witness identity protection certificate for an operative in\nrelation to a proceeding is filed in a court; and\n\n(b) a person applies:\n\n(i) for leave under section 15MI or 15MM; or\n\n(ii) for an order under section 15MK or 15MM.\n\n(2) The court in which the application is pending may allow a person\nto join the application as a respondent if:\n\n(a) the person is:\n\n\nWitness identity protection for operatives  Part IACA\nWitness Identity Protection Certificates for Operatives  Division 2\n\nSection 15MO\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(i) the operative in relation to whom the witness identity\nprotection certificate is given; or\n\n(ii) the chief officer of the agency who gave the witness\nidentity protection certificate; and\n\n(b) the person applies to be joined to the application as a\nrespondent; and\n\n(c) the person has sufficient interest in the subject matter of the\napplication.\n\n(3) If a court allows a person to join the application as a respondent\nunder subsection (2), the court must allow the person, or the\nperson’s legal representative, to appear and be heard.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15mn-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15mn-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15mn-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2b206030fec97b4a27e8284260c2bfa9901a6a12d163ac56daa30784808ece3d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15mn",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15MN Application for leave—joinder as respondent",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 156,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) a witness identity protection certificate for an operative in\nrelation to a proceeding is filed in a court; and\n\n(b) a person applies:\n\n(i) for leave under section 15MI or 15MM; or\n\n(ii) for an order under section 15MK or 15MM.\n\n(2) The court in which the application is pending may allow a person\nto join the application as a respondent if:\n\n(a) the person is:\n\n\nWitness identity protection for operatives  Part IACA\nWitness Identity Protection Certificates for Operatives  Division 2\n\nSection 15MO\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(i) the operative in relation to whom the witness identity\nprotection certificate is given; or\n\n(ii) the chief officer of the agency who gave the witness\nidentity protection certificate; and\n\n(b) the person applies to be joined to the application as a\nrespondent; and\n\n(c) the person has sufficient interest in the subject matter of the\napplication.\n\n(3) If a court allows a person to join the application as a respondent\nunder subsection (2), the court must allow the person, or the\nperson’s legal representative, to appear and be heard."
    },
    {
