      "values:originalText": "corresponding laws\n\nThe following provisions apply, with any necessary changes, to a\ncorresponding witness identity protection certificate as if it were a\nwitness identity protection certificate given under section 15ME:\n\n(a) section 15MH (filing and notification);\n\n(b) section 15MI (leave for non-compliance);\n\n(c) section 15MJ (effect of witness identity protection\ncertificate);\n\n(d) section 15MK (orders to protect operative’s identity etc.);\n\n(e) section 15ML (disclosure of operative’s identity to presiding\nofficer);\n\n(f) section 15MM (disclosure of operative’s identity etc. despite\ncertificate);\n\n(g) section 15MN (application for leave—joinder as respondent);\n\n(h) section 15MO (directions to jury);\n\n(i) section 15MP (adjournment for appeal decision);\n\n(j) section 15MS (disclosure offences);\n\n(k) section 15MT (evidentiary certificates).\n\n\nWitness identity protection for operatives  Part IACA\nGeneral  Division 4\n\nSection 15MX\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "corresponding laws\n\nThe following provisions apply, with any necessary changes, to a\ncorresponding witness identity protection certificate as if it were a\nwitness identity protection certificate given under section 15ME:\n\n(a) section 15MH (filing and notification);\n\n(b) section 15MI (leave for non-compliance);\n\n(c) section 15MJ (effect of witness identity protection\ncertificate);\n\n(d) section 15MK (orders to protect operative’s identity etc.);\n\n(e) section 15ML (disclosure of operative’s identity to presiding\nofficer);\n\n(f) section 15MM (disclosure of operative’s identity etc. despite\ncertificate);\n\n(g) section 15MN (application for leave—joinder as respondent);\n\n(h) section 15MO (directions to jury);\n\n(i) section 15MP (adjournment for appeal decision);\n\n(j) section 15MS (disclosure offences);\n\n(k) section 15MT (evidentiary certificates).\n\n\nWitness identity protection for operatives  Part IACA\nGeneral  Division 4\n\nSection 15MX\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15mw-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9ef5b73dadc4797695e4b0432e1e3e817918ca6f3daf1c10ea3dfa1b9174a7c9",
      "skos:note": "Recognition of witness identity protection certificates under corresponding laws"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15mw",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15MW Recognition of witness identity protection certificates under",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 164,
      "values:originalText": "corresponding laws\n\nThe following provisions apply, with any necessary changes, to a\ncorresponding witness identity protection certificate as if it were a\nwitness identity protection certificate given under section 15ME:\n\n(a) section 15MH (filing and notification);\n\n(b) section 15MI (leave for non-compliance);\n\n(c) section 15MJ (effect of witness identity protection\ncertificate);\n\n(d) section 15MK (orders to protect operative’s identity etc.);\n\n(e) section 15ML (disclosure of operative’s identity to presiding\nofficer);\n\n(f) section 15MM (disclosure of operative’s identity etc. despite\ncertificate);\n\n(g) section 15MN (application for leave—joinder as respondent);\n\n(h) section 15MO (directions to jury);\n\n(i) section 15MP (adjournment for appeal decision);\n\n(j) section 15MS (disclosure offences);\n\n(k) section 15MT (evidentiary certificates).\n\n\nWitness identity protection for operatives  Part IACA\nGeneral  Division 4\n\nSection 15MX\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15mw-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
