    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yc-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15YC(2) Evidence of sexual experience—child proceedings",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15yc-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.174",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The court must not give leave unless the court is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the evidence is substantially relevant to facts in issue in the\nproceeding; and\n\n(b) the evidence has substantial probative value; and\n\n(c) either:\n\n(i) the evidence is of sexual activity that is alleged to form\npart of a connected set of circumstances in which the\nalleged offence was committed; or\n\n(ii) if the evidence is of sexual activities with a defendant in\nthe proceeding—the evidence relates to sexual activity\nthat occurred or was recent at the time of the\ncommission of the alleged offence.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The court must not give leave unless the court is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the evidence is substantially relevant to facts in issue in the\nproceeding; and\n\n(b) the evidence has substantial probative value; and\n\n(c) either:\n\n(i) the evidence is of sexual activity that is alleged to form\npart of a connected set of circumstances in which the\nalleged offence was committed; or\n\n(ii) if the evidence is of sexual activities with a defendant in\nthe proceeding—the evidence relates to sexual activity\nthat occurred or was recent at the time of the\ncommission of the alleged offence.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yc"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yc-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yc-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yc-ss-2-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yc-ss-2-logic-alleninterval-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yc-ss-2-logic-ltl-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yc-ss-2-logic-deontic-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "02ed95b88cfea077340422e5870c65caa832310f590ed79d86d92cf8c01a96a5",
      "skos:note": "Court must not give leave unless certain conditions are met. Court must not give leave to admit evidence unless it meets certain conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15yc-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15YC(2) Evidence of sexual experience—child proceedings",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 174,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The court must not give leave unless the court is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the evidence is substantially relevant to facts in issue in the\nproceeding; and\n\n(b) the evidence has substantial probative value; and\n\n(c) either:\n\n(i) the evidence is of sexual activity that is alleged to form\npart of a connected set of circumstances in which the\nalleged offence was committed; or\n\n(ii) if the evidence is of sexual activities with a defendant in\nthe proceeding—the evidence relates to sexual activity\nthat occurred or was recent at the time of the\ncommission of the alleged offence."
    },
