    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ye",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15YE Disallowing inappropriate or aggressive cross-examination",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15ye"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.182",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The court must disallow a question put to a person in\ncross-examination in a proceeding if:\n\n(a) the question is inappropriate or unnecessarily aggressive; and\n\n(b) the person is a person to whom subsection (3) applies.\n\n(2) In considering whether a question is inappropriate or unnecessarily\naggressive, the court is to have regard to the person’s personal\ncharacteristics, including his or her age, culture, mental capacity\nand gender.\n\n(3) This subsection applies to the following persons:\n\n(a) for a child proceeding—a child witness;\n\n(b) for a vulnerable adult proceeding—a vulnerable adult\ncomplainant;\n\n(c) for a special witness proceeding—a special witness.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The court must disallow a question put to a person in\ncross-examination in a proceeding if:\n\n(a) the question is inappropriate or unnecessarily aggressive; and\n\n(b) the person is a person to whom subsection (3) applies.\n\n(2) In considering whether a question is inappropriate or unnecessarily\naggressive, the court is to have regard to the person’s personal\ncharacteristics, including his or her age, culture, mental capacity\nand gender.\n\n(3) This subsection applies to the following persons:\n\n(a) for a child proceeding—a child witness;\n\n(b) for a vulnerable adult proceeding—a vulnerable adult\ncomplainant;\n\n(c) for a special witness proceeding—a special witness.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ye-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ye-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ye-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c318c3983a79c9e57d4b5e9ab740e82159818a3c01d09a17c8b7b43ecbba2cfd"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15ye",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15YE Disallowing inappropriate or aggressive cross-examination",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 182,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The court must disallow a question put to a person in\ncross-examination in a proceeding if:\n\n(a) the question is inappropriate or unnecessarily aggressive; and\n\n(b) the person is a person to whom subsection (3) applies.\n\n(2) In considering whether a question is inappropriate or unnecessarily\naggressive, the court is to have regard to the person’s personal\ncharacteristics, including his or her age, culture, mental capacity\nand gender.\n\n(3) This subsection applies to the following persons:\n\n(a) for a child proceeding—a child witness;\n\n(b) for a vulnerable adult proceeding—a vulnerable adult\ncomplainant;\n\n(c) for a special witness proceeding—a special witness."
    },
