    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yf",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15YF Unrepresented defendants—cross-examination of child",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15yf"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.182",
      "values:originalText": "complainants\n\n(1) A defendant in a child proceeding who is not represented by\ncounsel is not to cross-examine a child complainant.\nNote:\nA person is not to cross-examine certain persons at committal\nproceedings or proceedings of a similar kind—see section 15YHA.\n\n(2) A person appointed by the court is to ask the child any questions\nthat the defendant requests the person to ask the child.\n15YFA  Unrepresented defendants—cross-examination of vulnerable\nadult complainants\n\n(1) A defendant in a vulnerable adult proceeding who is not\nrepresented by counsel is not to cross-examine a vulnerable adult\ncomplainant.\n\n\nProtecting vulnerable persons  Part IAD\nCross-examination  Division 3\n\nSection 15YG\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nNote:\nA person is not to cross-examine certain persons at committal\nproceedings or proceedings of a similar kind—see section 15YHA.\n\n(2) A person appointed by the court is to ask the vulnerable adult\ncomplainant any questions that the defendant requests the person to\nask the complainant.",
      "skos:definition": "complainants\n\n(1) A defendant in a child proceeding who is not represented by\ncounsel is not to cross-examine a child complainant.\nNote:\nA person is not to cross-examine certain persons at committal\nproceedings or proceedings of a similar kind—see section 15YHA.\n\n(2) A person appointed by the court is to ask the child any questions\nthat the defendant requests the person to ask the child.\n15YFA  Unrepresented defendants—cross-examination of vulnerable\nadult complainants\n\n(1) A defendant in a vulnerable adult proceeding who is not\nrepresented by counsel is not to cross-examine a vulnerable adult\ncomplainant.\n\n\nProtecting vulnerable persons  Part IAD\nCross-examination  Division 3\n\nSection 15YG\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nNote:\nA person is not to cross-examine certain persons at committal\nproceedings or proceedings of a similar kind—see section 15YHA.\n\n(2) A person appointed by the court is to ask the vulnerable adult\ncomplainant any questions that the defendant requests the person to\nask the complainant.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yf-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yf-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yf-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yf-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4f5daa89ec4a7aac8c27be0867f045b8a32072301809c6343193294e73b31bd3"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15yf",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15YF Unrepresented defendants—cross-examination of child",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 182,
      "values:originalText": "complainants\n\n(1) A defendant in a child proceeding who is not represented by\ncounsel is not to cross-examine a child complainant.\nNote:\nA person is not to cross-examine certain persons at committal\nproceedings or proceedings of a similar kind—see section 15YHA.\n\n(2) A person appointed by the court is to ask the child any questions\nthat the defendant requests the person to ask the child.\n15YFA  Unrepresented defendants—cross-examination of vulnerable\nadult complainants\n\n(1) A defendant in a vulnerable adult proceeding who is not\nrepresented by counsel is not to cross-examine a vulnerable adult\ncomplainant.\n\n\nProtecting vulnerable persons  Part IAD\nCross-examination  Division 3\n\nSection 15YG\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nNote:\nA person is not to cross-examine certain persons at committal\nproceedings or proceedings of a similar kind—see section 15YHA.\n\n(2) A person appointed by the court is to ask the vulnerable adult\ncomplainant any questions that the defendant requests the person to\nask the complainant."
    },
