    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yh",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15YH Represented defendants—cross-examination of vulnerable",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15yh"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.184",
      "values:originalText": "persons\n\n(1) A defendant in a proceeding who is represented by counsel is not\nto cross-examine, except through counsel, a person to whom\nsubsection (2) applies.\nNote:\nA person is not to cross-examine certain persons at committal\nproceedings or proceedings of a similar kind—see section 15YHA.\n\n(2) This subsection applies to the following persons:\n\n(a) for a child proceeding—a child witness;\n\n(b) for a vulnerable adult proceeding—a vulnerable adult\ncomplainant;\n\n(c) for a special witness proceeding—a special witness for whom\nan order under subsection 15YAB(3) is in force for this\nsection.\n15YHA  Committal proceedings—cross-examination of vulnerable\npersons\n\n(1) A person is not to cross-examine, at committal proceedings or\nproceedings of a similar kind, a person to whom subsection (2)\napplies.\n\n(2) This subsection applies to the following persons:\n\n(a) for a child proceeding—a child witness;\n\n(b) for a vulnerable adult proceeding—a vulnerable adult\ncomplainant;\n\n\nProtecting vulnerable persons  Part IAD\nCross-examination  Division 3\n\nSection 15YHA\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(c) for a special witness proceeding—a special witness for whom\nan order under subsection 15YAB(3) is in force for this\nsection.\n\n\nPart IAD  Protecting vulnerable persons",
      "skos:definition": "persons\n\n(1) A defendant in a proceeding who is represented by counsel is not\nto cross-examine, except through counsel, a person to whom\nsubsection (2) applies.\nNote:\nA person is not to cross-examine certain persons at committal\nproceedings or proceedings of a similar kind—see section 15YHA.\n\n(2) This subsection applies to the following persons:\n\n(a) for a child proceeding—a child witness;\n\n(b) for a vulnerable adult proceeding—a vulnerable adult\ncomplainant;\n\n(c) for a special witness proceeding—a special witness for whom\nan order under subsection 15YAB(3) is in force for this\nsection.\n15YHA  Committal proceedings—cross-examination of vulnerable\npersons\n\n(1) A person is not to cross-examine, at committal proceedings or\nproceedings of a similar kind, a person to whom subsection (2)\napplies.\n\n(2) This subsection applies to the following persons:\n\n(a) for a child proceeding—a child witness;\n\n(b) for a vulnerable adult proceeding—a vulnerable adult\ncomplainant;\n\n\nProtecting vulnerable persons  Part IAD\nCross-examination  Division 3\n\nSection 15YHA\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(c) for a special witness proceeding—a special witness for whom\nan order under subsection 15YAB(3) is in force for this\nsection.\n\n\nPart IAD  Protecting vulnerable persons",
      "cml:hasPart": [
