    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yl-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15YL(1) Alternative arrangements for giving evidence",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15yl-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.188",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The court must order that evidence given in person by a person to\nwhom subsection (2) applies is to be recorded if:\n\n(a) the court is satisfied that the evidence could be used in\nanother proceeding; and\n\n\nProtecting vulnerable persons  Part IAD\nSpecial facilities for vulnerable persons to give evidence  Division 4\n\nSection 15YLA\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) the court is equipped with the necessary facilities; and\n\n(c) the person agrees to the evidence being recorded.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The court must order that evidence given in person by a person to\nwhom subsection (2) applies is to be recorded if:\n\n(a) the court is satisfied that the evidence could be used in\nanother proceeding; and\n\n\nProtecting vulnerable persons  Part IAD\nSpecial facilities for vulnerable persons to give evidence  Division 4\n\nSection 15YLA\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) the court is equipped with the necessary facilities; and\n\n(c) the person agrees to the evidence being recorded.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yl"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yl-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yl-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yl-ss-1-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d21033b356ee53994b99b40b58e3b1263ff304cd182d9a1a25472f15826ccd24",
      "skos:note": "Court must order recording of evidence given by vulnerable persons under certain conditions. Court must make arrangements to restrict contact with defendant and public while giving evidence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15yl-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15YL(1) Alternative arrangements for giving evidence",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 188,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The court must order that evidence given in person by a person to\nwhom subsection (2) applies is to be recorded if:\n\n(a) the court is satisfied that the evidence could be used in\nanother proceeding; and\n\n\nProtecting vulnerable persons  Part IAD\nSpecial facilities for vulnerable persons to give evidence  Division 4\n\nSection 15YLA\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) the court is equipped with the necessary facilities; and\n\n(c) the person agrees to the evidence being recorded."
    },
