    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ym",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15YM Use of video or audio recordings of interviews",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15ym"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.190",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A video or audio recording of an interview of a person to whom\nsubsection (1A) applies in a proceeding may be admitted as\nevidence in chief if a constable, or a person of a kind specified in\nthe regulations, conducted the interview.\n\n(1A) This subsection applies to the following persons:\n\n(a) for a child proceeding—a child witness;\n\n(b) for a vulnerable adult proceeding—a vulnerable adult\ncomplainant;\n\n(c) for a special witness proceeding—a special witness for whom\nan order under subsection 15YAB(3) is in force for this\nsection.\n\n(2) However, a recording that is an audio recording only must not be\nadmitted under subsection (1) unless the court is satisfied that\nextraordinary circumstances require the use of audio recording\nonly.\n\n(4) Subject to Divisions 2A and 3, if a video or audio recording of an\ninterview of a person is admitted as evidence in chief under\nsubsection (1), the person must be available for cross-examination\nand re-examination.\nNote 1:\nDivision 4 provides for this evidence to be given using closed-circuit\ntelevision or other arrangements.\nNote 2:\nDivision 3 imposes limitations on cross-examinations. For example, a\nperson is not to cross-examine certain persons at committal\nproceedings or proceedings of a similar kind—see section 15YHA.\nOffence\n\n(5) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person:\n\n\nProtecting vulnerable persons  Part IAD\nUse of video or audio recordings of interviews  Division 5\n\nSection 15YN\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(i) makes a recording (or other copy) of a recording, or a\npart of a recording, to which subsection (1) applies; or\n\n(ii) does anything (whether directly or indirectly) to damage\nor alter a recording, or a part of a recording, to which\nsubsection (1) applies; or\n\n(iii) possesses or supplies a recording, or a part of a\nrecording, to which subsection (1) applies; or\n\n(iv) possesses or supplies a copy of a recording, or a part of\na recording, to which subsection (1) applies; and\n\n(b) the person does so without lawful authority or excuse.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 60 penalty units, or both.\n\n(6) The fault element for paragraph (5)(a) is intention.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A video or audio recording of an interview of a person to whom\nsubsection (1A) applies in a proceeding may be admitted as\nevidence in chief if a constable, or a person of a kind specified in\nthe regulations, conducted the interview.\n\n(1A) This subsection applies to the following persons:\n\n(a) for a child proceeding—a child witness;\n\n(b) for a vulnerable adult proceeding—a vulnerable adult\ncomplainant;\n\n(c) for a special witness proceeding—a special witness for whom\nan order under subsection 15YAB(3) is in force for this\nsection.\n\n(2) However, a recording that is an audio recording only must not be\nadmitted under subsection (1) unless the court is satisfied that\nextraordinary circumstances require the use of audio recording\nonly.\n\n(4) Subject to Divisions 2A and 3, if a video or audio recording of an\ninterview of a person is admitted as evidence in chief under\nsubsection (1), the person must be available for cross-examination\nand re-examination.\nNote 1:\nDivision 4 provides for this evidence to be given using closed-circuit\ntelevision or other arrangements.\nNote 2:\nDivision 3 imposes limitations on cross-examinations. For example, a\nperson is not to cross-examine certain persons at committal\nproceedings or proceedings of a similar kind—see section 15YHA.\nOffence\n\n(5) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person:\n\n\nProtecting vulnerable persons  Part IAD\nUse of video or audio recordings of interviews  Division 5\n\nSection 15YN\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(i) makes a recording (or other copy) of a recording, or a\npart of a recording, to which subsection (1) applies; or\n\n(ii) does anything (whether directly or indirectly) to damage\nor alter a recording, or a part of a recording, to which\nsubsection (1) applies; or\n\n(iii) possesses or supplies a recording, or a part of a\nrecording, to which subsection (1) applies; or\n\n(iv) possesses or supplies a copy of a recording, or a part of\na recording, to which subsection (1) applies; and\n\n(b) the person d",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ym-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ym-ss-1a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ym-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ym-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ym-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ym-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2500f316feb93792381fd345c8c9f193d66e342b5bbcb0fcabb01e300204481e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15ym",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15YM Use of video or audio recordings of interviews",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 190,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A video or audio recording of an interview of a person to whom\nsubsection (1A) applies in a proceeding may be admitted as\nevidence in chief if a constable, or a person of a kind specified in\nthe regulations, conducted the interview.\n\n(1A) This subsection applies to the following persons:\n\n(a) for a child proceeding—a child witness;\n\n(b) for a vulnerable adult proceeding—a vulnerable adult\ncomplainant;\n\n(c) for a special witness proceeding—a special witness for whom\nan order under subsection 15YAB(3) is in force for this\nsection.\n\n(2) However, a recording that is an audio recording only must not be\nadmitted under subsection (1) unless the court is satisfied that\nextraordinary circumstances require the use of audio recording\nonly.\n\n(4) Subject to Divisions 2A and 3, if a video or audio recording of an\ninterview of a person is admitted as evidence in chief under\nsubsection (1), the person must be available for cross-examination\nand re-examination.\nNote 1:\nDivision 4 provides for this evidence to be given using closed-circuit\ntelevision or other arrangements.\nNote 2:\nDivision 3 imposes limitations on cross-examinations. For example, a\nperson is not to cross-examine certain persons at committal\nproceedings or proceedings of a similar kind—see section 15YHA.\nOffence\n\n(5) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person:\n\n\nProtecting vulnerable persons  Part IAD\nUse of video or audio recordings of interviews  Division 5\n\nSection 15YN\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(i) makes a recording (or other copy) of a recording, or a\npart of a recording, to which subsection (1) applies; or\n\n(ii) does anything (whether directly or indirectly) to damage\nor alter a recording, or a part of a recording, to which\nsubsection (1) applies; or\n\n(iii) possesses or supplies a recording, or a part of a\nrecording, to which subsection (1) applies; or\n\n(iv) possesses or supplies a copy of a recording, or a part of\na recording, to which subsection (1) applies; and\n\n(b) the person does so without lawful authority or excuse.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 60 penalty units, or both.\n\n(6) The fault element for paragraph (5)(a) is intention."
    },
