    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ym-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15YM(5) Use of video or audio recordings of interviews",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15ym-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.190",
      "values:originalText": "(5) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person:\n\n\nProtecting vulnerable persons  Part IAD\nUse of video or audio recordings of interviews  Division 5\n\nSection 15YN\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(i) makes a recording (or other copy) of a recording, or a\npart of a recording, to which subsection (1) applies; or\n\n(ii) does anything (whether directly or indirectly) to damage\nor alter a recording, or a part of a recording, to which\nsubsection (1) applies; or\n\n(iii) possesses or supplies a recording, or a part of a\nrecording, to which subsection (1) applies; or\n\n(iv) possesses or supplies a copy of a recording, or a part of\na recording, to which subsection (1) applies; and\n\n(b) the person does so without lawful authority or excuse.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 60 penalty units, or both.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person:\n\n\nProtecting vulnerable persons  Part IAD\nUse of video or audio recordings of interviews  Division 5\n\nSection 15YN\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(i) makes a recording (or other copy) of a recording, or a\npart of a recording, to which subsection (1) applies; or\n\n(ii) does anything (whether directly or indirectly) to damage\nor alter a recording, or a part of a recording, to which\nsubsection (1) applies; or\n\n(iii) possesses or supplies a recording, or a part of a\nrecording, to which subsection (1) applies; or\n\n(iv) possesses or supplies a copy of a recording, or a part of\na recording, to which subsection (1) applies; and\n\n(b) the person does so without lawful authority or excuse.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 60 penalty units, or both.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ym"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ym-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15ym-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bc31fe1f4e6ca77cc8fcf93fbfb2751cb3e03794c2323a76e7adaebcd9bdb930",
      "skos:note": "Making, possessing, or supplying recordings of interviews without lawful authority is prohibited."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15ym-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15YM(5) Use of video or audio recordings of interviews",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 190,
      "values:originalText": "(5) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person:\n\n\nProtecting vulnerable persons  Part IAD\nUse of video or audio recordings of interviews  Division 5\n\nSection 15YN\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(i) makes a recording (or other copy) of a recording, or a\npart of a recording, to which subsection (1) applies; or\n\n(ii) does anything (whether directly or indirectly) to damage\nor alter a recording, or a part of a recording, to which\nsubsection (1) applies; or\n\n(iii) possesses or supplies a recording, or a part of a\nrecording, to which subsection (1) applies; or\n\n(iv) possesses or supplies a copy of a recording, or a part of\na recording, to which subsection (1) applies; and\n\n(b) the person does so without lawful authority or excuse.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 60 penalty units, or both."
    },
