    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yn",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15YN Admissibility of evidence given using video or audio",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15yn"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.191",
      "values:originalText": "recordings of interviews\n\n(1) The admissibility of the evidence given by video or audio\nrecording is not affected by the fact that it is evidence of previous\nrepresentations that the person made in the interview that was\nbeing recorded.\n\n(2) Evidence given by video or audio recording under section 15YM is\nnot admissible if the court is satisfied that:\n\n(a) any defendant in the proceeding (other than the person if the\nperson is a defendant); or\n\n(b) the defendant’s lawyer (if any);\nwas not given a reasonable opportunity to view or listen to the\nrecording.\n\n(3) The court may refuse to admit the whole or part of the contents of a\nrecording adduced as evidence under section 15YM.\n\n\nPart IAD  Protecting vulnerable persons",
      "skos:definition": "recordings of interviews\n\n(1) The admissibility of the evidence given by video or audio\nrecording is not affected by the fact that it is evidence of previous\nrepresentations that the person made in the interview that was\nbeing recorded.\n\n(2) Evidence given by video or audio recording under section 15YM is\nnot admissible if the court is satisfied that:\n\n(a) any defendant in the proceeding (other than the person if the\nperson is a defendant); or\n\n(b) the defendant’s lawyer (if any);\nwas not given a reasonable opportunity to view or listen to the\nrecording.\n\n(3) The court may refuse to admit the whole or part of the contents of a\nrecording adduced as evidence under section 15YM.\n\n\nPart IAD  Protecting vulnerable persons",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yn-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yn-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yn-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7ff04b70be5232919113371b6a5e9645766f5e62fc0fb152690143a6af65c586"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15yn",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15YN Admissibility of evidence given using video or audio",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 191,
      "values:originalText": "recordings of interviews\n\n(1) The admissibility of the evidence given by video or audio\nrecording is not affected by the fact that it is evidence of previous\nrepresentations that the person made in the interview that was\nbeing recorded.\n\n(2) Evidence given by video or audio recording under section 15YM is\nnot admissible if the court is satisfied that:\n\n(a) any defendant in the proceeding (other than the person if the\nperson is a defendant); or\n\n(b) the defendant’s lawyer (if any);\nwas not given a reasonable opportunity to view or listen to the\nrecording.\n\n(3) The court may refuse to admit the whole or part of the contents of a\nrecording adduced as evidence under section 15YM.\n\n\nPart IAD  Protecting vulnerable persons"
    },
