    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yq",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15YQ Warnings etc. not to be given about vulnerable persons",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15yq"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.196",
      "values:originalText": "evidence\n\n(1) If there is a jury in a proceeding in which a person to whom\nsubsection (2) applies has given or will give evidence, the judge is\nnot to warn the jury, or suggest to the jury in any way:\n\n(a) that the law regards persons to whom subsection (2) applies\nas an unreliable class of witness; or\n\n\nProtecting vulnerable persons  Part IAD\nMiscellaneous  Division 6\n\nSection 15YR\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) that the law requires greater or lesser weight to be given to\nevidence that is given by closed-circuit television or\nalternative arrangements under Division 4; or\n\n(c) that the law requires greater or lesser weight to be given to\nevidence that is given by a video or audio recording under",
      "skos:definition": "evidence\n\n(1) If there is a jury in a proceeding in which a person to whom\nsubsection (2) applies has given or will give evidence, the judge is\nnot to warn the jury, or suggest to the jury in any way:\n\n(a) that the law regards persons to whom subsection (2) applies\nas an unreliable class of witness; or\n\n\nProtecting vulnerable persons  Part IAD\nMiscellaneous  Division 6\n\nSection 15YR\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) that the law requires greater or lesser weight to be given to\nevidence that is given by closed-circuit television or\nalternative arrangements under Division 4; or\n\n(c) that the law requires greater or lesser weight to be given to\nevidence that is given by a video or audio recording under",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yq-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yq-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yq-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d044c720baee40034ea344bea189a473877686147e8c42ba953d611d0b4d9254",
      "skos:note": "Judge must not warn jury about vulnerable persons"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15yq",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15YQ Warnings etc. not to be given about vulnerable persons",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 196,
      "values:originalText": "evidence\n\n(1) If there is a jury in a proceeding in which a person to whom\nsubsection (2) applies has given or will give evidence, the judge is\nnot to warn the jury, or suggest to the jury in any way:\n\n(a) that the law regards persons to whom subsection (2) applies\nas an unreliable class of witness; or\n\n\nProtecting vulnerable persons  Part IAD\nMiscellaneous  Division 6\n\nSection 15YR\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) that the law requires greater or lesser weight to be given to\nevidence that is given by closed-circuit television or\nalternative arrangements under Division 4; or\n\n(c) that the law requires greater or lesser weight to be given to\nevidence that is given by a video or audio recording under"
    },
    {
