      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Section 15YW(2)",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Witness must provide evidence by video link."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yu-ss-2-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "also applies",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to apply",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) This Part also applies to:"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yu-ss-2-logic-deontic-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "extends",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Extends the definition of prosecutor and defendant",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) were instituted before or after the commencement of this Part.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The extended meaning applies to proceedings instituted before or after the commencement of this Part."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yu-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15YU(4) Proceedings to which this Part applies",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15yu-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.202",
      "values:originalText": "(4) This Part has effect, in relation to a proceeding under the Proceeds\nof Crime Act 2002, as if:\n\n(a) the responsible authority for the proceeding under that Act\nwere the prosecutor; and\n\n(b) each other party to the proceeding were a defendant in the\nproceeding.\nNote:\nUnder that Act, the responsible authority is the Commissioner of the\nAustralian Federal Police or the Director of Public Prosecutions (see\nthe definitions of responsible authority and proceeds of crime\nauthority in section 338 of that Act). Responsibility can be transferred\nbetween these authorities (see section 315B of that Act).\nDefinitions",
      "skos:definition": "(4) This Part has effect, in relation to a proceeding under the Proceeds\nof Crime Act 2002, as if:\n\n(a) the responsible authority for the proceeding under that Act\nwere the prosecutor; and\n\n(b) each other party to the proceeding were a defendant in the\nproceeding.\nNote:\nUnder that Act, the responsible authority is the Commissioner of the\nAustralian Federal Police or the Director of Public Prosecutions (see\nthe definitions of responsible authority and proceeds of crime\nauthority in section 338 of that Act). Responsibility can be transferred\nbetween these authorities (see section 315B of that Act).\nDefinitions",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yu"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yu-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yu-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yu-ss-4-logic-deontic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "578aaf2a7c4c9b3e4b7ce466efc08b8fc3f9d0ca59196981a4d21892b76d208a",
      "skos:note": "Transfers responsibility between authorities under the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15yu-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15YU(4) Proceedings to which this Part applies",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 202,
      "values:originalText": "(4) This Part has effect, in relation to a proceeding under the Proceeds\nof Crime Act 2002, as if:\n\n(a) the responsible authority for the proceeding under that Act\nwere the prosecutor; and\n\n(b) each other party to the proceeding were a defendant in the\nproceeding.\nNote:\nUnder that Act, the responsible authority is the Commissioner of the\nAustralian Federal Police or the Director of Public Prosecutions (see\nthe definitions of responsible authority and proceeds of crime\nauthority in section 338 of that Act). Responsibility can be transferred\nbetween these authorities (see section 315B of that Act).\nDefinitions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yu-ss-4-norm",
