      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yu-ss-4-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Transfer",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Transfers responsibility",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a) the responsible authority for the proceeding under that Act were the prosecutor;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Responsibility can be transferred between these authorities (see section 315B of that Act)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yu-ss-4-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Assignment",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Assigns responsibility to the prosecutor",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(b) each other party to the proceeding were a defendant in the proceeding."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yu-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15YU(5) Proceedings to which this Part applies",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15yu-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.202",
      "values:originalText": "(5) In this section:\n\n\nPart IAE  Video link evidence in proceedings for terrorism and related offences etc.\n\nSection 15YV\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nPMV-related questioning warrant means a questioning warrant\nthat is issued in relation to politically motivated violence (within\nthe meaning of the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation\nAct 1979).\nquestioning warrant has the same meaning as in Division 3 of\nPart III of the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation Act\n1979.\n15YV  When court may take evidence by video link\nApplication by prosecutor",
      "skos:definition": "(5) In this section:\n\n\nPart IAE  Video link evidence in proceedings for terrorism and related offences etc.\n\nSection 15YV\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nPMV-related questioning warrant means a questioning warrant\nthat is issued in relation to politically motivated violence (within\nthe meaning of the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation\nAct 1979).\nquestioning warrant has the same meaning as in Division 3 of\nPart III of the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation Act\n1979.\n15YV  When court may take evidence by video link\nApplication by prosecutor",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yu"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yu-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yu-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yu-ss-5-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "abbe80369e41cab9362147b50e2ad32377fd1cb1949bc57efe56bbe96aff8592",
      "skos:note": "Application by prosecutor for court to take evidence by video link"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15yu-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15YU(5) Proceedings to which this Part applies",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 202,
      "values:originalText": "(5) In this section:\n\n\nPart IAE  Video link evidence in proceedings for terrorism and related offences etc.\n\nSection 15YV\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nPMV-related questioning warrant means a questioning warrant\nthat is issued in relation to politically motivated violence (within\nthe meaning of the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation\nAct 1979).\nquestioning warrant has the same meaning as in Division 3 of\nPart III of the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation Act\n1979.\n15YV  When court may take evidence by video link\nApplication by prosecutor"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yu-ss-5-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yu-ss-5"
      },
