    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yu-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15YU(2) Proceedings to which this Part applies",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15yu-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.202",
      "values:originalText": "(2) In a proceeding, the court must:\n\n(a) direct; or\n\n(b) by order, allow;\na witness to give evidence by video link if:\n\n\nVideo link evidence in proceedings for terrorism and related offences etc.  Part IAE\n\nSection 15YW\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(c) both:\n\n(i) a defendant in the proceeding applies for the direction\nor order; and\n\n(ii) the court is satisfied that the defendant gave the court\nreasonable notice of his or her intention to make the\napplication; and\n\n(d) the witness is not a defendant in the proceeding; and\n\n(e) the witness is available, or will reasonably be available, to\ngive evidence by video link; and\n\n(f) the facilities required by section 15YY are available or can\nreasonably be made available;\nunless the court is satisfied that it would be inconsistent with the\ninterests of justice for the evidence to be given by video link.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) In a proceeding, the court must:\n\n(a) direct; or\n\n(b) by order, allow;\na witness to give evidence by video link if:\n\n\nVideo link evidence in proceedings for terrorism and related offences etc.  Part IAE\n\nSection 15YW\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(c) both:\n\n(i) a defendant in the proceeding applies for the direction\nor order; and\n\n(ii) the court is satisfied that the defendant gave the court\nreasonable notice of his or her intention to make the\napplication; and\n\n(d) the witness is not a defendant in the proceeding; and\n\n(e) the witness is available, or will reasonably be available, to\ngive evidence by video link; and\n\n(f) the facilities required by section 15YY are available or can\nreasonably be made available;\nunless the court is satisfied that it would be inconsistent with the\ninterests of justice for the evidence to be given by video link.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yu"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yu-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yu-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yu-ss-2-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yu-ss-2-logic-deontic-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c27971f7c3ebcc78cf8abe98e119ca2965db4f1c64ad26ff6e355dc6632cb30e",
      "skos:note": "Must allow witness to give evidence by video link under specified conditions. Proceedings under this Part also apply to proceedings under the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002. Extended meaning of prosecutor and defendant"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15yu-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15YU(2) Proceedings to which this Part applies",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 202,
      "values:originalText": "(2) In a proceeding, the court must:\n\n(a) direct; or\n\n(b) by order, allow;\na witness to give evidence by video link if:\n\n\nVideo link evidence in proceedings for terrorism and related offences etc.  Part IAE\n\nSection 15YW\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(c) both:\n\n(i) a defendant in the proceeding applies for the direction\nor order; and\n\n(ii) the court is satisfied that the defendant gave the court\nreasonable notice of his or her intention to make the\napplication; and\n\n(d) the witness is not a defendant in the proceeding; and\n\n(e) the witness is available, or will reasonably be available, to\ngive evidence by video link; and\n\n(f) the facilities required by section 15YY are available or can\nreasonably be made available;\nunless the court is satisfied that it would be inconsistent with the\ninterests of justice for the evidence to be given by video link."
    },
