      "cml:integrityHash": "079ea53ed8c3c460cb22e17596301823a7ee8f92e34a5cfb790e9e1018d6da03",
      "skos:note": "Defendant may appeal against section 15YV direction or order. Ensure equal weight to witness evidence in jury proceedings. A person must give evidence at the courtroom or other place where the court is sitting."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15yz-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15YZ(1) Direction to jury",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 209,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) a court gives a section 15YV direction or makes a\nsection 15YV order; and\n\n(b) the prosecutor applied for the direction or order;\n\n\nVideo link evidence in proceedings for terrorism and related offences etc.  Part IAE\n\nSection 15YZE\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\na defendant in the proceeding may appeal against the direction or\norder."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yz-ss-1-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yz-ss-1"
