    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yz-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15YZ(5) Direction to jury",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-15yz-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.209",
      "values:originalText": "(5) A court that has jurisdiction to hear and determine appeals from a\njudgment, order or direction in the proceeding has jurisdiction to\nhear and determine any appeal under this section.\n15YZE  Other laws about evidence not affected\n\nThis Part does not prevent any other law about taking evidence of a\nwitness from applying for the purposes of a proceeding.\n\n\nPart IAE  Video link evidence in proceedings for terrorism and related offences etc.\n\nSection 15YZF\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n15YZF  Saving of other laws\n\nThis Part is not intended to exclude or limit the operation of any\nother law of the Commonwealth or any law of a State or Territory.\n\n\nSentencing, imprisonment and release of federal offenders  Part IB\nInterpretation  Division 1\n\nSection 16\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(5) A court that has jurisdiction to hear and determine appeals from a\njudgment, order or direction in the proceeding has jurisdiction to\nhear and determine any appeal under this section.\n15YZE  Other laws about evidence not affected\n\nThis Part does not prevent any other law about taking evidence of a\nwitness from applying for the purposes of a proceeding.\n\n\nPart IAE  Video link evidence in proceedings for terrorism and related offences etc.\n\nSection 15YZF\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n15YZF  Saving of other laws\n\nThis Part is not intended to exclude or limit the operation of any\nother law of the Commonwealth or any law of a State or Territory.\n\n\nSentencing, imprisonment and release of federal offenders  Part IB\nInterpretation  Division 1\n\nSection 16\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-15yz"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
