      "skos:definition": "(1) In determining the sentence to be passed, or the order to be made,\nin respect of any person for a federal offence, a court must impose\na sentence or make an order that is of a severity appropriate in all\nthe circumstances of the offence.\nNote:\nMinimum penalties apply for certain offences—see sections 16AAA,\n16AAB and 16AAC.",
