      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-16c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "16C Fines",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-16c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.236",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), before imposing a fine on a person for a\nfederal offence, a court must take into account the financial\ncircumstances of the person, in addition to any other matters that\nthe court is required or permitted to take into account.\n\n(2) Nothing in subsection (1) prevents a court from imposing a fine on\na person because the financial circumstances of the offender cannot\nbe ascertained by the court.\n\n\nSentencing, imprisonment and release of federal offenders  Part IB\nGeneral sentencing principles  Division 2\n\nSection 16D\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), before imposing a fine on a person for a\nfederal offence, a court must take into account the financial\ncircumstances of the person, in addition to any other matters that\nthe court is required or permitted to take into account.\n\n(2) Nothing in subsection (1) prevents a court from imposing a fine on\na person because the financial circumstances of the offender cannot\nbe ascertained by the court.\n\n\nSentencing, imprisonment and release of federal offenders  Part IB\nGeneral sentencing principles  Division 2\n\nSection 16D\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-16c-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-16c-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "dbb4eb7bdd142faaa3e402b12a70bc42ad97ed90b70364fdee16f5818a8de4e0"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-16c",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "16C Fines",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 236,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), before imposing a fine on a person for a\nfederal offence, a court must take into account the financial\ncircumstances of the person, in addition to any other matters that\nthe court is required or permitted to take into account.\n\n(2) Nothing in subsection (1) prevents a court from imposing a fine on\na person because the financial circumstances of the offender cannot\nbe ascertained by the court.\n\n\nSentencing, imprisonment and release of federal offenders  Part IB\nGeneral sentencing principles  Division 2\n\nSection 16D\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026"
    },
    {
