      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19ad-ss-1"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19ad-ss-1-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Imposes duty on the state to consider existing non-parole period when imposing further sentence.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a) a non-parole period (in this section called the existing\nnon-parole period) has been fixed in respect of a federal\nsentence or federal sentences;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "This section applies."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19ad-ss-1-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Overlaps",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Defines temporal relationship between existing and imposed sentences.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(b) while the offender is serving the existing non-parole period, a\ncourt imposes a further federal sentence on the person;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The existing and imposed sentences overlap in time."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19ad-ss-1-logic-ltl-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LTL"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Recurrent",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Defines recurring trace of persons subject to non-parole period.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::temporal_ltl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a) a non-parole period (in this section called the existing\nnon-parole period) has been fixed in respect of a federal\nsentence or federal sentences;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The person is part of a recurring trace of persons subject to non-parole periods."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19ad-ss-1-logic-deontic-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Permission",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Allows state to impose further sentence without violating existing non-parole period.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(b) while the offender is serving the existing non-parole period, a\ncourt imposes a further federal sentence on the person;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The court may impose a further sentence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19ad-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "19AD(2) Persons already subject to a non-parole period",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-19ad-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.247",
      "values:originalText": "(2) Where this section applies, the court must, after considering the\nrelevant circumstances, including:\n\n(a) the existing non-parole period; and\n\n(b) the nature and circumstances of the offence or offences\nconcerned; and\n\n(c) the antecedents of the person;\ndo one of the following things:\n\n(d) make an order confirming the existing non-parole period;\n\n(e) fix a new single non-parole period in respect of all federal\nsentences the person is to serve or complete;\n\n(f) where the court decides that, in the circumstances, a\nnon-parole period is not appropriate—cancel the existing\nnon-parole period and decline to fix a new non-parole period.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) Where this section applies, the court must, after considering the\nrelevant circumstances, including:\n\n(a) the existing non-parole period; and\n\n(b) the nature and circumstances of the offence or offences\nconcerned; and\n\n(c) the antecedents of the person;\ndo one of the following things:\n\n(d) make an order confirming the existing non-parole period;\n\n(e) fix a new single non-parole period in respect of all federal\nsentences the person is to serve or complete;\n\n(f) where the court decides that, in the circumstances, a\nnon-parole period is not appropriate—cancel the existing\nnon-parole period and decline to fix a new non-parole period.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19ad"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19ad-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19ad-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d5ccdf6a0ee0159cd719b9d21e0cf31da7e4727672d139bb2d38bef3f6282fc1",
      "skos:note": "Court must consider circumstances and decide on a non-parole period."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-19ad-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "19AD(2) Persons already subject to a non-parole period",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 247,
      "values:originalText": "(2) Where this section applies, the court must, after considering the\nrelevant circumstances, including:\n\n(a) the existing non-parole period; and\n\n(b) the nature and circumstances of the offence or offences\nconcerned; and\n\n(c) the antecedents of the person;\ndo one of the following things:\n\n(d) make an order confirming the existing non-parole period;\n\n(e) fix a new single non-parole period in respect of all federal\nsentences the person is to serve or complete;\n\n(f) where the court decides that, in the circumstances, a\nnon-parole period is not appropriate—cancel the existing\nnon-parole period and decline to fix a new non-parole period."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19ad-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19ad-ss-2"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19ad-ss-2-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Court must consider circumstances and decide on a non-parole period.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19ad-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "19AD(3) Persons already subject to a non-parole period",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-19ad-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.247",
      "values:originalText": "(3) Where, under paragraph (2)(e), the court fixes a new single\nnon-parole period, it:\n\n(a) is to be treated as having superseded the existing non-parole\nperiod; and\n\n(b) must not be such as to allow the person to be released on\nparole earlier then would have been the case if the further\nsentence had not been imposed.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) Where, under paragraph (2)(e), the court fixes a new single\nnon-parole period, it:\n\n(a) is to be treated as having superseded the existing non-parole\nperiod; and\n\n(b) must not be such as to allow the person to be released on\nparole earlier then would have been the case if the further\nsentence had not been imposed.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19ad"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19ad-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19ad-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19ad-ss-3-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19ad-ss-3-logic-alleninterval-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19ad-ss-3-logic-argumentation-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19ad-ss-3-logic-diffusion-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b378d4cd558190f374e97781d209e3a1e963cbeb4de95f82eb78cb1d2e5cbd1d",
      "skos:note": "Supersedes existing non-parole period if new sentence is imposed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-19ad-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "19AD(3) Persons already subject to a non-parole period",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 247,
      "values:originalText": "(3) Where, under paragraph (2)(e), the court fixes a new single\nnon-parole period, it:\n\n(a) is to be treated as having superseded the existing non-parole\nperiod; and\n\n(b) must not be such as to allow the person to be released on\nparole earlier then would have been the case if the further\nsentence had not been imposed."
    },
    {
