    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19al-ss-2a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "19AL(2A) Release on parole—making of parole order",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-19al-ss-2a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.254",
      "values:originalText": "(2A) If the Attorney-General does not, under paragraph (2)(b),\nreconsider the making of a parole order for a person and either\nmake, or refuse to make, such an order before the end of the 12\nmonth period referred to in that paragraph, the Attorney-General\nmust, as soon as practicable after the end of that period, reconsider\nand either make, or refuse to make, a parole order for the person.\nContents of parole order",
      "skos:definition": "(2A) If the Attorney-General does not, under paragraph (2)(b),\nreconsider the making of a parole order for a person and either\nmake, or refuse to make, such an order before the end of the 12\nmonth period referred to in that paragraph, the Attorney-General\nmust, as soon as practicable after the end of that period, reconsider\nand either make, or refuse to make, a parole order for the person.\nContents of parole order",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19al"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19al-ss-2a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19al-ss-2a-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f2a3e8d668c291eadecb86e3fd3ee69a399a5af3acd3fc46b64c1ea7b5953292",
      "skos:note": "Reconsideration of parole order within a specified timeframe."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-19al-ss-2a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "19AL(2A) Release on parole—making of parole order",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 254,
      "values:originalText": "(2A) If the Attorney-General does not, under paragraph (2)(b),\nreconsider the making of a parole order for a person and either\nmake, or refuse to make, such an order before the end of the 12\nmonth period referred to in that paragraph, the Attorney-General\nmust, as soon as practicable after the end of that period, reconsider\nand either make, or refuse to make, a parole order for the person.\nContents of parole order"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19al-ss-2a-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
