    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19al-ss-2a-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to reconsider parole order",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The Attorney-General must reconsider the making of a parole order.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The Attorney-General must reconsider and either make or refuse to make a parole order for the person."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19al-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "19AL(3) Release on parole—making of parole order",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-19al-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.254",
      "values:originalText": "(3) A parole order must:\n\n(a) be in writing; and\n\n(b) specify whether or not the person is to be released subject to\nsupervision; and\n\n(c) if it is proposed that the supervision period for a person\nreleased on parole subject to supervision should end before\nthe end of the person’s parole period—specify the day on\nwhich the supervision period ends.\nNote 1:\nFor when a person is released on parole in accordance with a parole\norder, see section 19AM.\nNote 2:\nA person released on parole must comply with any conditions of the\nparole order during the parole period (see sections 19AMA, 19AN and\n19AU).",
      "skos:definition": "(3) A parole order must:\n\n(a) be in writing; and\n\n(b) specify whether or not the person is to be released subject to\nsupervision; and\n\n(c) if it is proposed that the supervision period for a person\nreleased on parole subject to supervision should end before\nthe end of the person’s parole period—specify the day on\nwhich the supervision period ends.\nNote 1:\nFor when a person is released on parole in accordance with a parole\norder, see section 19AM.\nNote 2:\nA person released on parole must comply with any conditions of the\nparole order during the parole period (see sections 19AMA, 19AN and\n19AU).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19al"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19al-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19al-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19al-ss-3-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19al-ss-3-logic-deontic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19al-ss-3-logic-alleninterval-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19al-ss-3-logic-deontic-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "141d48216024846bb86e62058d2fe4065d662acb8891918f7fa028c1138104f6",
      "skos:note": "Parole order must be in writing and specify supervision conditions.",
      "dc:description": "(a) A parole order must be in writing; (b) specify whether or not the person is to be released subject to supervision; (c) if it is proposed that the supervision period for a person released on parole subject to supervision should end before the end of the person’s parole period—specify the day on which the supervision period ends."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-19al-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "19AL(3) Release on parole—making of parole order",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 254,
      "values:originalText": "(3) A parole order must:\n\n(a) be in writing; and\n\n(b) specify whether or not the person is to be released subject to\nsupervision; and\n\n(c) if it is proposed that the supervision period for a person\nreleased on parole subject to supervision should end before\nthe end of the person’s parole period—specify the day on\nwhich the supervision period ends.\nNote 1:\nFor when a person is released on parole in accordance with a parole\norder, see section 19AM.\nNote 2:\nA person released on parole must comply with any conditions of the\nparole order during the parole period (see sections 19AMA, 19AN and\n19AU)."
    },
