    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19al-ss-3a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "19AL(3A) Release on parole—making of parole order",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-19al-ss-3a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.254",
      "values:originalText": "(3A) If the Attorney-General considers that in all the circumstances it is\nappropriate to do so, the Attorney-General may specify in a parole\norder that a person is to be released from prison on a day that is\nbefore the end of the non-parole period, but is not earlier than 30\ndays before the end of the non-parole period.",
      "skos:definition": "(3A) If the Attorney-General considers that in all the circumstances it is\nappropriate to do so, the Attorney-General may specify in a parole\norder that a person is to be released from prison on a day that is\nbefore the end of the non-parole period, but is not earlier than 30\ndays before the end of the non-parole period.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19al"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19al-ss-3a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19al-ss-3a-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "01c62549d480aa5839181e9df2dc02a0829499d3e63b11a9d5e8c56c7f6b5714",
      "skos:note": "Specify parole order release date within 30 days before non-parole period end"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-19al-ss-3a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "19AL(3A) Release on parole—making of parole order",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 254,
      "values:originalText": "(3A) If the Attorney-General considers that in all the circumstances it is\nappropriate to do so, the Attorney-General may specify in a parole\norder that a person is to be released from prison on a day that is\nbefore the end of the non-parole period, but is not earlier than 30\ndays before the end of the non-parole period."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19al-ss-3a-norm",
