      "skos:note": "Revocation of parole licence upon new offence conviction"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-19aq-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "19AQ(2) Parole order or licence revoked following further offence",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 265,
      "values:originalText": "(2) If a person to whom a licence relates is sentenced to life\nimprisonment or to a sentence of, or sentences aggregating, more\nthan 3 months in respect of a federal, State or Territory offence\n(the new offence) committed during the licence period, the court\nthat sentences the person for the new offence must determine the\ntime (the revocation time) when the licence is taken to have been\nrevoked."
    },
    {
