    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19as",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "19AS Court to issue warrant of detention where person required to",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-19as"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.268",
      "values:originalText": "serve balance of sentence\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) a person who is serving or is to serve a federal sentence or\nfederal sentences is released on parole or licence under this\nAct; and\n\n(b) the person is later sentenced (the new sentence or sentences)\nto a term of imprisonment in respect of one or more federal,\nState or Territory offences committed during the parole\nperiod or licence period; and\n\n(c) under section 19AQ:\n\n(i) the parole order or licence is to be taken to have been\nrevoked; and\n\n(ii) the person becomes liable to serve a part of a sentence\nor sentences (the outstanding sentence or sentences);\nthen:\n\n(d) the court imposing the new sentence or sentences must issue\na warrant authorising the person to be detained in prison to\n\n\nSentencing, imprisonment and release of federal offenders  Part IB\nConditional release on parole or licence  Division 5\n\nSection 19AT\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nundergo imprisonment for the unserved part of the\noutstanding sentence or sentences; and\n\n(e) the person must begin to serve the unserved part of the\noutstanding sentence or of the first to be served of the\noutstanding sentences on the day that the new sentence is, or\nthe new sentences are, imposed; and\n\n(f) the unserved part of the outstanding sentence or of each of\nthe outstanding sentences must be served in the State or\nTerritory where the new sentence is, or the new sentences\nare, imposed.\n\n(2) Where the court fails to issue a warrant under paragraph (1)(d), the\nDirector of Public Prosecutions may apply to that court for such a\nwarrant.",
      "skos:definition": "serve balance of sentence\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) a person who is serving or is to serve a federal sentence or\nfederal sentences is released on parole or licence under this\nAct; and\n\n(b) the person is later sentenced (the new sentence or sentences)\nto a term of imprisonment in respect of one or more federal,\nState or Territory offences committed during the parole\nperiod or licence period; and\n\n(c) under section 19AQ:\n\n(i) the parole order or licence is to be taken to have been\nrevoked; and\n\n(ii) the person becomes liable to serve a part of a sentence\nor sentences (the outstanding sentence or sentences);\nthen:\n\n(d) the court imposing the new sentence or sentences must issue\na warrant authorising the person to be detained in prison to\n\n\nSentencing, imprisonment and release of federal offenders  Part IB\nConditional release on parole or licence  Division 5\n\nSection 19AT\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nundergo imprisonment for the unserved part of the\noutstanding sentence or sentences; and\n\n(e) the person must begin to serve the unserved part of the\noutstanding sentence or of the first to be served of the\noutstanding sentences on the day that the new sentence is, or\nthe new sentences are, imposed; and\n\n(f) the unserved part of the outstanding sentence or of each of\nthe outstanding sentences must be served in the State or\nTerritory where the new sentence is, or the new sentences\nare, imposed.\n\n(2) Where the court fails to issue a warrant under paragraph (1)(d), the\nDirector of Public Prosecutions may apply to that court for such a\nwarrant.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19as-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19as-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "692fd2655ffa1eb65a0fb5882d67c40c5b933d3e255bb5d5f413ae094f22f117"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-19as",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "19AS Court to issue warrant of detention where person required to",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 268,
      "values:originalText": "serve balance of sentence\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) a person who is serving or is to serve a federal sentence or\nfederal sentences is released on parole or licence under this\nAct; and\n\n(b) the person is later sentenced (the new sentence or sentences)\nto a term of imprisonment in respect of one or more federal,\nState or Territory offences committed during the parole\nperiod or licence period; and\n\n(c) under section 19AQ:\n\n(i) the parole order or licence is to be taken to have been\nrevoked; and\n\n(ii) the person becomes liable to serve a part of a sentence\nor sentences (the outstanding sentence or sentences);\nthen:\n\n(d) the court imposing the new sentence or sentences must issue\na warrant authorising the person to be detained in prison to\n\n\nSentencing, imprisonment and release of federal offenders  Part IB\nConditional release on parole or licence  Division 5\n\nSection 19AT\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nundergo imprisonment for the unserved part of the\noutstanding sentence or sentences; and\n\n(e) the person must begin to serve the unserved part of the\noutstanding sentence or of the first to be served of the\noutstanding sentences on the day that the new sentence is, or\nthe new sentences are, imposed; and\n\n(f) the unserved part of the outstanding sentence or of each of\nthe outstanding sentences must be served in the State or\nTerritory where the new sentence is, or the new sentences\nare, imposed.\n\n(2) Where the court fails to issue a warrant under paragraph (1)(d), the\nDirector of Public Prosecutions may apply to that court for such a\nwarrant."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19as-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "19AS(1) Court to issue warrant of detention where person required to",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-19as-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
