          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19au-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19au-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19au-ss-1-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19au-ss-1-logic-alleninterval-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "244700c671ce4a5318e57227790dba5ca3fa277f3f8431da3cc68030269af7e6",
      "skos:note": "Attorney-General may revoke parole order or licence under certain conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-19au-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "19AU(1) Attorney-General may revoke parole order or licence",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 271,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Attorney-General may, by instrument in writing, revoke a\nparole order or licence at any time before the end of the parole\nperiod or licence period:\n\n(a) if the offender has, during that period, failed to comply with\na condition of the order or licence; or\n\n(b) if there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that the\noffender has, during that period, so failed to comply;\nand the instrument of revocation must specify the condition that\nwas breached or is suspected of having been breached."
    },
    {
