    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19av-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "19AV(2) Arrest of person whose parole order or licence revoked by",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-19av-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.272",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The Attorney-General or the Director of Public Prosecutions may,\nin relation to a person whose parole order or licence has been\nrevoked by the Attorney-General, apply to a prescribed authority\nfor a warrant in the form prescribed for the purposes of this\nsubsection for the arrest of the person.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The Attorney-General or the Director of Public Prosecutions may,\nin relation to a person whose parole order or licence has been\nrevoked by the Attorney-General, apply to a prescribed authority\nfor a warrant in the form prescribed for the purposes of this\nsubsection for the arrest of the person.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19av"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19av-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19av-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19av-ss-2-logic-deontic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "13778c8a83a68c1584e5ecb1551c5f170b9f55474c5ce09c4ad1b5dad4f90722",
      "skos:note": "Authority must issue warrant for remand pending hearing completion. The Attorney-General or Director of Public Prosecutions may apply for a warrant to arrest a person whose parole order or licence has been revoked."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-19av-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "19AV(2) Arrest of person whose parole order or licence revoked by",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 272,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The Attorney-General or the Director of Public Prosecutions may,\nin relation to a person whose parole order or licence has been\nrevoked by the Attorney-General, apply to a prescribed authority\nfor a warrant in the form prescribed for the purposes of this\nsubsection for the arrest of the person."
    },
