      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19av-ss-3-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "exemption",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Authority exempt from fixing non-parole period due to serious breach.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a) the prescribed authority considers it inappropriate to do so because of the serious nature of the breach...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The authority is not required to fix a non-parole period under paragraph (1)(f)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19av-ss-3-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "permission",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Authority permitted to deviate from non-parole period requirement.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(b) the unserved part of the outstanding sentence or sentences is, nor aggregates, 3 months or less.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The authority may fix a non-parole period under paragraph (1)(f) if it is 3 months or less."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19av-ss-3-logic-alleninterval-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "overlap",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Non-parole period may overlap with other sentence periods.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(b) the unserved part of the outstanding sentence or sentences is, nor aggregates, 3 months or less.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The non-parole period may overlap with other sentence periods if it is 3 months or less."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19av-ss-3-logic-ltl-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LTL"
      },
      "cml:operator": "trace",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Non-parole period requirement applies to certain breaches.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::temporal_ltl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(3) The prescribed authority is not required to fix a non-parole period under paragraph (1)(f).",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The non-parole period requirement only applies to serious breaches."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19av-ss-3-logic-deontic-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to be brought before a prescribed authority.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19av-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "19AV(1) Arrest of person whose parole order or licence revoked by",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-19av-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.272",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where a prescribed authority before whom a person is brought\nunder section 19AV because of an order revoking a parole order or\nlicence is satisfied:\n\n(a) that the person is the person named in that revocation order;\nand\n\n(b) that the person was notified by the Attorney-General of the\nproposal to make the revocation order; and\n\n(c) that the revocation order is still in force;\n\n\nSentencing, imprisonment and release of federal offenders  Part IB\nConditional release on parole or licence  Division 5\n\nSection 19AW\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nthe prescribed authority must issue a warrant, in the prescribed\nform:\n\n(d) authorising any constable to take the person to a specified\nprison in the State or Territory in which the person was\narrested; and\n\n(e) directing that the person be detained in prison in that State or\nTerritory to undergo imprisonment for the unserved part of\nthe sentence, or of each sentence, of imprisonment (in this\nsection called the outstanding sentence or sentences) that\nthe person was serving or had yet to serve at the time of his\nor her release; and\n\n(f) subject to subsections (3) and (3A), fixing a non-parole\nperiod in respect of the outstanding sentence or sentences.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Where a prescribed authority before whom a person is brought\nunder section 19AV because of an order revoking a parole order or\nlicence is satisfied:\n\n(a) that the person is the person named in that revocation order;\nand\n\n(b) that the person was notified by the Attorney-General of the\nproposal to make the revocation order; and\n\n(c) that the revocation order is still in force;\n\n\nSentencing, imprisonment and release of federal offenders  Part IB\nConditional release on parole or licence  Division 5\n\nSection 19AW\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nthe prescribed authority must issue a warrant, in the prescribed\nform:\n\n(d) authorising any constable to take the person to a specified\nprison in the State or Territory in which the person was\narrested; and\n\n(e) directing that the person be detained in prison in that State or\nTerritory to undergo imprisonment for the unserved part of\nthe sentence, or of each sentence, of imprisonment (in this\nsection called the outstanding sentence or sentences) that\nthe person was serving or had yet to serve at the time of his\nor her release; and\n\n(f) subject to subsections (3) and (3A), fixing a non-parole\nperiod in respect of the outstanding sentence or sentences.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19av"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19av-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19av-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19av-ss-1-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19av-ss-1-logic-deontic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19av-ss-1-logic-deontic-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19av-ss-1-logic-linearlogic-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3f5569d348675100a8e6edf1b261c16970b954f727fd063a66a39757c166bb59",
      "skos:note": "Constable may arrest person whose parole order or licence revoked by Attorney-General. Authority must issue warrant for arrest and detention of person whose parole order or licence is revoked."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-19av-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "19AV(1) Arrest of person whose parole order or licence revoked by",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 272,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where a prescribed authority before whom a person is brought\nunder section 19AV because of an order revoking a parole order or\nlicence is satisfied:\n\n(a) that the person is the person named in that revocation order;\nand\n\n(b) that the person was notified by the Attorney-General of the\nproposal to make the revocation order; and\n\n(c) that the revocation order is still in force;\n\n\nSentencing, imprisonment and release of federal offenders  Part IB\nConditional release on parole or licence  Division 5\n\nSection 19AW\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nthe prescribed authority must issue a warrant, in the prescribed\nform:\n\n(d) authorising any constable to take the person to a specified\nprison in the State or Territory in which the person was\narrested; and\n\n(e) directing that the person be detained in prison in that State or\nTerritory to undergo imprisonment for the unserved part of\nthe sentence, or of each sentence, of imprisonment (in this\nsection called the outstanding sentence or sentences) that\nthe person was serving or had yet to serve at the time of his\nor her release; and\n\n(f) subject to subsections (3) and (3A), fixing a non-parole\nperiod in respect of the outstanding sentence or sentences."
    },
