    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19az",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "19AZ Evidence before prescribed authority",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-19az"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.277",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A prescribed authority exercising any powers under this Division\nmay take evidence on oath or affirmation and for that purpose may\nadminister an oath or affirmation.\n\n(2) A prescribed authority exercising any powers under this Division\nmay summon a person to appear before the prescribed authority to\ngive evidence and to produce such documents and articles (if any)\nas are referred to in the summons.\n\n(3) A summons under this section shall be served in the same manner\nas a summons to a witness to appear before a court of summary\njurisdiction in the State or Territory where the summons under this\nsection is issued.\n19AZA  Disobedience of summons etc.\n\n(1) A person who has been served with a summons to appear before a\nprescribed authority must not fail to appear in obedience to the\nsummons.\nPenalty: 10 penalty units.\n\n(2) A person who has been served with a summons to produce a\ndocument or article to a prescribed authority shall not fail to\nproduce the document or article.\nPenalty: 10 penalty units.\n\n(3) A person who appears before a prescribed authority shall not refuse\nto be sworn or make an affirmation or refuse to produce documents\nor articles, or to answer questions, that he or she is required by the\nprescribed authority to produce or answer.\nPenalty: 10 penalty units.\n\n(4) Subsections (1), (2) and (3) do not apply if the person has a\nreasonable excuse.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A prescribed authority exercising any powers under this Division\nmay take evidence on oath or affirmation and for that purpose may\nadminister an oath or affirmation.\n\n(2) A prescribed authority exercising any powers under this Division\nmay summon a person to appear before the prescribed authority to\ngive evidence and to produce such documents and articles (if any)\nas are referred to in the summons.\n\n(3) A summons under this section shall be served in the same manner\nas a summons to a witness to appear before a court of summary\njurisdiction in the State or Territory where the summons under this\nsection is issued.\n19AZA  Disobedience of summons etc.\n\n(1) A person who has been served with a summons to appear before a\nprescribed authority must not fail to appear in obedience to the\nsummons.\nPenalty: 10 penalty units.\n\n(2) A person who has been served with a summons to produce a\ndocument or article to a prescribed authority shall not fail to\nproduce the document or article.\nPenalty: 10 penalty units.\n\n(3) A person who appears before a prescribed authority shall not refuse\nto be sworn or make an affirmation or refuse to produce documents\nor articles, or to answer questions, that he or she is required by the\nprescribed authority to produce or answer.\nPenalty: 10 penalty units.\n\n(4) Subsections (1), (2) and (3) do not apply if the person has a\nreasonable excuse.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19az-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19az-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19az-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19az-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19az-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19az-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19az-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6160a94239c6737a210f72add956944657e37d88e32200f97a4d325db22b7518"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-19az",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "19AZ Evidence before prescribed authority",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 277,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A prescribed authority exercising any powers under this Division\nmay take evidence on oath or affirmation and for that purpose may\nadminister an oath or affirmation.\n\n(2) A prescribed authority exercising any powers under this Division\nmay summon a person to appear before the prescribed authority to\ngive evidence and to produce such documents and articles (if any)\nas are referred to in the summons.\n\n(3) A summons under this section shall be served in the same manner\nas a summons to a witness to appear before a court of summary\njurisdiction in the State or Territory where the summons under this\nsection is issued.\n19AZA  Disobedience of summons etc.\n\n(1) A person who has been served with a summons to appear before a\nprescribed authority must not fail to appear in obedience to the\nsummons.\nPenalty: 10 penalty units.\n\n(2) A person who has been served with a summons to produce a\ndocument or article to a prescribed authority shall not fail to\nproduce the document or article.\nPenalty: 10 penalty units.\n\n(3) A person who appears before a prescribed authority shall not refuse\nto be sworn or make an affirmation or refuse to produce documents\nor articles, or to answer questions, that he or she is required by the\nprescribed authority to produce or answer.\nPenalty: 10 penalty units.\n\n(4) Subsections (1), (2) and (3) do not apply if the person has a\nreasonable excuse."
    },
