    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "19B Discharge of offenders without proceeding to conviction",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-19b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.279",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where:\n\n(a) a person is charged before a court with a federal offence or\nfederal offences; and\n\n(b) the court is satisfied, in respect of that charge or more than\none of those charges, that the charge is proved, but is of the\nopinion, having regard to:\n\n(i) the character, antecedents, age, health or mental\ncondition of the person;\n\n(ii) the extent (if any) to which the offence is of a trivial\nnature; or\n\n(iii) the extent (if any) to which the offence was committed\nunder extenuating circumstances;\n\nthat it is inexpedient to inflict any punishment, or to inflict\nany punishment other than a nominal punishment, or that it is\nexpedient to release the offender on probation;\nthe court may, by order:\n\n(c) dismiss the charge or charges in respect of which the court is\nso satisfied; or\n\n(d) discharge the person, without proceeding to conviction in\nrespect of any charge referred to in paragraph (c), upon his or\nher giving security, with or without sureties, by recognizance",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Where:\n\n(a) a person is charged before a court with a federal offence or\nfederal offences; and\n\n(b) the court is satisfied, in respect of that charge or more than\none of those charges, that the charge is proved, but is of the\nopinion, having regard to:\n\n(i) the character, antecedents, age, health or mental\ncondition of the person;\n\n(ii) the extent (if any) to which the offence is of a trivial\nnature; or\n\n(iii) the extent (if any) to which the offence was committed\nunder extenuating circumstances;\n\nthat it is inexpedient to inflict any punishment, or to inflict\nany punishment other than a nominal punishment, or that it is\nexpedient to release the offender on probation;\nthe court may, by order:\n\n(c) dismiss the charge or charges in respect of which the court is\nso satisfied; or\n\n(d) discharge the person, without proceeding to conviction in\nrespect of any charge referred to in paragraph (c), upon his or\nher giving security, with or without sureties, by recognizance",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19b-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19b-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19b-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19b-logic-deontic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19b-logic-alleninterval-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19b-logic-ltl-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "28094c8a9b7ee5d46b8b2fe68e7b6e57e28e80ae15ca2776048c60f533e275bf",
      "skos:note": "Court may dismiss or discharge charges under certain conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-19b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "19B Discharge of offenders without proceeding to conviction",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 279,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where:\n\n(a) a person is charged before a court with a federal offence or\nfederal offences; and\n\n(b) the court is satisfied, in respect of that charge or more than\none of those charges, that the charge is proved, but is of the\nopinion, having regard to:\n\n(i) the character, antecedents, age, health or mental\ncondition of the person;\n\n(ii) the extent (if any) to which the offence is of a trivial\nnature; or\n\n(iii) the extent (if any) to which the offence was committed\nunder extenuating circumstances;\n\nthat it is inexpedient to inflict any punishment, or to inflict\nany punishment other than a nominal punishment, or that it is\nexpedient to release the offender on probation;\nthe court may, by order:\n\n(c) dismiss the charge or charges in respect of which the court is\nso satisfied; or\n\n(d) discharge the person, without proceeding to conviction in\nrespect of any charge referred to in paragraph (c), upon his or\nher giving security, with or without sureties, by recognizance"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-19b-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
