    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20aa-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20AA(4) Power to discharge or vary conditions of recognizance",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-20aa-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.290",
      "values:originalText": "(4) The court shall not extend the duration of a recognizance beyond:\n\n(a) in the case of a recognizance entered into in pursuance of an\norder made under subsection 19B(1)—the period of 3 years\nfrom the date on which the recognizance was entered into; or\n\n(b) in the case of a recognizance entered into in pursuance of an\norder made under subsection 20(1)—the period of 5 years\nfrom the date on which the recognizance was entered into.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) The court shall not extend the duration of a recognizance beyond:\n\n(a) in the case of a recognizance entered into in pursuance of an\norder made under subsection 19B(1)—the period of 3 years\nfrom the date on which the recognizance was entered into; or\n\n(b) in the case of a recognizance entered into in pursuance of an\norder made under subsection 20(1)—the period of 5 years\nfrom the date on which the recognizance was entered into.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20aa"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20aa-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20aa-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "220b2f8e35e0c68f4d3b686aadcb4f78fc3208590381567823db741f575bbd22",
      "skos:note": "Court cannot extend recognizance duration beyond specified periods."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-20aa-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20AA(4) Power to discharge or vary conditions of recognizance",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 290,
      "values:originalText": "(4) The court shall not extend the duration of a recognizance beyond:\n\n(a) in the case of a recognizance entered into in pursuance of an\norder made under subsection 19B(1)—the period of 3 years\nfrom the date on which the recognizance was entered into; or\n\n(b) in the case of a recognizance entered into in pursuance of an\norder made under subsection 20(1)—the period of 5 years\nfrom the date on which the recognizance was entered into."
    },
