    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20aa-ss-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20AA(6) Power to discharge or vary conditions of recognizance",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-20aa-ss-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.290",
      "values:originalText": "(6) Where an application is made under subsection (1) by a person\nother than an authorized person, the person making the application\nshall cause notice of the application, and of the date, time and place\nfixed for the hearing of the application, to be served on the\nDirector of Public Prosecutions or, if the Director of Public\nProsecutions has not established an office in the State or Territory\nin which the application is made, on the Director of Legal Services,\nin that State or Territory, in the Attorney-General’s Department,\nand:\n\n(a) if the application is made by the person who entered into the\nrecognizance and that person has a surety—on the surety;\n\n(b) if the application is made by a surety in respect of the\nrecognizance—on the person who entered into the\nrecognizance; or\n\n(c) if the application is made by a probation officer in respect of\nthe recognizance—on the person who entered into the",
      "skos:definition": "(6) Where an application is made under subsection (1) by a person\nother than an authorized person, the person making the application\nshall cause notice of the application, and of the date, time and place\nfixed for the hearing of the application, to be served on the\nDirector of Public Prosecutions or, if the Director of Public\nProsecutions has not established an office in the State or Territory\nin which the application is made, on the Director of Legal Services,\nin that State or Territory, in the Attorney-General’s Department,\nand:\n\n(a) if the application is made by the person who entered into the\nrecognizance and that person has a surety—on the surety;\n\n(b) if the application is made by a surety in respect of the\nrecognizance—on the person who entered into the\nrecognizance; or\n\n(c) if the application is made by a probation officer in respect of\nthe recognizance—on the person who entered into the",
      "values:partOf": {
