      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.300",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where, in proceedings for the commitment of a person for trial of a\nfederal offence on indictment, being proceedings begun after this\nsection commences, the question of the person’s fitness to be tried\nin respect of the offence, is raised by the prosecution, the person or\nthe person’s legal representative, the magistrate must refer the\nproceedings to the court to which the proceedings would have been\nreferred had the person been committed for trial.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Where, in proceedings for the commitment of a person for trial of a\nfederal offence on indictment, being proceedings begun after this\nsection commences, the question of the person’s fitness to be tried\nin respect of the offence, is raised by the prosecution, the person or\nthe person’s legal representative, the magistrate must refer the\nproceedings to the court to which the proceedings would have been\nreferred had the person been committed for trial.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b1d3e8e030389bf7af3f5a19d5818f5b6d40305a09488011f45c93c9a29cd8c2",
      "skos:note": "Must refer proceedings to court if person's fitness is raised"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-20b-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20B(1) Consequences of preliminary finding that person unfit to be",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 300,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where, in proceedings for the commitment of a person for trial of a\nfederal offence on indictment, being proceedings begun after this\nsection commences, the question of the person’s fitness to be tried\nin respect of the offence, is raised by the prosecution, the person or\nthe person’s legal representative, the magistrate must refer the\nproceedings to the court to which the proceedings would have been\nreferred had the person been committed for trial."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b-ss-1-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b-ss-1"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b-ss-1-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Must refer proceedings to court",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The magistrate must refer the proceedings.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "to the court."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20B(2) Consequences of preliminary finding that person unfit to be",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-20b-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.300",
      "values:originalText": "(2) If the court to which the proceedings have been referred finds the\nperson charged to be fit to be tried, the court must remit the\nproceedings to the magistrate and proceedings for the commitment\nmust be continued as soon as practicable.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) If the court to which the proceedings have been referred finds the\nperson charged to be fit to be tried, the court must remit the\nproceedings to the magistrate and proceedings for the commitment\nmust be continued as soon as practicable.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b-ss-2-logic-linearlogic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b-ss-2-logic-alleninterval-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b-ss-2-logic-argumentation-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b-ss-2-logic-diffusion-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "552a81d45ff4cda69f6a3e509ec77333de3d182e48f89fe26fcde3ef1a6e6164",
      "skos:note": "Court must remit proceedings to magistrate if person is deemed fit for trial."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-20b-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20B(2) Consequences of preliminary finding that person unfit to be",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 300,
      "values:originalText": "(2) If the court to which the proceedings have been referred finds the\nperson charged to be fit to be tried, the court must remit the\nproceedings to the magistrate and proceedings for the commitment\nmust be continued as soon as practicable."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b-ss-2"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b-ss-2-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Court obligation to remit proceedings",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Court has jurisdiction over the case",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Proceedings must be remitted to magistrate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b-ss-2-logic-linearlogic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LinearLogic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "⇒",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Court obligation implies remittal",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::linear",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "If the person is deemed fit for trial, then the court must remit proceedings",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The court's obligation to remit proceedings follows from the fact that the person is deemed fit for trial"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b-ss-2-logic-alleninterval-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "BETWEEN",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Remittal occurs between the court and the magistrate",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The court has jurisdiction over the case, but must remit proceedings to the magistrate",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The remittal of proceedings occurs between these two entities"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b-ss-2-logic-argumentation-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Argumentation"
      },
      "cml:operator": "⇒",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Remittal is a response to the person's fitness for trial",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::argumentation",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "If the person is deemed fit for trial, then the court must remit proceedings as a response",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The court's obligation to remit proceedings follows from the fact that the person is deemed fit for trial and the need to respond accordingly"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b-ss-2-logic-diffusion-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Diffusion"
      },
      "cml:operator": "⇒",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Remittal spreads to other courts and authorities",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::diffusion",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The court's obligation to remit proceedings implies that this action will be taken by other courts and authorities",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The remittal of proceedings has implications for the actions of other courts and authorities"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20B(3) Consequences of preliminary finding that person unfit to be",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-20b-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.300",
      "values:originalText": "(3) Where a court:\n\n(a) to which proceedings have been referred under\nsubsection (1); or\n\n(b) before which a person appears in proceedings for trial of a\nfederal offence on indictment, being proceedings begun after\nthis section commences;\nfinds the person charged unfit to be tried, the court must determine\nwhether there has been established a prima facie case that the\nperson committed the offence concerned.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) Where a court:\n\n(a) to which proceedings have been referred under\nsubsection (1); or\n\n(b) before which a person appears in proceedings for trial of a\nfederal offence on indictment, being proceedings begun after\nthis section commences;\nfinds the person charged unfit to be tried, the court must determine\nwhether there has been established a prima facie case that the\nperson committed the offence concerned.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c04ccddd706f75da73a99b7e145b5c1a2c765d8501098b5fc1ef7a98ed0ef757",
      "skos:note": "Court must determine if prima facie case has been established for unfit person to be tried."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-20b-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20B(3) Consequences of preliminary finding that person unfit to be",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 300,
      "values:originalText": "(3) Where a court:\n\n(a) to which proceedings have been referred under\nsubsection (1); or\n\n(b) before which a person appears in proceedings for trial of a\nfederal offence on indictment, being proceedings begun after\nthis section commences;\nfinds the person charged unfit to be tried, the court must determine\nwhether there has been established a prima facie case that the\nperson committed the offence concerned."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b-ss-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b-ss-3"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b-ss-3-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Court obligation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Court must determine",
      "cml:conclusionText": "if prima facie case has been established"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20B(4) Consequences of preliminary finding that person unfit to be",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-20b-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.300",
      "values:originalText": "(4) Where a magistrate refers proceedings to a court under\nsubsection (1), the magistrate may order the person charged to be\ndetained in prison or in hospital for so long only as is reasonably\nnecessary to allow the court to which the person is referred to\ndetermine whether it will make an order under subsection (2)\nremitting the person to the magistrate, an order under section 20BA\ndismissing the charge or an order under section 20BB detaining the\nperson in prison or hospital or granting the person bail.\n\n\nSentencing, imprisonment and release of federal offenders  Part IB\nUnfitness to be tried  Division 6\n\nSection 20BA\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(4) Where a magistrate refers proceedings to a court under\nsubsection (1), the magistrate may order the person charged to be\ndetained in prison or in hospital for so long only as is reasonably\nnecessary to allow the court to which the person is referred to\ndetermine whether it will make an order under subsection (2)\nremitting the person to the magistrate, an order under section 20BA\ndismissing the charge or an order under section 20BB detaining the\nperson in prison or hospital or granting the person bail.\n\n\nSentencing, imprisonment and release of federal offenders  Part IB\nUnfitness to be tried  Division 6\n\nSection 20BA\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "27f7612e3e0ff200305fa71fd4b927cc6530d366554b5caadd24e5a0effd0b5c",
      "skos:note": "Magistrate may order detention in prison or hospital for a reasonable period."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-20b-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20B(4) Consequences of preliminary finding that person unfit to be",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 300,
      "values:originalText": "(4) Where a magistrate refers proceedings to a court under\nsubsection (1), the magistrate may order the person charged to be\ndetained in prison or in hospital for so long only as is reasonably\nnecessary to allow the court to which the person is referred to\ndetermine whether it will make an order under subsection (2)\nremitting the person to the magistrate, an order under section 20BA\ndismissing the charge or an order under section 20BB detaining the\nperson in prison or hospital or granting the person bail.\n\n\nSentencing, imprisonment and release of federal offenders  Part IB\nUnfitness to be tried  Division 6\n\nSection 20BA\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b-ss-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b-ss-4"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b-ss-4-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "may",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Magistrate may order detention.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20B(5) Consequences of preliminary finding that person unfit to be",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-20b-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.300",
      "values:originalText": "(5) Where a court finds a person, other than a person in respect of\nwhom proceedings have been referred to it by a magistrate under\nsubsection (1), to be unfit to be tried, the court may order the\nperson to be detained in prison or hospital for so long only as is\nreasonably necessary to allow the court to determine whether it\nwill make an order under section 20BA dismissing the charge or an\norder under section 20BB detaining the person in prison or hospital\nor granting the person bail.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) Where a court finds a person, other than a person in respect of\nwhom proceedings have been referred to it by a magistrate under\nsubsection (1), to be unfit to be tried, the court may order the\nperson to be detained in prison or hospital for so long only as is\nreasonably necessary to allow the court to determine whether it\nwill make an order under section 20BA dismissing the charge or an\norder under section 20BB detaining the person in prison or hospital\nor granting the person bail.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4f2d88a6c39431b824ef4f344d7f32abe351b1a88535bb760da9ff1b8b98df94",
      "skos:note": "Court may order detention for a person unfit to be tried."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-20b-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20B(5) Consequences of preliminary finding that person unfit to be",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 300,
      "values:originalText": "(5) Where a court finds a person, other than a person in respect of\nwhom proceedings have been referred to it by a magistrate under\nsubsection (1), to be unfit to be tried, the court may order the\nperson to be detained in prison or hospital for so long only as is\nreasonably necessary to allow the court to determine whether it\nwill make an order under section 20BA dismissing the charge or an\norder under section 20BB detaining the person in prison or hospital\nor granting the person bail."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b-ss-5-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
