      "cml:conclusionText": "Duty to put person on trial"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b-ss-7",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20B(7) Consequences of preliminary finding that person unfit to be",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-20b-ss-7"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.300",
      "values:originalText": "(7) In proceedings to determine whether, for the purposes of\nsubsection (3), a prima facie case has been established:\n\n(a) the person may give evidence or make an unsworn statement;\nand\n\n(b) the person may raise any defence that could properly be\nraised if the proceedings were a trial for that offence; and\n\n(c) the court may seek such other evidence, whether oral or in\nwriting, as it considers likely to assist in determining the\nmatter.",
      "skos:definition": "(7) In proceedings to determine whether, for the purposes of\nsubsection (3), a prima facie case has been established:\n\n(a) the person may give evidence or make an unsworn statement;\nand\n\n(b) the person may raise any defence that could properly be\nraised if the proceedings were a trial for that offence; and\n\n(c) the court may seek such other evidence, whether oral or in\nwriting, as it considers likely to assist in determining the\nmatter.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b-ss-7-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b-ss-7-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "98f224fc7383643e13950a5c50e988a49fb2b0f962fc2defdb9a127d997bf1de",
      "skos:note": "Person may give evidence or make an unsworn statement in proceedings."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-20b-ss-7",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20B(7) Consequences of preliminary finding that person unfit to be",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 300,
      "values:originalText": "(7) In proceedings to determine whether, for the purposes of\nsubsection (3), a prima facie case has been established:\n\n(a) the person may give evidence or make an unsworn statement;\nand\n\n(b) the person may raise any defence that could properly be\nraised if the proceedings were a trial for that offence; and\n\n(c) the court may seek such other evidence, whether oral or in\nwriting, as it considers likely to assist in determining the\nmatter."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b-ss-7-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20b-ss-7"
      },
