    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bd",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20BD Review by Attorney-General",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-20bd"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.306",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where a court makes an order under subsection 20BC(2), the\nAttorney-General must, at least once in each period of 6 months\nafter the day the person is detained under the order, consider\nwhether or not the person should be released from detention.\n\n(2) In considering whether the person should be released from\ndetention the Attorney-General:\n\n(a) must obtain and consider:\n\n(i) a report from a duly qualified psychiatrist or\npsychologist; and\n\n\nSentencing, imprisonment and release of federal offenders  Part IB\nUnfitness to be tried  Division 6\n\nSection 20BE\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(ii) a report from another duly qualified medical\npractitioner; and\n\n(b) may obtain and consider such other reports as the\nAttorney-General considers necessary; and\n\n(c) must take into account any representations made to the\nAttorney-General by the person or on the person’s behalf.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Where a court makes an order under subsection 20BC(2), the\nAttorney-General must, at least once in each period of 6 months\nafter the day the person is detained under the order, consider\nwhether or not the person should be released from detention.\n\n(2) In considering whether the person should be released from\ndetention the Attorney-General:\n\n(a) must obtain and consider:\n\n(i) a report from a duly qualified psychiatrist or\npsychologist; and\n\n\nSentencing, imprisonment and release of federal offenders  Part IB\nUnfitness to be tried  Division 6\n\nSection 20BE\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(ii) a report from another duly qualified medical\npractitioner; and\n\n(b) may obtain and consider such other reports as the\nAttorney-General considers necessary; and\n\n(c) must take into account any representations made to the\nAttorney-General by the person or on the person’s behalf.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bd-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bd-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cb4394417fb78914b6ab4bac79c61410a3b507703edb56802eebc74faf69c890"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-20bd",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20BD Review by Attorney-General",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 306,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where a court makes an order under subsection 20BC(2), the\nAttorney-General must, at least once in each period of 6 months\nafter the day the person is detained under the order, consider\nwhether or not the person should be released from detention.\n\n(2) In considering whether the person should be released from\ndetention the Attorney-General:\n\n(a) must obtain and consider:\n\n(i) a report from a duly qualified psychiatrist or\npsychologist; and\n\n\nSentencing, imprisonment and release of federal offenders  Part IB\nUnfitness to be tried  Division 6\n\nSection 20BE\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(ii) a report from another duly qualified medical\npractitioner; and\n\n(b) may obtain and consider such other reports as the\nAttorney-General considers necessary; and\n\n(c) must take into account any representations made to the\nAttorney-General by the person or on the person’s behalf."
    },
