      "values:originalText": "(2) In considering whether the person should be released from\ndetention the Attorney-General:\n\n(a) must obtain and consider:\n\n(i) a report from a duly qualified psychiatrist or\npsychologist; and\n\n\nSentencing, imprisonment and release of federal offenders  Part IB\nUnfitness to be tried  Division 6\n\nSection 20BE\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(ii) a report from another duly qualified medical\npractitioner; and\n\n(b) may obtain and consider such other reports as the\nAttorney-General considers necessary; and\n\n(c) must take into account any representations made to the\nAttorney-General by the person or on the person’s behalf.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) In considering whether the person should be released from\ndetention the Attorney-General:\n\n(a) must obtain and consider:\n\n(i) a report from a duly qualified psychiatrist or\npsychologist; and\n\n\nSentencing, imprisonment and release of federal offenders  Part IB\nUnfitness to be tried  Division 6\n\nSection 20BE\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(ii) a report from another duly qualified medical\npractitioner; and\n\n(b) may obtain and consider such other reports as the\nAttorney-General considers necessary; and\n\n(c) must take into account any representations made to the\nAttorney-General by the person or on the person’s behalf.",
