    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bd-ss-2-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Attorney-General has an obligation to consider reports from psychiatrists and psychologists.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The Attorney-General is responsible for making decisions about the release of federal offenders.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The Attorney-General must obtain and consider reports from psychiatrists and psychologists."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bd-ss-2-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Attorney-General has an obligation to take into account representations made by the person or on their behalf.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The Attorney-General is responsible for making decisions about the release of federal offenders.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The Attorney-General must take into account any representations made to the Attorney-General by the person or on the person's behalf."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bd-ss-2-logic-deontic-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MAY",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Attorney-General may obtain and consider additional reports as necessary.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The Attorney-General is responsible for making decisions about the release of federal offenders.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The Attorney-General may obtain and consider such other reports as the Attorney-General considers necessary."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bd-ss-2-logic-epistemic-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Epistemic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "OUGHT_TO",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Attorney-General ought to consider reports from psychiatrists and psychologists based on their expertise.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::epistemic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The Attorney-General is responsible for making decisions about the release of federal offenders.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The Attorney-General ought to obtain and consider a report from a duly qualified psychiatrist or psychologist."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bd-ss-2-logic-ltl-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LTL"
      },
      "cml:operator": "AT",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Attorney-General must take into account representations made by the person or on their behalf within a certain timeframe.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::temporal_ltl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The Attorney-General is responsible for making decisions about the release of federal offenders.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The Attorney-General must take into account any representations made to the Attorney-General by the person or on the person's behalf at some point in time."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20be",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20BE Attorney-General may order release",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-20be"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.307",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Attorney-General may, after considering under\nsubsection 20BD(1) whether or not the person should be released\nfrom detention, order that the person be released from detention.\n\n(2) The Attorney-General must not order a person’s release from\ndetention unless the Attorney-General is satisfied that the person is\nnot a threat or danger either to himself or herself or to the\ncommunity.\n\n(3) An order:\n\n(a) must be in writing; and\n\n(b) remains in force for such period as is specified in the order\n(being a period equal to the balance of the period fixed by the\ncourt for detention under subsection 20BC(2)) or for a period\nof 5 years, whichever is the lesser; and\n\n(c) is subject to such conditions (if any) as are specified in the\norder.\n\n(4) Without limiting the generality of paragraph (3)(c), the conditions\nthat may be specified in the order may include all or any of the\nfollowing:\n\n(a) a condition that the person reside at an address specified in\nthe order;\n\n(b) a condition that the person present himself or herself for such\nmedical or psychiatric treatment as is specified in the order at\nsuch times as are specified in the order;\n\n(c) a condition that the person undertake such medical or mental\nhealth therapy as is specified in the order;",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Attorney-General may, after considering under\nsubsection 20BD(1) whether or not the person should be released\nfrom detention, order that the person be released from detention.\n\n(2) The Attorney-General must not order a person’s release from\ndetention unless the Attorney-General is satisfied that the person is\nnot a threat or danger either to himself or herself or to the\ncommunity.\n\n(3) An order:\n\n(a) must be in writing; and\n\n(b) remains in force for such period as is specified in the order\n(being a period equal to the balance of the period fixed by the\ncourt for detention under subsection 20BC(2)) or for a period\nof 5 years, whichever is the lesser; and\n\n(c) is subject to such conditions (if any) as are specified in the\norder.\n\n(4) Without limiting the generality of paragraph (3)(c), the conditions\nthat may be specified in the order may include all or any of the\nfollowing:\n\n(a) a condition that the person reside at an address specified in\nthe order;\n\n(b) a condition that the person present himself or herself for such\nmedical or psychiatric treatment as is specified in the order at\nsuch times as are specified in the order;\n\n(c) a condition that the person undertake such medical or mental\nhealth therapy as is specified in the order;",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20be-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20be-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20be-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20be-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c5e6b3638d36ec3f7c1d4ae71d2aa62feabc923f98b7a91e45cbec11958ccfa7"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-20be",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20BE Attorney-General may order release",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 307,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Attorney-General may, after considering under\nsubsection 20BD(1) whether or not the person should be released\nfrom detention, order that the person be released from detention.\n\n(2) The Attorney-General must not order a person’s release from\ndetention unless the Attorney-General is satisfied that the person is\nnot a threat or danger either to himself or herself or to the\ncommunity.\n\n(3) An order:\n\n(a) must be in writing; and\n\n(b) remains in force for such period as is specified in the order\n(being a period equal to the balance of the period fixed by the\ncourt for detention under subsection 20BC(2)) or for a period\nof 5 years, whichever is the lesser; and\n\n(c) is subject to such conditions (if any) as are specified in the\norder.\n\n(4) Without limiting the generality of paragraph (3)(c), the conditions\nthat may be specified in the order may include all or any of the\nfollowing:\n\n(a) a condition that the person reside at an address specified in\nthe order;\n\n(b) a condition that the person present himself or herself for such\nmedical or psychiatric treatment as is specified in the order at\nsuch times as are specified in the order;\n\n(c) a condition that the person undertake such medical or mental\nhealth therapy as is specified in the order;"
    },
