      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bf-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bf-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "55590bf0e1e88b78ec771d0c83733dc218f53d786cd7c228af3dcb2584f96d71",
      "skos:note": "Revocation of release order"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-20bf-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20BF(1) Release order may be revoked",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 308,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Attorney-General may, by instrument in writing, revoke an\norder made under subsection 20BE(1) (in this section called a\nrelease order) at any time while that release order remains in force:\n\n(a) if the person concerned has, during that period, failed,\nwithout reasonable excuse, to comply with a condition of the\norder; or\n\n(b) if there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that the person\nhas, during that period, failed, without reasonable excuse, so\nto comply;\nand, where the Attorney-General does so, the instrument of\nrevocation must specify the condition of the order that the person\nhas breached or is suspected of having breached."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bf-ss-1-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bf-ss-1"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bf-ss-1-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibition",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits revocation of release order",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bf-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20BF(2) Release order may be revoked",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-20bf-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.308",
      "values:originalText": "(2) Before revoking a release order, the Attorney-General must make\nall such enquiries and call for all such reports as are reasonably\nnecessary for the purpose of determining whether the\ncircumstances referred to in paragraph (1)(a) or (b) apply.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) Before revoking a release order, the Attorney-General must make\nall such enquiries and call for all such reports as are reasonably\nnecessary for the purpose of determining whether the\ncircumstances referred to in paragraph (1)(a) or (b) apply.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bf"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bf-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bf-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "99a05cac72ebc7fbe2e45a238dd7f4c2f774f240da8fa0dc12b42e0b2bf40965",
      "skos:note": "Attorney-General must make enquiries before revoking a release order."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-20bf-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20BF(2) Release order may be revoked",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 308,
      "values:originalText": "(2) Before revoking a release order, the Attorney-General must make\nall such enquiries and call for all such reports as are reasonably\nnecessary for the purpose of determining whether the\ncircumstances referred to in paragraph (1)(a) or (b) apply."
    },
    {
