    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bf-ss-8",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20BF(8) Release order may be revoked",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-20bf-ss-8"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.308",
      "values:originalText": "(8) Where for urgent medical or security reasons it becomes necessary\nto do so, an officer of the State or Territory in which a person is\ndetained may vary the prison or hospital at which the person is\ndetained but, where the officer does so, the officer must forthwith\nnotify the Attorney-General, in writing, of the variation and of the\nreasons for that variation.",
      "skos:definition": "(8) Where for urgent medical or security reasons it becomes necessary\nto do so, an officer of the State or Territory in which a person is\ndetained may vary the prison or hospital at which the person is\ndetained but, where the officer does so, the officer must forthwith\nnotify the Attorney-General, in writing, of the variation and of the\nreasons for that variation.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bf"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bf-ss-8-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bf-ss-8-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6dcc3698d0df9f9eab771f95be9306ac1c5c903194e1cb1f3095ab179b335742",
      "skos:note": "Notify Attorney-General of variation in detention facility",
      "dc:description": "Reasons for variation"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-20bf-ss-8",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20BF(8) Release order may be revoked",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 308,
      "values:originalText": "(8) Where for urgent medical or security reasons it becomes necessary\nto do so, an officer of the State or Territory in which a person is\ndetained may vary the prison or hospital at which the person is\ndetained but, where the officer does so, the officer must forthwith\nnotify the Attorney-General, in writing, of the variation and of the\nreasons for that variation."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bf-ss-8-norm",
