      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bg",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20BG Attorney-General to review detention of persons taken back",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-20bg"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.310",
      "values:originalText": "into detention\n\n(1) Where, under subsection 20BF(5), a prescribed authority directs\nthat a person be detained in prison or in a hospital, the\nAttorney-General must, as soon as practicable after the person is so\ndetained, consider (in this section called the initial consideration)\nwhether or not the person should be released from detention and\nmust, while the person is in detention, reconsider the matter at least\nonce in each period of 6 months after the initial consideration.\n\n(2) Subsection 20BD(2) and, subject to the modification set out in\nsubsection (3), section 20BE, apply in relation to an initial\nconsideration and to any reconsideration under subsection (1).\n\n(3) For the purposes of applying section 20BE, subsection 20BE(1)\nhas effect as if the reference in that subsection to\nsubsection 20BD(1) were a reference to subsection (1) of this\nsection.",
      "skos:definition": "into detention\n\n(1) Where, under subsection 20BF(5), a prescribed authority directs\nthat a person be detained in prison or in a hospital, the\nAttorney-General must, as soon as practicable after the person is so\ndetained, consider (in this section called the initial consideration)\nwhether or not the person should be released from detention and\nmust, while the person is in detention, reconsider the matter at least\nonce in each period of 6 months after the initial consideration.\n\n(2) Subsection 20BD(2) and, subject to the modification set out in\nsubsection (3), section 20BE, apply in relation to an initial\nconsideration and to any reconsideration under subsection (1).\n\n(3) For the purposes of applying section 20BE, subsection 20BE(1)\nhas effect as if the reference in that subsection to\nsubsection 20BD(1) were a reference to subsection (1) of this\nsection.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bg-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bg-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bg-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a658a29dc855dbdb0bd5b4caadf61ab5d69b461969fd7bc195b5f3632543ed44"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-20bg",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20BG Attorney-General to review detention of persons taken back",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 310,
      "values:originalText": "into detention\n\n(1) Where, under subsection 20BF(5), a prescribed authority directs\nthat a person be detained in prison or in a hospital, the\nAttorney-General must, as soon as practicable after the person is so\ndetained, consider (in this section called the initial consideration)\nwhether or not the person should be released from detention and\nmust, while the person is in detention, reconsider the matter at least\nonce in each period of 6 months after the initial consideration.\n\n(2) Subsection 20BD(2) and, subject to the modification set out in\nsubsection (3), section 20BE, apply in relation to an initial\nconsideration and to any reconsideration under subsection (1).\n\n(3) For the purposes of applying section 20BE, subsection 20BE(1)\nhas effect as if the reference in that subsection to\nsubsection 20BD(1) were a reference to subsection (1) of this\nsection."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bg-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20BG(1) Attorney-General to review detention of persons taken back",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-20bg-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.310",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where, under subsection 20BF(5), a prescribed authority directs\nthat a person be detained in prison or in a hospital, the\nAttorney-General must, as soon as practicable after the person is so\ndetained, consider (in this section called the initial consideration)\nwhether or not the person should be released from detention and\nmust, while the person is in detention, reconsider the matter at least\nonce in each period of 6 months after the initial consideration.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Where, under subsection 20BF(5), a prescribed authority directs\nthat a person be detained in prison or in a hospital, the\nAttorney-General must, as soon as practicable after the person is so\ndetained, consider (in this section called the initial consideration)\nwhether or not the person should be released from detention and\nmust, while the person is in detention, reconsider the matter at least\nonce in each period of 6 months after the initial consideration.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bg"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
