          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bi-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bi-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d9c8b455dae9fe109559b1103af8bc3b35b6edd95fe089014f10572cadb0f1d7",
      "skos:note": "Right to appeal against unfitness to be tried"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-20bi-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20BI(1) Appeals against some Victorian jury findings of unfitness to be",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 310,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if:\n\n(a) in proceedings for a federal offence in the Trial Division of\nthe Supreme Court of Victoria or in the County Court of\nVictoria, a question arises whether the accused is fit to stand\ntrial; and\n\n\nSentencing, imprisonment and release of federal offenders  Part IB\nUnfitness to be tried  Division 6\n\nSection 20BI\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) a jury finds that the accused is unfit.\nRight to appeal"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bi-ss-1-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bi-ss-1"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bi-ss-1-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to appeal",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(1) This section applies if...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...a jury finds that the accused is unfit."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bi-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20BI(2) Appeals against some Victorian jury findings of unfitness to be",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-20bi-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.310",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The accused may appeal to the Court of Appeal of Victoria against\nthe finding:\n\n(a) on a ground involving only one or more questions of law\nalone; or\n\n(b) on a ground involving one or more questions of fact alone, or\none or more questions of mixed law and fact, if the judge\nbefore whom the accused came for trial certifies the ground\nis fit for appeal; or\n\n(c) on any ground if the Court of Appeal gives leave.\nDecision on appeal",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The accused may appeal to the Court of Appeal of Victoria against\nthe finding:\n\n(a) on a ground involving only one or more questions of law\nalone; or\n\n(b) on a ground involving one or more questions of fact alone, or\none or more questions of mixed law and fact, if the judge\nbefore whom the accused came for trial certifies the ground\nis fit for appeal; or\n\n(c) on any ground if the Court of Appeal gives leave.\nDecision on appeal",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bi"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bi-ss-2-norm"
        },
