    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bj-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20BJ(5) Acquittal where person mentally ill",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-20bj-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.313",
      "values:originalText": "(5) The conditions may include:\n\n(a) a condition that the person remain in the care of a responsible\nperson nominated in the order; and\n\n(b) a condition that the person attend upon a person nominated,\nor at a place specified, in the order for assessment of the\nperson’s mental illness, mental condition or intellectual\ndisability and, where appropriate, for treatment.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) The conditions may include:\n\n(a) a condition that the person remain in the care of a responsible\nperson nominated in the order; and\n\n(b) a condition that the person attend upon a person nominated,\nor at a place specified, in the order for assessment of the\nperson’s mental illness, mental condition or intellectual\ndisability and, where appropriate, for treatment.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bj"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bj-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bj-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f954eaade5d1cc1698d4a33edb5fb0baea5dc00f640e8a4b8ce520774619a1ca",
      "skos:note": "Condition for acquittal where person mentally ill"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-20bj-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20BJ(5) Acquittal where person mentally ill",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 313,
      "values:originalText": "(5) The conditions may include:\n\n(a) a condition that the person remain in the care of a responsible\nperson nominated in the order; and\n\n(b) a condition that the person attend upon a person nominated,\nor at a place specified, in the order for assessment of the\nperson’s mental illness, mental condition or intellectual\ndisability and, where appropriate, for treatment."
    },
