      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The conditions may include:"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bk",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20BK Review by Attorney-General",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-20bk"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.314",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where, under subsection 20BJ(1), a court orders that a person be\ndetained in safe custody in prison or in a hospital, the\nAttorney-General must, as soon as practicable after the person is so\ndetained, consider (in this section called the initial consideration)\nwhether or not the person should be released from detention and\nmust, while the person is in detention, reconsider the matter at least\nonce in each period of 6 months after the initial consideration.\n\n(2) In considering whether a person should be released from custody\nthe Attorney-General:\n\n(a) must obtain and consider:\n\n(i) a report from a duly qualified psychiatrist or\npsychologist; and\n\n(ii) a report from another duly qualified medical\npractitioner; and\n\n(b) may obtain and consider such other reports as the\nAttorney-General considers necessary; and\n\n(c) must take into account any representations made to the\nAttorney-General by the person or on the person’s behalf.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Where, under subsection 20BJ(1), a court orders that a person be\ndetained in safe custody in prison or in a hospital, the\nAttorney-General must, as soon as practicable after the person is so\ndetained, consider (in this section called the initial consideration)\nwhether or not the person should be released from detention and\nmust, while the person is in detention, reconsider the matter at least\nonce in each period of 6 months after the initial consideration.\n\n(2) In considering whether a person should be released from custody\nthe Attorney-General:\n\n(a) must obtain and consider:\n\n(i) a report from a duly qualified psychiatrist or\npsychologist; and\n\n(ii) a report from another duly qualified medical\npractitioner; and\n\n(b) may obtain and consider such other reports as the\nAttorney-General considers necessary; and\n\n(c) must take into account any representations made to the\nAttorney-General by the person or on the person’s behalf.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bk-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bk-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b13769cb3bf4451f8bac6b4f164c8278c97cb185f4367d091ddfe08bc6c7277a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-20bk",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20BK Review by Attorney-General",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 314,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where, under subsection 20BJ(1), a court orders that a person be\ndetained in safe custody in prison or in a hospital, the\nAttorney-General must, as soon as practicable after the person is so\ndetained, consider (in this section called the initial consideration)\nwhether or not the person should be released from detention and\nmust, while the person is in detention, reconsider the matter at least\nonce in each period of 6 months after the initial consideration.\n\n(2) In considering whether a person should be released from custody\nthe Attorney-General:\n\n(a) must obtain and consider:\n\n(i) a report from a duly qualified psychiatrist or\npsychologist; and\n\n(ii) a report from another duly qualified medical\npractitioner; and\n\n(b) may obtain and consider such other reports as the\nAttorney-General considers necessary; and\n\n(c) must take into account any representations made to the\nAttorney-General by the person or on the person’s behalf."
    },
