    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bm",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20BM Release order may be revoked",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-20bm"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.315",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Attorney-General may, by instrument in writing, revoke an\norder made under subsection 20BL(1) (in this section called a\nrelease order) at any time while that release order remains in force:\n\n(a) if the person concerned has, during that period, failed,\nwithout reasonable excuse, to comply with a condition of the\norder; or\n\n(b) if there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that the person\nhas, during that period, failed, without reasonable excuse, so\nto comply;",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Attorney-General may, by instrument in writing, revoke an\norder made under subsection 20BL(1) (in this section called a\nrelease order) at any time while that release order remains in force:\n\n(a) if the person concerned has, during that period, failed,\nwithout reasonable excuse, to comply with a condition of the\norder; or\n\n(b) if there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that the person\nhas, during that period, failed, without reasonable excuse, so\nto comply;",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bm-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bm-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
