        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bm-logic-deontic-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3c127fbaccfc3819c907b0e0c4ab09bb739b447dbab0373e7ae3da1a7f6f5ad0",
      "skos:note": "Revocation of release order"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-20bm",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20BM Release order may be revoked",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 315,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Attorney-General may, by instrument in writing, revoke an\norder made under subsection 20BL(1) (in this section called a\nrelease order) at any time while that release order remains in force:\n\n(a) if the person concerned has, during that period, failed,\nwithout reasonable excuse, to comply with a condition of the\norder; or\n\n(b) if there are reasonable grounds for suspecting that the person\nhas, during that period, failed, without reasonable excuse, so\nto comply;"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bm-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bm"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bm-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibition",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibition of release order revocation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Release order may be revoked",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Revocation is prohibited"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bm-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Permission",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Permission to revoke release order under certain conditions",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The Attorney-General may revoke the release order",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Revocation of release order is permitted under certain conditions"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bm-logic-ltl-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LTL"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Until",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Temporal relationship between revocation and release order",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::temporal_ltl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The revocation takes effect while the release order remains in force",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Revocation occurs until the release order is no longer in force"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bm-logic-deontic-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to comply with conditions of release order",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The person concerned must comply with the condition",
      "cml:conclusionText": "There is an obligation to comply with the condition"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bn",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20BN Attorney-General to review detention of persons taken back",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-20bn"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.317",
      "values:originalText": "into detention\n\n(1) Where, under subsection 20BM(5), a prescribed authority directs\nthat a person be detained in prison or in a hospital, the\nAttorney-General must, as soon as practicable after the person is so\ndetained, consider (in this section called the initial consideration)\nwhether or not the person should be released from detention and\nmust, while the person is in detention, reconsider the matter at least\nonce in each period of 6 months after the initial consideration.\n\n(2) Subsection 20BK(2) and, subject to the modification in\nsubsection (3), section 20BL, apply in relation to an initial\nconsideration and a reconsideration under subsection (1).\n\n(3) For the purposes of applying section 20BL, subsection 20BL(1)\nhas effect as if the reference in that subsection to\nsubsection 20BK(1) were a reference to subsection (1) of this\nsection.",
      "skos:definition": "into detention\n\n(1) Where, under subsection 20BM(5), a prescribed authority directs\nthat a person be detained in prison or in a hospital, the\nAttorney-General must, as soon as practicable after the person is so\ndetained, consider (in this section called the initial consideration)\nwhether or not the person should be released from detention and\nmust, while the person is in detention, reconsider the matter at least\nonce in each period of 6 months after the initial consideration.\n\n(2) Subsection 20BK(2) and, subject to the modification in\nsubsection (3), section 20BL, apply in relation to an initial\nconsideration and a reconsideration under subsection (1).\n\n(3) For the purposes of applying section 20BL, subsection 20BL(1)\nhas effect as if the reference in that subsection to\nsubsection 20BK(1) were a reference to subsection (1) of this\nsection.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bn-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bn-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bn-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a658a29dc855dbdb0bd5b4caadf61ab5d69b461969fd7bc195b5f3632543ed44"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-20bn",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20BN Attorney-General to review detention of persons taken back",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 317,
      "values:originalText": "into detention\n\n(1) Where, under subsection 20BM(5), a prescribed authority directs\nthat a person be detained in prison or in a hospital, the\nAttorney-General must, as soon as practicable after the person is so\ndetained, consider (in this section called the initial consideration)\nwhether or not the person should be released from detention and\nmust, while the person is in detention, reconsider the matter at least\nonce in each period of 6 months after the initial consideration.\n\n(2) Subsection 20BK(2) and, subject to the modification in\nsubsection (3), section 20BL, apply in relation to an initial\nconsideration and a reconsideration under subsection (1).\n\n(3) For the purposes of applying section 20BL, subsection 20BL(1)\nhas effect as if the reference in that subsection to\nsubsection 20BK(1) were a reference to subsection (1) of this\nsection."
    },
