    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bt",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20BT Lesser periods of imprisonment fixed under hospital orders",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-20bt"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.322",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where a lesser period of detention is fixed under\nsubsection 20BS(4) in relation to a person detained in hospital\nunder a hospital order, the Attorney-General must, at the end of the\nlesser period, obtain and consider the reports of 2 duly qualified\npsychiatrists with experience in the diagnosis and treatment of\nmental illness so as to determine whether or not to release the\nperson from the detention.\n\n(2) Unless:\n\n\nSentencing, imprisonment and release of federal offenders  Part IB\nSentencing alternatives for persons suffering from mental illness or intellectual\ndisability  Division 9\n\nSection 20BU\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) either of the reports of the psychiatrists recommends that the\nperson not be released because of a continuing need for\nhospital treatment; or\n\n(b) the person continues, at the end of the lesser period of\ndetention, to be required to serve a federal sentence of\nimprisonment that the person was serving at the time when\nthe hospital order began;\nthe Attorney-General must order the person to be released on such\nconditions (including conditions relating to release into the care of\nanother person specified in the order) for the balance of the period\nof the hospital order as the Attorney-General considers appropriate\nhaving regard to the reports and to such other matters as he or she\nconsiders relevant.\n\n(3) Sections 20BM and 20BN apply in relation to a person released\nfrom involuntary hospitalisation by order under subsection (2) as\nif:\n\n(a) the order under that subsection were a release order made\nunder subsection 20BL(1); and\n\n(b) the references in each of those sections to detention in a\nprison or a hospital were references only to detention in a\nhospital; and\n\n(c) the reference in subsection 20BM(5) to the period of\ndetention in safe custody under subsection 20BJ(1) were a\nreference to the period of detention in a hospital specified in\nthe order under subsection 20BS(1).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Where a lesser period of detention is fixed under\nsubsection 20BS(4) in relation to a person detained in hospital\nunder a hospital order, the Attorney-General must, at the end of the\nlesser period, obtain and consider the reports of 2 duly qualified\npsychiatrists with experience in the diagnosis and treatment of\nmental illness so as to determine whether or not to release the\nperson from the detention.\n\n(2) Unless:\n\n\nSentencing, imprisonment and release of federal offenders  Part IB\nSentencing alternatives for persons suffering from mental illness or intellectual\ndisability  Division 9\n\nSection 20BU\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) either of the reports of the psychiatrists recommends that the\nperson not be released because of a continuing need for\nhospital treatment; or\n\n(b) the person continues, at the end of the lesser period of\ndetention, to be required to serve a federal sentence of\nimprisonment that the person was serving at the time when\nthe hospital order began;\nthe Attorney-General must order the person to be released on such\nconditions (including conditions relating to release into the care of\nanother person specified in the order) for the balance of the period\nof the hospital order as the Attorney-General considers appropriate\nhaving regard to the reports and to such other matters as he or she\nconsiders relevant.\n\n(3) Sections 20BM and 20BN apply in relation to a person released\nfrom involuntary hospitalisation by order under subsection (2) as\nif:\n\n(a) the order under that subsection were a release order made\nunder subsection 20BL(1); and\n\n(b) the references in each of those sections to detention in a\nprison or a hospital were references only to detention in a\nhospital; and\n\n(c) the reference in subsection 20BM(5) to the period of\ndetention in safe custody under subsection 20BJ(1) were a\nreference to the period of detention in a hospital specified in\nthe order under subsection 20BS(1).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bt-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bt-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bt-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8408a7eb4acbafb6979040e65f39cd57a5c78deb3c908e1e64419edc309c032d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-20bt",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20BT Lesser periods of imprisonment fixed under hospital orders",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 322,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where a lesser period of detention is fixed under\nsubsection 20BS(4) in relation to a person detained in hospital\nunder a hospital order, the Attorney-General must, at the end of the\nlesser period, obtain and consider the reports of 2 duly qualified\npsychiatrists with experience in the diagnosis and treatment of\nmental illness so as to determine whether or not to release the\nperson from the detention.\n\n(2) Unless:\n\n\nSentencing, imprisonment and release of federal offenders  Part IB\nSentencing alternatives for persons suffering from mental illness or intellectual\ndisability  Division 9\n\nSection 20BU\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) either of the reports of the psychiatrists recommends that the\nperson not be released because of a continuing need for\nhospital treatment; or\n\n(b) the person continues, at the end of the lesser period of\ndetention, to be required to serve a federal sentence of\nimprisonment that the person was serving at the time when\nthe hospital order began;\nthe Attorney-General must order the person to be released on such\nconditions (including conditions relating to release into the care of\nanother person specified in the order) for the balance of the period\nof the hospital order as the Attorney-General considers appropriate\nhaving regard to the reports and to such other matters as he or she\nconsiders relevant.\n\n(3) Sections 20BM and 20BN apply in relation to a person released\nfrom involuntary hospitalisation by order under subsection (2) as\nif:\n\n(a) the order under that subsection were a release order made\nunder subsection 20BL(1); and\n\n(b) the references in each of those sections to detention in a\nprison or a hospital were references only to detention in a\nhospital; and\n\n(c) the reference in subsection 20BM(5) to the period of\ndetention in safe custody under subsection 20BJ(1) were a\nreference to the period of detention in a hospital specified in\nthe order under subsection 20BS(1)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bt-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20BT(1) Lesser periods of imprisonment fixed under hospital orders",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-20bt-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.322",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where a lesser period of detention is fixed under\nsubsection 20BS(4) in relation to a person detained in hospital\nunder a hospital order, the Attorney-General must, at the end of the\nlesser period, obtain and consider the reports of 2 duly qualified\npsychiatrists with experience in the diagnosis and treatment of\nmental illness so as to determine whether or not to release the\nperson from the detention.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Where a lesser period of detention is fixed under\nsubsection 20BS(4) in relation to a person detained in hospital\nunder a hospital order, the Attorney-General must, at the end of the\nlesser period, obtain and consider the reports of 2 duly qualified\npsychiatrists with experience in the diagnosis and treatment of\nmental illness so as to determine whether or not to release the\nperson from the detention.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bt"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bt-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bt-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "243ae7127fdd5a4fe7dbe84454197817c96dab461bc367b6a175cd6e3a6eed76",
      "skos:note": "Attorney-General must obtain and consider reports of psychiatrists to determine release from detention."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-20bt-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20BT(1) Lesser periods of imprisonment fixed under hospital orders",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 322,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where a lesser period of detention is fixed under\nsubsection 20BS(4) in relation to a person detained in hospital\nunder a hospital order, the Attorney-General must, at the end of the\nlesser period, obtain and consider the reports of 2 duly qualified\npsychiatrists with experience in the diagnosis and treatment of\nmental illness so as to determine whether or not to release the\nperson from the detention."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bt-ss-1-norm",
