    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bt-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20BT(2) Lesser periods of imprisonment fixed under hospital orders",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-20bt-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.322",
      "values:originalText": "(2) Unless:\n\n\nSentencing, imprisonment and release of federal offenders  Part IB\nSentencing alternatives for persons suffering from mental illness or intellectual\ndisability  Division 9\n\nSection 20BU\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) either of the reports of the psychiatrists recommends that the\nperson not be released because of a continuing need for\nhospital treatment; or\n\n(b) the person continues, at the end of the lesser period of\ndetention, to be required to serve a federal sentence of\nimprisonment that the person was serving at the time when\nthe hospital order began;\nthe Attorney-General must order the person to be released on such\nconditions (including conditions relating to release into the care of\nanother person specified in the order) for the balance of the period\nof the hospital order as the Attorney-General considers appropriate\nhaving regard to the reports and to such other matters as he or she\nconsiders relevant.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) Unless:\n\n\nSentencing, imprisonment and release of federal offenders  Part IB\nSentencing alternatives for persons suffering from mental illness or intellectual\ndisability  Division 9\n\nSection 20BU\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) either of the reports of the psychiatrists recommends that the\nperson not be released because of a continuing need for\nhospital treatment; or\n\n(b) the person continues, at the end of the lesser period of\ndetention, to be required to serve a federal sentence of\nimprisonment that the person was serving at the time when\nthe hospital order began;\nthe Attorney-General must order the person to be released on such\nconditions (including conditions relating to release into the care of\nanother person specified in the order) for the balance of the period\nof the hospital order as the Attorney-General considers appropriate\nhaving regard to the reports and to such other matters as he or she\nconsiders relevant.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bt"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bt-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bt-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "eef7d6583015150613e81ebd07d07feb4ee2c15b1b4ee4e022d8751becaadaa3",
      "skos:note": "The Attorney-General must order release on conditions if reports recommend continued hospital treatment or a federal sentence remains."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-20bt-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20BT(2) Lesser periods of imprisonment fixed under hospital orders",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 322,
      "values:originalText": "(2) Unless:\n\n\nSentencing, imprisonment and release of federal offenders  Part IB\nSentencing alternatives for persons suffering from mental illness or intellectual\ndisability  Division 9\n\nSection 20BU\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) either of the reports of the psychiatrists recommends that the\nperson not be released because of a continuing need for\nhospital treatment; or\n\n(b) the person continues, at the end of the lesser period of\ndetention, to be required to serve a federal sentence of\nimprisonment that the person was serving at the time when\nthe hospital order began;\nthe Attorney-General must order the person to be released on such\nconditions (including conditions relating to release into the care of\nanother person specified in the order) for the balance of the period\nof the hospital order as the Attorney-General considers appropriate\nhaving regard to the reports and to such other matters as he or she\nconsiders relevant."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bt-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
