      "cml:conclusionText": "Sections 20BM and 20BN apply to the person."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bu",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20BU Discharge of hospital orders",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-20bu"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.323",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Where a person is subject to a hospital order, the person or the\nDirector of Public Prosecutions may, at any time while the order is\nin force, apply to the court that imposed the order to discharge the\norder and to impose such other sentence as the court thinks\nappropriate, being a sentence that could have been imposed when\nthe order was made.\n\n(2) The court must not discharge a hospital order unless the court is\nsatisfied:",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Where a person is subject to a hospital order, the person or the\nDirector of Public Prosecutions may, at any time while the order is\nin force, apply to the court that imposed the order to discharge the\norder and to impose such other sentence as the court thinks\nappropriate, being a sentence that could have been imposed when\nthe order was made.\n\n(2) The court must not discharge a hospital order unless the court is\nsatisfied:",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bu-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-20bu-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "48a086b3f9d1eb2690a5363bb7c1421f06f10cd9026d9e2e866f9872850ac1b5"
    },
