      "skos:definition": "(1) Where a person who is subject to an order under section 20BV\nappears before the court by which the order was made and the\ncourt is satisfied that the person has, without reasonable excuse,\nfailed to comply with a condition of the order, the court may:\n\n(a) without prejudice to the continuance of the order, impose a\npecuniary penalty not exceeding 10 penalty units on the\nperson; or\n\n(b) discharge the order and make an order under section 20; or\n\n(c) revoke the order and, subject to subsection (2), deal with the\nperson for the offence in respect of which the order was\nmade, in any way in which the person could have been dealt\nwith for that offence if the order had not been made and the\nperson was before the court for sentence in respect of the\noffence; or\n\n(d) take no action.",
