      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.335",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), the Governor-General may arrange with\nthe Governor of a State, the Australian Capital Territory Executive\nor the Administrator of the Northern Territory:\n\n(a) for the performance by persons who hold office as\nMagistrates in that State or Territory of the functions of a\nprescribed authority under this Part; and\n\n(b) for the performance by officers of that State or Territory of\nthe functions of a parole officer under this Part.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not authorise an arrangement of the kind\nreferred to in paragraph (1)(a) to be entered into between the",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), the Governor-General may arrange with\nthe Governor of a State, the Australian Capital Territory Executive\nor the Administrator of the Northern Territory:\n\n(a) for the performance by persons who hold office as\nMagistrates in that State or Territory of the functions of a\nprescribed authority under this Part; and\n\n(b) for the performance by officers of that State or Territory of\nthe functions of a parole officer under this Part.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not authorise an arrangement of the kind\nreferred to in paragraph (1)(a) to be entered into between the",
      "cml:hasPart": [
