    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-22-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "22(5) Conditions etc. that a court may impose on certain offenders",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-22-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.336",
      "values:originalText": "(5) If the court makes an order under paragraph (1)(e):\n\n(a) the Australian travel document must be given to the Registrar\nor other appropriate officer of the court; and\n\n(b) the Registrar or officer must cause the Australian travel\ndocument to be kept in such custody as he or she thinks fit\nuntil:\n\n(i) the Australian travel document is required to be released\nunder subsection (6); or\n\n(ii) the Australian travel document is cancelled or expires;\n\nwhichever happens first.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) If the court makes an order under paragraph (1)(e):\n\n(a) the Australian travel document must be given to the Registrar\nor other appropriate officer of the court; and\n\n(b) the Registrar or officer must cause the Australian travel\ndocument to be kept in such custody as he or she thinks fit\nuntil:\n\n(i) the Australian travel document is required to be released\nunder subsection (6); or\n\n(ii) the Australian travel document is cancelled or expires;\n\nwhichever happens first.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-22"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-22-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-22-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "48f47fe0644a6691e2f577f006c1abb2c72cf78ba4d68e668ba02bd0fa7cba8e",
      "skos:note": "Australian travel document must be given to the Registrar or other appropriate officer of the court.",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-22-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "22(5) Conditions etc. that a court may impose on certain offenders",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 336,
      "values:originalText": "(5) If the court makes an order under paragraph (1)(e):\n\n(a) the Australian travel document must be given to the Registrar\nor other appropriate officer of the court; and\n\n(b) the Registrar or officer must cause the Australian travel\ndocument to be kept in such custody as he or she thinks fit\nuntil:\n\n(i) the Australian travel document is required to be released\nunder subsection (6); or\n\n(ii) the Australian travel document is cancelled or expires;\n\nwhichever happens first."
    },
