    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-22-ss-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "22(6) Conditions etc. that a court may impose on certain offenders",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-22-ss-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.336",
      "values:originalText": "(6) If an Australian travel document surrendered under an order under\nparagraph (1)(e) is in force when that order ceases to have effect,\nthe person having the custody of the Australian travel document at\nthat time must, on the application of the person to whom it was\nissued, cause it to be returned to that person.",
      "skos:definition": "(6) If an Australian travel document surrendered under an order under\nparagraph (1)(e) is in force when that order ceases to have effect,\nthe person having the custody of the Australian travel document at\nthat time must, on the application of the person to whom it was\nissued, cause it to be returned to that person.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-22"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-22-ss-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-22-ss-6-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "823dfd5d24ac561ee7e74900f577eec66a745ec7b27799361196bd6016df17d8",
      "skos:note": "Return of Australian travel document upon request"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-22-ss-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "22(6) Conditions etc. that a court may impose on certain offenders",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 336,
      "values:originalText": "(6) If an Australian travel document surrendered under an order under\nparagraph (1)(e) is in force when that order ceases to have effect,\nthe person having the custody of the Australian travel document at\nthat time must, on the application of the person to whom it was\nissued, cause it to be returned to that person."
    },
