    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23c-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23C(4) Period of investigation if arrested for a non-terrorism offence",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23c-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.346",
      "values:originalText": "(4) For the purposes of this section, but subject to subsections (6) and\n(7), the investigation period begins when the person is arrested, and\nends at a time thereafter that is reasonable, having regard to all the\ncircumstances, but does not extend beyond:\n\n(a) if the person is or appears to be under 18, an Aboriginal\nperson or a Torres Strait Islander—2 hours; or\n\n\nInvestigation of Commonwealth offences  Part IC\nPowers of detention  Division 2\n\nSection 23C\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) in any other case—4 hours;\nafter the arrest, unless the period is extended under section 23DA.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) For the purposes of this section, but subject to subsections (6) and\n(7), the investigation period begins when the person is arrested, and\nends at a time thereafter that is reasonable, having regard to all the\ncircumstances, but does not extend beyond:\n\n(a) if the person is or appears to be under 18, an Aboriginal\nperson or a Torres Strait Islander—2 hours; or\n\n\nInvestigation of Commonwealth offences  Part IC\nPowers of detention  Division 2\n\nSection 23C\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) in any other case—4 hours;\nafter the arrest, unless the period is extended under section 23DA.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23c"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23c-ss-4-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "72f4d9babc875ea458d688d3b14937cb7a2fd6d62d8e938ef65c075f973d1aca",
      "skos:note": "Investigation period begins when arrested and ends at a reasonable time, not exceeding 2 hours for minors or 4 hours in other cases."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23c-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23C(4) Period of investigation if arrested for a non-terrorism offence",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 346,
      "values:originalText": "(4) For the purposes of this section, but subject to subsections (6) and\n(7), the investigation period begins when the person is arrested, and\nends at a time thereafter that is reasonable, having regard to all the\ncircumstances, but does not extend beyond:\n\n(a) if the person is or appears to be under 18, an Aboriginal\nperson or a Torres Strait Islander—2 hours; or\n\n\nInvestigation of Commonwealth offences  Part IC\nPowers of detention  Division 2\n\nSection 23C\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(b) in any other case—4 hours;\nafter the arrest, unless the period is extended under section 23DA."
    },
