      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(4) If the person is not released within the investigation period...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The person must be brought before a bail authority or as soon as practicable after."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23db-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23DB(5) Period of investigation if arrested for a terrorism offence",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23db-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.352",
      "values:originalText": "(5) For the purposes of this section, but subject to subsections (7) and\n(9), the investigation period begins when the person is arrested, and\nends at a later time that is reasonable, having regard to all the\ncircumstances, but does not extend beyond:\n\n(a) if the person is or appears to be under 18, an Aboriginal\nperson or a Torres Strait Islander—2 hours; or\n\n(b) in any other case—4 hours;\nafter the arrest, unless the period is extended under section 23DF.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) For the purposes of this section, but subject to subsections (7) and\n(9), the investigation period begins when the person is arrested, and\nends at a later time that is reasonable, having regard to all the\ncircumstances, but does not extend beyond:\n\n(a) if the person is or appears to be under 18, an Aboriginal\nperson or a Torres Strait Islander—2 hours; or\n\n(b) in any other case—4 hours;\nafter the arrest, unless the period is extended under section 23DF.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23db"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23db-ss-5-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "90efba6ebc7bad29ef151cf01db62d8683b0278fcdebc976e0c29e5bd441a408",
      "skos:note": "Investigation period duration after arrest for terrorism offence"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23db-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23DB(5) Period of investigation if arrested for a terrorism offence",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 352,
      "values:originalText": "(5) For the purposes of this section, but subject to subsections (7) and\n(9), the investigation period begins when the person is arrested, and\nends at a later time that is reasonable, having regard to all the\ncircumstances, but does not extend beyond:\n\n(a) if the person is or appears to be under 18, an Aboriginal\nperson or a Torres Strait Islander—2 hours; or\n\n(b) in any other case—4 hours;\nafter the arrest, unless the period is extended under section 23DF."
    },
    {
