    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23dc-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23DC(5) Time during which suspension or delay of questioning may be",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23dc-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.356",
      "values:originalText": "(5) Subsection (4) does not require any information to be included in\nthe application if disclosure of that information is likely:\n\n(a) to prejudice national security (within the meaning of the\nNational Security Information (Criminal and Civil\nProceedings) Act 2004); or\n\n(b) to be protected by public interest immunity; or\n\n(c) to put at risk ongoing operations by law enforcement\nagencies or intelligence agencies; or\n\n(d) to put at risk the safety of the community, law enforcement\nofficers or intelligence officers.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) Subsection (4) does not require any information to be included in\nthe application if disclosure of that information is likely:\n\n(a) to prejudice national security (within the meaning of the\nNational Security Information (Criminal and Civil\nProceedings) Act 2004); or\n\n(b) to be protected by public interest immunity; or\n\n(c) to put at risk ongoing operations by law enforcement\nagencies or intelligence agencies; or\n\n(d) to put at risk the safety of the community, law enforcement\nofficers or intelligence officers.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23dc"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23dc-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23dc-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d4e2738ae654babbea9e0deb70c503f64c539f88e9b391f17f0bb8637fb6cf7a",
      "skos:note": "No information must be included in the application if disclosure is likely to cause harm."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23dc-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23DC(5) Time during which suspension or delay of questioning may be",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 356,
      "values:originalText": "(5) Subsection (4) does not require any information to be included in\nthe application if disclosure of that information is likely:\n\n(a) to prejudice national security (within the meaning of the\nNational Security Information (Criminal and Civil\nProceedings) Act 2004); or\n\n(b) to be protected by public interest immunity; or\n\n(c) to put at risk ongoing operations by law enforcement\nagencies or intelligence agencies; or\n\n(d) to put at risk the safety of the community, law enforcement\nofficers or intelligence officers."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23dc-ss-5-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
