      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23dd-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23DD(5) Time during which suspension or delay of questioning may be",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23dd-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.358",
      "values:originalText": "(5) The magistrate must:\n\n(a) give the investigating official a copy of the instrument as\nsoon as practicable after signing it; and\n\n(b) if the instrument was made as a result of an application made\nby telex, fax or other electronic means—inform the\ninvestigating official of the matters included in the\ninstrument.\nNote:\nSee section 23E.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) The magistrate must:\n\n(a) give the investigating official a copy of the instrument as\nsoon as practicable after signing it; and\n\n(b) if the instrument was made as a result of an application made\nby telex, fax or other electronic means—inform the\ninvestigating official of the matters included in the\ninstrument.\nNote:\nSee section 23E.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23dd"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23dd-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23dd-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23dd-ss-5-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e9cff375f1ce5cc7716498c90bd540b0375eafe25d0c8005a9ccd765e3016f19",
      "skos:note": "Magistrate must provide information to investigating official",
      "dc:description": "instrument, matters included in instrument",
      "dc:references": [
        "sec-23E"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23dd-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23DD(5) Time during which suspension or delay of questioning may be",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 358,
      "values:originalText": "(5) The magistrate must:\n\n(a) give the investigating official a copy of the instrument as\nsoon as practicable after signing it; and\n\n(b) if the instrument was made as a result of an application made\nby telex, fax or other electronic means—inform the\ninvestigating official of the matters included in the\ninstrument.\nNote:\nSee section 23E."
    },
