    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23e",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23E Evidentiary provisions if application made by electronic means",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23e"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.363",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if a magistrate has, under\nparagraph 23DA(5)(b), 23DD(5)(b) or 23DF(5)(b), informed an\ninvestigating official of matters included in an instrument.\n\n(2) As soon as practicable after being informed of those matters, the\ninvestigating official must:\n\n(a) complete a form of the instrument and write on it the name of\nthe magistrate and the particulars given by him or her; and\n\n(b) forward it to the magistrate.\n\n(3) If the form of the instrument completed by the investigating\nofficial does not, in all material respects, accord with the terms of\nthe instrument signed by the magistrate, the instrument is taken to\nhave had no effect.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies if a magistrate has, under\nparagraph 23DA(5)(b), 23DD(5)(b) or 23DF(5)(b), informed an\ninvestigating official of matters included in an instrument.\n\n(2) As soon as practicable after being informed of those matters, the\ninvestigating official must:\n\n(a) complete a form of the instrument and write on it the name of\nthe magistrate and the particulars given by him or her; and\n\n(b) forward it to the magistrate.\n\n(3) If the form of the instrument completed by the investigating\nofficial does not, in all material respects, accord with the terms of\nthe instrument signed by the magistrate, the instrument is taken to\nhave had no effect.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23e-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23e-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23e-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3b8abbb7794c1a629cfbe5eb9a0f888a4fd9430d808671351955b0622591f83b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23e",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23E Evidentiary provisions if application made by electronic means",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 363,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if a magistrate has, under\nparagraph 23DA(5)(b), 23DD(5)(b) or 23DF(5)(b), informed an\ninvestigating official of matters included in an instrument.\n\n(2) As soon as practicable after being informed of those matters, the\ninvestigating official must:\n\n(a) complete a form of the instrument and write on it the name of\nthe magistrate and the particulars given by him or her; and\n\n(b) forward it to the magistrate.\n\n(3) If the form of the instrument completed by the investigating\nofficial does not, in all material respects, accord with the terms of\nthe instrument signed by the magistrate, the instrument is taken to\nhave had no effect."
    },
