      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.363",
      "values:originalText": "(2) As soon as practicable after being informed of those matters, the\ninvestigating official must:\n\n(a) complete a form of the instrument and write on it the name of\nthe magistrate and the particulars given by him or her; and\n\n(b) forward it to the magistrate.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) As soon as practicable after being informed of those matters, the\ninvestigating official must:\n\n(a) complete a form of the instrument and write on it the name of\nthe magistrate and the particulars given by him or her; and\n\n(b) forward it to the magistrate.",
