    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23f",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23F Cautioning persons who are under arrest or protected suspects",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23f"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.365",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsection (3), if a person is under arrest or a protected\nsuspect, an investigating official must, before starting to question\nthe person, caution the person that he or she does not have to say or\ndo anything, but that anything the person does say or do may be\nused in evidence.\n\n(2) The investigating official must inform the person of the caution in\naccordance with subsection (1), but need only do so in writing if\nthat is the most appropriate means of informing the person.\n\n(3) Subsections (1) and (2) do not apply so far as another law of the\nCommonwealth requires the person to answer questions put by, or\ndo things required by, the investigating official.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Subject to subsection (3), if a person is under arrest or a protected\nsuspect, an investigating official must, before starting to question\nthe person, caution the person that he or she does not have to say or\ndo anything, but that anything the person does say or do may be\nused in evidence.\n\n(2) The investigating official must inform the person of the caution in\naccordance with subsection (1), but need only do so in writing if\nthat is the most appropriate means of informing the person.\n\n(3) Subsections (1) and (2) do not apply so far as another law of the\nCommonwealth requires the person to answer questions put by, or\ndo things required by, the investigating official.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23f-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23f-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23f-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "eec88c8292d1938a2642a1c61cc98e6ee5fda8a113f0d4b466c2cb7c974a5717"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23f",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23F Cautioning persons who are under arrest or protected suspects",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 365,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsection (3), if a person is under arrest or a protected\nsuspect, an investigating official must, before starting to question\nthe person, caution the person that he or she does not have to say or\ndo anything, but that anything the person does say or do may be\nused in evidence.\n\n(2) The investigating official must inform the person of the caution in\naccordance with subsection (1), but need only do so in writing if\nthat is the most appropriate means of informing the person.\n\n(3) Subsections (1) and (2) do not apply so far as another law of the\nCommonwealth requires the person to answer questions put by, or\ndo things required by, the investigating official."
    },
