    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23g",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23G Right to communicate with friend, relative and legal",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23g"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.365",
      "values:originalText": "practitioner\n\n(1) Subject to section 23L, if a person is under arrest or a protected\nsuspect, an investigating official must, before starting to question\nthe person, inform the person that he or she may:\n\n(a) communicate, or attempt to communicate, with a friend or\nrelative to inform that person of his or her whereabouts; and\n\n(b) communicate, or attempt to communicate, with a legal\npractitioner of the person’s choice and arrange, or attempt to\narrange, for a legal practitioner of the person’s choice to be\npresent during the questioning;\nand the investigating official must defer the questioning for a\nreasonable time to allow the person to make, or attempt to make,\nthe communication and, if the person has arranged for a legal\npractitioner to be present, to allow the legal practitioner to attend\nthe questioning.",
      "skos:definition": "practitioner\n\n(1) Subject to section 23L, if a person is under arrest or a protected\nsuspect, an investigating official must, before starting to question\nthe person, inform the person that he or she may:\n\n(a) communicate, or attempt to communicate, with a friend or\nrelative to inform that person of his or her whereabouts; and\n\n(b) communicate, or attempt to communicate, with a legal\npractitioner of the person’s choice and arrange, or attempt to\narrange, for a legal practitioner of the person’s choice to be\npresent during the questioning;\nand the investigating official must defer the questioning for a\nreasonable time to allow the person to make, or attempt to make,\nthe communication and, if the person has arranged for a legal\npractitioner to be present, to allow the legal practitioner to attend\nthe questioning.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23g-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23g-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23g-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23g-logic-deontic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23g-logic-deontic-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23g-logic-deontic-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23g-logic-deontic-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "510ec06db4bf0be5fecf59387a4a89ddb2ba3e67867ffe0541d69c285f3643b3",
      "skos:note": "Right to communicate with friend, relative and legal practitioner during questioning."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23g",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23G Right to communicate with friend, relative and legal",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 365,
      "values:originalText": "practitioner\n\n(1) Subject to section 23L, if a person is under arrest or a protected\nsuspect, an investigating official must, before starting to question\nthe person, inform the person that he or she may:\n\n(a) communicate, or attempt to communicate, with a friend or\nrelative to inform that person of his or her whereabouts; and\n\n(b) communicate, or attempt to communicate, with a legal\npractitioner of the person’s choice and arrange, or attempt to\narrange, for a legal practitioner of the person’s choice to be\npresent during the questioning;\nand the investigating official must defer the questioning for a\nreasonable time to allow the person to make, or attempt to make,\nthe communication and, if the person has arranged for a legal\npractitioner to be present, to allow the legal practitioner to attend\nthe questioning."
    },
