    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23h-ss-1a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23H(1A) Aboriginal persons and Torres Strait Islanders",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23h-ss-1a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.366",
      "values:originalText": "(1A) To avoid doubt, the obligations imposed by subsection (1) do not\nlimit and are not limited by any other obligations imposed, or\nrights conferred, by this section.\n\n(1AB) If a representative of an Aboriginal legal assistance organisation is\nnotified under subsection (1), the investigating official must not\nquestion the person until the earlier of the following times:\n\n(a) the representative has communicated with the person;\n\n(b) 2 hours have elapsed since the representative was notified.",
      "skos:definition": "(1A) To avoid doubt, the obligations imposed by subsection (1) do not\nlimit and are not limited by any other obligations imposed, or\nrights conferred, by this section.\n\n(1AB) If a representative of an Aboriginal legal assistance organisation is\nnotified under subsection (1), the investigating official must not\nquestion the person until the earlier of the following times:\n\n(a) the representative has communicated with the person;\n\n(b) 2 hours have elapsed since the representative was notified.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23h"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23h-ss-1a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23h-ss-1a-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23h-ss-1a-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23h-ss-1a-logic-ltl-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0ace585f0e59d70fe1f3e7d51d52d07a98c2bfcad0f6e56c45472189677bd0d7",
      "skos:note": "Official must not question Aboriginal person until notified representative has communicated or 2 hours have passed."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23h-ss-1a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23H(1A) Aboriginal persons and Torres Strait Islanders",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 366,
      "values:originalText": "(1A) To avoid doubt, the obligations imposed by subsection (1) do not\nlimit and are not limited by any other obligations imposed, or\nrights conferred, by this section.\n\n(1AB) If a representative of an Aboriginal legal assistance organisation is\nnotified under subsection (1), the investigating official must not\nquestion the person until the earlier of the following times:\n\n(a) the representative has communicated with the person;\n\n(b) 2 hours have elapsed since the representative was notified."
    },
