    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23h-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23H(2) Aboriginal persons and Torres Strait Islanders",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23h-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.366",
      "values:originalText": "(2) Subject to subsection (7) and section 23L, if an investigating\nofficial:\n\n(a) interviews a person as a suspect (whether under arrest or not)\nfor a Commonwealth offence, and believes on reasonable\ngrounds that the person is an Aboriginal person or a Torres\nStrait Islander; or\n\n(b) believes on reasonable grounds that a person who is under\narrest or a protected suspect is an Aboriginal person or a\nTorres Strait Islander;\nthe official must not question the person unless:\n\n(c) an interview friend is present while the person is being\nquestioned and, before the start of the questioning, the\nofficial has allowed the person to communicate with the\ninterview friend in circumstances in which, as far as\npracticable, the communication will not be overheard; or\n\n(d) the person has expressly and voluntarily waived his or her\nright to have such a person present.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) Subject to subsection (7) and section 23L, if an investigating\nofficial:\n\n(a) interviews a person as a suspect (whether under arrest or not)\nfor a Commonwealth offence, and believes on reasonable\ngrounds that the person is an Aboriginal person or a Torres\nStrait Islander; or\n\n(b) believes on reasonable grounds that a person who is under\narrest or a protected suspect is an Aboriginal person or a\nTorres Strait Islander;\nthe official must not question the person unless:\n\n(c) an interview friend is present while the person is being\nquestioned and, before the start of the questioning, the\nofficial has allowed the person to communicate with the\ninterview friend in circumstances in which, as far as\npracticable, the communication will not be overheard; or\n\n(d) the person has expressly and voluntarily waived his or her\nright to have such a person present.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23h"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23h-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23h-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23h-ss-2-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23h-ss-2-logic-argumentation-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23h-ss-2-logic-deontic-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6b23fec4491d6926a17e5998f531bc212c17cc02884783cd709c94a11a6c2777",
      "skos:note": "Official must not question Aboriginal person or Torres Strait Islander without interview friend present."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23h-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23H(2) Aboriginal persons and Torres Strait Islanders",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 366,
      "values:originalText": "(2) Subject to subsection (7) and section 23L, if an investigating\nofficial:\n\n(a) interviews a person as a suspect (whether under arrest or not)\nfor a Commonwealth offence, and believes on reasonable\ngrounds that the person is an Aboriginal person or a Torres\nStrait Islander; or\n\n(b) believes on reasonable grounds that a person who is under\narrest or a protected suspect is an Aboriginal person or a\nTorres Strait Islander;\nthe official must not question the person unless:\n\n(c) an interview friend is present while the person is being\nquestioned and, before the start of the questioning, the\nofficial has allowed the person to communicate with the\ninterview friend in circumstances in which, as far as\npracticable, the communication will not be overheard; or\n\n(d) the person has expressly and voluntarily waived his or her\nright to have such a person present."
    },
