    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23h-ss-2a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23H(2A) Aboriginal persons and Torres Strait Islanders",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23h-ss-2a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.366",
      "values:originalText": "(2A) The person suspected, or under arrest, may choose his or her own\ninterview friend unless:\n\n(a) he or she expressly and voluntarily waives this right; or\n\n(b) he or she fails to exercise this right within a reasonable\nperiod; or\n\n(c) the interview friend chosen does not arrive within 2 hours of\nthe person’s first opportunity to contact an interview friend.",
      "skos:definition": "(2A) The person suspected, or under arrest, may choose his or her own\ninterview friend unless:\n\n(a) he or she expressly and voluntarily waives this right; or\n\n(b) he or she fails to exercise this right within a reasonable\nperiod; or\n\n(c) the interview friend chosen does not arrive within 2 hours of\nthe person’s first opportunity to contact an interview friend.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23h"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23h-ss-2a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23h-ss-2a-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23h-ss-2a-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23h-ss-2a-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23h-ss-2a-logic-deontic-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23h-ss-2a-logic-deontic-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "37f961e4b5bd479add3d3431df3a2be064d0f428c268560051bb8a826f539c36",
      "skos:note": "Right to choose an interview friend under certain conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23h-ss-2a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23H(2A) Aboriginal persons and Torres Strait Islanders",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 366,
      "values:originalText": "(2A) The person suspected, or under arrest, may choose his or her own\ninterview friend unless:\n\n(a) he or she expressly and voluntarily waives this right; or\n\n(b) he or she fails to exercise this right within a reasonable\nperiod; or\n\n(c) the interview friend chosen does not arrive within 2 hours of\nthe person’s first opportunity to contact an interview friend."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23h-ss-2a-norm",
