    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23m",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23M Providing information relating to persons who are under arrest",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23m"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.371",
      "values:originalText": "or protected suspects\n\n(1) An investigating official must inform a person (the first person)\nwho is under arrest or a protected suspect of any request for\ninformation as to his or her whereabouts by any of his or her\nrelatives, friends or legal representatives.\n\n(2) The investigating official must then provide that information to the\nother person unless:\n\n(a) the first person does not agree to the provision of that\ninformation; or\n\n(b) the investigating official believes on reasonable grounds that\nthe other person is not the first person’s relative, friend or\nlegal representative.\n\n(3) This section has effect subject to section 23L.",
      "skos:definition": "or protected suspects\n\n(1) An investigating official must inform a person (the first person)\nwho is under arrest or a protected suspect of any request for\ninformation as to his or her whereabouts by any of his or her\nrelatives, friends or legal representatives.\n\n(2) The investigating official must then provide that information to the\nother person unless:\n\n(a) the first person does not agree to the provision of that\ninformation; or\n\n(b) the investigating official believes on reasonable grounds that\nthe other person is not the first person’s relative, friend or\nlegal representative.\n\n(3) This section has effect subject to section 23L.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23m-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23m-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23m-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "da11586d88f16d9ce19f10f37ff4f3db1e289baf632623e389e4b076d16ac2d8"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23m",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23M Providing information relating to persons who are under arrest",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 371,
      "values:originalText": "or protected suspects\n\n(1) An investigating official must inform a person (the first person)\nwho is under arrest or a protected suspect of any request for\ninformation as to his or her whereabouts by any of his or her\nrelatives, friends or legal representatives.\n\n(2) The investigating official must then provide that information to the\nother person unless:\n\n(a) the first person does not agree to the provision of that\ninformation; or\n\n(b) the investigating official believes on reasonable grounds that\nthe other person is not the first person’s relative, friend or\nlegal representative.\n\n(3) This section has effect subject to section 23L."
    },
