    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23p-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23P(2) Right of non-Australian nationals to communicate with",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23p-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-act-1914.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.372",
      "values:originalText": "(2) Without limiting subsection (1), an investigating official must not\nstart to question the person unless paragraphs (1)(c), (d) and (f)\nhave been complied with.\n\n\nInvestigation of Commonwealth offences  Part IC\nObligations of investigating officials  Division 3\n\nSection 23Q\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(2) Without limiting subsection (1), an investigating official must not\nstart to question the person unless paragraphs (1)(c), (d) and (f)\nhave been complied with.\n\n\nInvestigation of Commonwealth offences  Part IC\nObligations of investigating officials  Division 3\n\nSection 23Q\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23p"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23p-ss-2-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5d7a45ce77f3d8c193363351f41403c5dc40f9ede4ee9b7625a9cafe9bc536e0",
      "skos:note": "Must comply with paragraphs (1)(c), (d) and (f) before questioning a person."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-act-1914#sec-23p-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "23P(2) Right of non-Australian nationals to communicate with",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 372,
      "values:originalText": "(2) Without limiting subsection (1), an investigating official must not\nstart to question the person unless paragraphs (1)(c), (d) and (f)\nhave been complied with.\n\n\nInvestigation of Commonwealth offences  Part IC\nObligations of investigating officials  Division 3\n\nSection 23Q\n\nCrimes Act 1914\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-23p-ss-2-norm",
